WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

2
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.070
[popping]

3
00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:45.750
[soft rustling]

4
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.576
[KAGAYA] Within the next five days.

5
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.270
Muzan will come.

6
00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.410
I will be the bait you use.

7
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.080
When he comes.
I need you to behead him.

8
00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.540
Master. what leads you
to believe he'll find you?

9
00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.526
[Kagaya chuckles weakly]

10
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:30.260
My intuition. That's all.

11
00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:32.760
Nothing beyond that.

12
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:36.310
But listen. the others can't know.

13
00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:41.536
They would never agree
to using me as bait like this.

14
00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.900
They would sooner die than do it.

15
00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:48.940
You're the only one
that I can ask. Gyomei.

16
00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.846
Even if you behead him.
he won't die.

17
00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.280
♪

18
00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.516
There's likely only one way
to destroy Muzan.

19
00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.120
Trapping him in place
until sunlight shines upon him.

20
00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.726
If beheading isn't enough to kill him.

21
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.800
there's only one option left.

22
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:14.550
You all must endure a battle
until the sun rises.

23
00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:16.850
Yes. sir.

24
00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:21.140
If that is your wish.
then so be it. Master.

25
00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.400
[KAGAYA] Thank goodness.

26
00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.660
Gyomei. after I have perished.

27
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.056
please do not let any more of my children

28
00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.580
be sent to their graves.

29
00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:43.500
That is my wish.

30
00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.786
[♪ tense music playing]

31
00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.076
[MUZAN] You think
you've driven me into a corner

32
00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.480
with your little plan?

33
00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:09.876
But you are all about to be
going straight to hell!

34
00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.046
Mark my words. Demon Slayers.

35
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:15.716
I'll massacre every one of you
before sunrise!

36
00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.006
[grunts angrily]

37
00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.570
[Nakime plucking biwa strings]

38
00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.556
You're the only one going to hell!

39
00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:24.290
And you won't get away!

40
00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.396
Oh. is that so?

41
00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.500
Let's see you try.

42
00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.476
Tanjiro Kamado!

43
00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.146
[rumbling]

44
00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:36.550
I will defeat you!

45
00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.076
Muzan Kibutsuji!

46
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:45.270
DEMON SLAYER: KIMETSU NO YAIBA
THE MOVIE: INFINITY CASTLE

47
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.980
[♪ opening theme song playing]

48
00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.980
What is this place?

49
00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.610
Everything's upside down.

50
00:03:57.820 --> 00:03:58.820
KILL

51
00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.700
Was all of this made using
the enemy's Blood Demon Art?

52
00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.516
I don't understand what's happening.

53
00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.540
except that Ms. Tamayo
was restraining Muzan.

54
00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.026
Even so. how long
can she keep that up?

55
00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:16.566
[screaming]

56
00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.300
[IGURO] Calm down. Kanroji.

57
00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.050
[gasps] Yes!

58
00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:22.050
[IGURO] Stay with me.

59
00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:35.570
[gasps]

60
00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.070
[Gyomei grunts]

61
00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:56.800
[effort grunts]

62
00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.470
[effort grunts]

63
00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:19.586
[TANJIRO] I need to reach Muzan
as soon as possible

64
00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:22.610
and defeat him by whatever means!

65
00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.200
[grunts]

66
00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:31.136
[♪ Gregorian chanting]

67
00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.726
That's the bottom!

68
00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:34.590
I'll be killed at this speed!

69
00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.856
I'll use a move to change directions.

70
00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:39.066
Then find something to grab on to.

71
00:05:39.090 --> 00:05:40.316
DESTROY

72
00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.880
[♪ music intensifies]

73
00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:46.510
It didn't work. I can't
break away from this free fall.

74
00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:50.770
DESTROYER OF DEMONS

75
00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.160
[♪ low tense music playing]

76
00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:21.130
[♪ music fades]

77
00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:30.430
[Tanjiro panting]

78
00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.270
[GIYU] You all right?

79
00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:41.230
Yes. Thanks for your help.

80
00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:42.860
[sighs in relief]

81
00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.610
You really saved...

82
00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.306
Water Breathing. First Form:

83
00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.950
Water Surface Slash.

84
00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:54.250
[GIYU] Tanjiro!

85
00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.880
[♪ intense music playing]

86
00:07:00.590 --> 00:07:02.550
[hinges creaking]

87
00:07:04.550 --> 00:07:05.840
[snarling]

88
00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:17.850
[BOTH] Water Breathing.

89
00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:19.706
[TANJIRO] Sixth Form.

90
00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:21.150
[GIYU] Third Form.

91
00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:24.506
[TANJIRO] Whirlpool!

92
00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:26.110
[GIYU] Flowing Dance.

93
00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:32.990
[Tanjiro groans nervously]

94
00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.830
Mr. Giyu's amazing.

95
00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:39.290
He can tell exactly which move
I'm gonna use.

96
00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:41.016
Then he follows up with one

97
00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.510
that prevents any kind of friendly fire.

98
00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.010
He's unbelievable.

99
00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.116
Just what's behind those eyes?

100
00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.260
[stifled whimpering]

101
00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:53.350
If I'm not mistaken...

102
00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.036
this is the place

103
00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:57.246
that Shinazugawa and Iguro mentioned.

104
00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.310
[♪ Gregorian chanting]

105
00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:01.996
Which means

106
00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:05.126
Kibutsuji's plan
was to gather everyone here.

107
00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:07.740
then kill us all in one fell swoop.

108
00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:13.160
From here on out. we'll need
to be even more vigilant.

109
00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:15.160
Right.

110
00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.726
- Let's go.
- Right!

111
00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:19.766
PITTER PATTER

112
00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:22.000
[♪ dramatic music playing]

113
00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.770
[demons snarling]

114
00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.400
[IGURO] Serpent Breathing. Fifth Form:

115
00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:53.620
Slithering Serpent!

116
00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.936
You demon scum!
Stay away from Kanroji!

117
00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:01.686
[squealing]

118
00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:04.130
Mr. Iguro is so cool!

119
00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.146
- Are you hurt?
- No. not at all!

120
00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.090
- Then. let's go.
- Okay!

121
00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:12.050
[Kanroji squealing]

122
00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.440
[grunts]

123
00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:31.086
Tokito!

124
00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.620
[demons snarling]

125
00:09:38.080 --> 00:09:40.266
[MUICHIRO] There's a whole lot
of demons. huh?

126
00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:41.976
[GYOMEI] It would seem
they've been given

127
00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.896
the strength of the Lower Ranks.

128
00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:47.170
It's clear that they're being
used to try and exhaust us.

129
00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.986
[metallic rattling]

130
00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:52.180
[MUICHIRO] Hmm.

131
00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:54.340
What of the Master?

132
00:09:55.430 --> 00:09:58.310
[GYOMEI] He has departed
from this world.

133
00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:01.350
It was a truly noble end.

134
00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:03.770
Knowing him.

135
00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:07.480
he never would have allowed
himself to be caught unawares.

136
00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.360
Did he sacrifice himself?

137
00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:15.160
[GYOMEI] Indeed. The Master
did not have much time left.

138
00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.420
[MUICHIRO] Master.

139
00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.986
Back when I was mortally wounded
by a demon

140
00:10:33.010 --> 00:10:35.066
and found myself teetering on the edge

141
00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:36.680
between life and death...

142
00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:39.430
he stayed by my side.

143
00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:45.076
He did the same
for every Corps member

144
00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.860
who was on the brink of death.

145
00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:50.530
Like a father.

146
00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:54.530
[GYOMEI] Yes. I know.

147
00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:58.070
[MUICHIRO] Muzan not only
took my brother from me.

148
00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:00.200
but our father as well.

149
00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:02.766
That bastard.

150
00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:04.160
Damn him!

151
00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:06.766
I swear I'll make him suffer.

152
00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:08.880
I'll send him straight to hell!

153
00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:11.630
[GYOMEI] You're not alone.

154
00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.970
Trust me. we all feel the same.

155
00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:26.036
DESTROY

156
00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:28.270
[SHINAZUGAWA] Forgive me. Master.

157
00:11:29.900 --> 00:11:32.070
I couldn't protect you.

158
00:11:35.530 --> 00:11:37.950
[distorted grunting]

159
00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:40.870
[blade rasps]

160
00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.040
[♪ upbeat music playing]

161
00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:50.840
There's no end to you lowlifes. huh?

162
00:11:51.420 --> 00:11:53.646
[demon cackling]

163
00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:56.066
That's just fine by me.

164
00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.050
I'll kill all of you!

165
00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.480
[INOSUKE] Hyah!

166
00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.940
Make way! I'm coming through!

167
00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.206
[chuckles]

168
00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:16.070
Whole lotta falling happening here!

169
00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:21.046
Hyah! Pretty rude to just
drop me in here out of nowhere!

170
00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:23.676
Though I've been itching to see
how my training's paying off.

171
00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:27.766
So with that in mind.
let's test it out on you chubs!

172
00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:29.096
[chuckles]

173
00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.396
Let's go!

174
00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:34.040
[grunting]

175
00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.720
[Genya panting]

176
00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:40.866
Where am I?
The Demon Headquarters?

177
00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:42.390
Where are the others?

178
00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:44.600
Big Brother.

179
00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:47.730
I hope you're safe. too.

180
00:12:52.360 --> 00:12:54.110
[ZENITSU] I just heard a sound.

181
00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:57.150
Could it be that he's somewhere nearby?

182
00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.780
[demons snarling]

183
00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.240
You'll regret this.

184
00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:07.676
I won't forgive you.

185
00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.710
Not in a million years.

186
00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:22.590
♪

187
00:13:34.190 --> 00:13:35.650
[SHINOBU] I smell blood.

188
00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.450
What is this place?

189
00:13:54.210 --> 00:13:56.090
[chomping]

190
00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.510
[DEMON] Hmm?

191
00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.470
Oh. my. You're here.

192
00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:09.157
UPPER TWO

193
00:14:09.181 --> 00:14:11.140
Oh! And you're a girl. too!

194
00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:15.400
What a young and tasty morsel
we have. [chuckles]

195
00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:19.570
I'll have to properly thank
Nakime for this later.

196
00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:24.030
[Shinobu panting]

197
00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:34.040
[whimpers softly]

198
00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:36.816
[KANAE] Shinobu.

199
00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:40.010
You must leave
the Demon Slayer Corps.

200
00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.680
I know that you've trained really hard

201
00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:47.680
and you're fighting to make a difference.

202
00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:51.310
- [sobbing softly]
- But I don't think you'll...

203
00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.036
[sighs softly]

204
00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:54.730
[stifled sobbing]

205
00:14:56.980 --> 00:15:00.780
I want you to live the life
of a happy. normal girl.

206
00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:04.530
To be able to see your own hair turn gray.

207
00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:07.007
DESTROYER OF DEMONS

208
00:15:07.031 --> 00:15:09.636
Really... you've done enough.

209
00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:12.096
[SHINOBU] No! [sobbing]
Can't stop now!

210
00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.266
I will avenge you if
it's the last thing I do!

211
00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:17.726
This demon! I need to know...

212
00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.750
I have to know what it looked like!

213
00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.816
Please. Big Sister.
I'm begging you!

214
00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:24.130
Tell me!

215
00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:28.776
I could never live a normal life
knowing someone did this to you!

216
00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.560
[sobbing] Please!

217
00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:33.140
[sighs weakly]

218
00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:36.616
[KANAE] It was a demon

219
00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:39.560
with a blood-stained pattern on his head.

220
00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:44.416
[DEMON] I must say. it's very
nice to meet you. miss.

221
00:15:44.440 --> 00:15:47.070
You may refer to me as Doma.

222
00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:50.740
Ah. what a wonderful night!

223
00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.370
[SHINOBU] Such a warm smile
and gentle voice.

224
00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:59.130
There's a soft.
benevolent presence to him.

225
00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:03.090
[woman weakly] Please. help me.

226
00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.486
Please help me!

227
00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:06.840
Shh.

228
00:16:07.340 --> 00:16:09.220
Can't you see that we're talking?

229
00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:13.996
Hmm?

230
00:16:14.020 --> 00:16:15.470
[SHINOBU] Are you all right?

231
00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.496
[DOMA] Wow!

232
00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.536
That was fast. Are you a Hashira?

233
00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:22.570
[labored breathing]

234
00:16:23.320 --> 00:16:24.780
[squelching]

235
00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.990
- [gasps]
- [♪ unsettling music playing]

236
00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:31.136
[DOMA] Oh. don't worry about that.

237
00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.096
You can just leave her right there.

238
00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:35.410
I'll make a proper meal of her later.

239
00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:36.910
[exhales]

240
00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.210
And this demon...

241
00:16:40.710 --> 00:16:42.420
the weapon he used.

242
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.630
it was a pair of sharp fans.

243
00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:48.090
[metallic scraping]

244
00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:51.696
As the founder
of the Eternal Paradise Faith.

245
00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.696
it is my sworn duty to see that

246
00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:56.220
all my followers attain happiness.

247
00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.310
I'll be sure to consume her completely.

248
00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:02.626
[SHINOBU] There's no doubt.

249
00:17:02.650 --> 00:17:05.190
This is the demon who killed my sister.

250
00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.586
Attaining happiness?

251
00:17:08.610 --> 00:17:10.240
For who exactly?

252
00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:13.660
This girl was horrified.
crying out for help.

253
00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:16.000
- And that's why I saved her.
- [fans scraping]

254
00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:19.460
Her suffering has come to an end.

255
00:17:19.790 --> 00:17:21.330
No more pain.

256
00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:23.000
No more fear.

257
00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.210
Everyone is afraid of death.

258
00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.220
So I help them by consuming them.

259
00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:34.446
This way. they get to live on
within me for all eternity.

260
00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:37.246
I take in their entire being.

261
00:17:37.270 --> 00:17:39.480
Blood. Desires.

262
00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:41.730
Even the last bit of their sinew

263
00:17:42.230 --> 00:17:45.036
- and help their souls transcend.
- [♪ unsettling music playing]

264
00:17:45.060 --> 00:17:47.690
What you're spouting is sheer nonsense.

265
00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:50.150
And to say it with such glee...

266
00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:52.586
You truly make me sick!

267
00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:54.570
Aw.

268
00:17:55.200 --> 00:17:58.886
I can't believe you'd say that
after we'd only just met.

269
00:17:58.910 --> 00:18:00.596
Oh. I see.

270
00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.896
Oh. you poor thing.

271
00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:05.606
Did something unfortunate happen?

272
00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:07.186
Let's hear it.

273
00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:08.670
Go on. tell me.

274
00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:13.196
"Unfortunate" doesn't begin
to describe it!

275
00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:16.366
You are the one who killed
my big sister. weren't you?

276
00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:19.406
Does the haori I'm wearing
mean nothing to you?!

277
00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:20.680
Huh?

278
00:18:21.100 --> 00:18:23.310
♪

279
00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.860
[blade rasps]

280
00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:32.320
[flesh squelching]

281
00:18:32.860 --> 00:18:34.216
[DOMA] That's right.

282
00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.330
It belonged to the girl
who used Flower Breathing.

283
00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:40.200
Such a sweet. gentle child.

284
00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.766
The sun came up and cut our time short.

285
00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.186
I remember.

286
00:18:45.210 --> 00:18:47.790
It's a shame I didn't get... Her.

287
00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:50.896
[SHINOBU] Insect Breathing.

288
00:18:50.920 --> 00:18:53.670
Dance of the Bee Sting:
True Flutter.

289
00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:56.906
A marvelous thrust.

290
00:18:56.930 --> 00:18:58.850
I hardly even saw it.

291
00:19:00.810 --> 00:19:02.560
Blood Demon Art:

292
00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:05.810
Frozen Lotus.

293
00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.376
[Shinobu shivering] So cold.

294
00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:10.730
It feels like my lungs are bursting.

295
00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:12.966
[DOMA] Hmm.

296
00:19:12.990 --> 00:19:15.150
Look at that. You are fast.

297
00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:17.796
Unfortunately for you.

298
00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:20.966
those thrusts aren't enough
to kill a demon.

299
00:19:20.990 --> 00:19:22.200
[slurps]

300
00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.096
[rattling]

301
00:19:24.120 --> 00:19:25.830
Aim for here.

302
00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:28.920
You need to chop off my head.

303
00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.977
DESTROY

304
00:19:31.001 --> 00:19:33.896
My thrusts alone may not be enough.

305
00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:35.406
but what of this?

306
00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:37.510
- [clanks]
- [ratchets. clicks]

307
00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:39.470
[Doma groans]

308
00:19:39.890 --> 00:19:42.116
[SHINOBU] Time to see
whether this toxin

309
00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.890
works on an Upper Rank.

310
00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:50.230
Sister. lend me your strength. please.

311
00:19:51.020 --> 00:19:52.296
[retches]

312
00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:54.216
[straining] This poison.

313
00:19:54.240 --> 00:19:57.426
It's clearly far stronger
than the strain you used

314
00:19:57.450 --> 00:20:00.240
up on Rui's mountain. [wheezing]

315
00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:02.990
[SHINOBU] So they did
exchange information.

316
00:20:03.450 --> 00:20:05.846
This is the drawback to using poison.

317
00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:09.896
[DOMA] He told me that
you've been changing concoction

318
00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:13.226
for each demon you face.
[straining]

319
00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:15.590
- [coughs. retches]
- [blood splatters]

320
00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:18.050
[wheezing]

321
00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:22.236
Oh. my.

322
00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:26.706
It would seem that I've already
neutralized all of your poison.

323
00:20:26.730 --> 00:20:28.036
How rude of me.

324
00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:31.360
And after you'd made it just for me.

325
00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:33.770
That sword of yours.

326
00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:37.570
it makes quite an interesting
sound when you sheathe it.

327
00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:41.676
Is that where you change
what poison you use?

328
00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:44.490
Yay! This is fun!

329
00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:48.226
Who knew being poisoned
was so invigorating?

330
00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:50.016
It's almost addictive.

331
00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.516
What will the next formula
be like? [chuckles]

332
00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:54.920
Come on. let's give it a try.

333
00:20:56.550 --> 00:20:58.550
- [swishing]
- [rattling]

334
00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:02.590
Very well then.

335
00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.736
I'll oblige.

336
00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:05.810
See...

337
00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:12.310
I'd already anticipated this would happen.

338
00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:15.770
[Doma chuckling]
Is your next batch set?

339
00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:18.150
I'm ready whenever you are.

340
00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:25.410
I know I just said to give it a try...

341
00:21:26.950 --> 00:21:29.870
but you could at least
change up your offense.

342
00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:33.920
- [metallic clanking]
- [Doma chuckles]

343
00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:37.380
- [continues chuckling]
- [grunts]

344
00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:46.326
What's this?

345
00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:48.826
You seem to be slower than earlier.

346
00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.366
So sad.

347
00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:53.826
[SHINOBU] Insect Breathing.
Dance of the Horsefly:

348
00:21:53.850 --> 00:21:55.860
Enticing Slash!

349
00:22:03.320 --> 00:22:06.596
Oh. my.
You were able to land a hit.

350
00:22:06.620 --> 00:22:09.476
The way you got through
all my defenses.

351
00:22:09.500 --> 00:22:10.976
it's amazing!

352
00:22:11.000 --> 00:22:12.516
I'm truly impressed.

353
00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:15.566
It's almost enough
to bring a tear to my eye.

354
00:22:15.590 --> 00:22:17.816
Come on. what are you waiting for?

355
00:22:17.840 --> 00:22:21.816
Hurry up and attack me again.
before I stop the poison.

356
00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:24.486
Please? You're doing so well.

357
00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:26.326
Maybe the next attack kills me.

358
00:22:26.350 --> 00:22:27.390
[disgruntled sigh]

359
00:22:31.230 --> 00:22:34.770
[laughs] Yes! That's the spirit!

360
00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:40.206
Ever since I was a child.

361
00:22:40.230 --> 00:22:42.240
I was kind and clever.

362
00:22:43.030 --> 00:22:45.296
I always helped those who were in need

363
00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:47.780
and led them to the path of happiness.

364
00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:50.620
It was my duty after all.

365
00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:55.080
[DOMA'S FATHER] His eyes
have the colors of a rainbow.

366
00:22:56.080 --> 00:22:59.210
And this gray hair
is proof of his innocence.

367
00:23:00.210 --> 00:23:02.170
This child is truly special.

368
00:23:02.670 --> 00:23:05.406
Surely he can hear
the voices of the gods.

369
00:23:05.430 --> 00:23:07.326
[♪ slow piano notes playing]

370
00:23:07.350 --> 00:23:11.060
[DOMA] My parents were
hopelessly naive simpletons.

371
00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:13.206
You'd have to be

372
00:23:13.230 --> 00:23:17.060
in order to found a religion
like the Eternal Paradise Faith.

373
00:23:18.020 --> 00:23:19.626
I pitied them.

374
00:23:19.650 --> 00:23:23.190
so I always played along
with their make-believe ideas.

375
00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:27.240
I never once heard the voice of the gods.

376
00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:30.886
At first. I didn't know how to deal

377
00:23:30.910 --> 00:23:34.460
with the hordes of people
worshiping and praying to me.

378
00:23:35.410 --> 00:23:38.476
Seeing these grown-ups
come crying to a child

379
00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:41.606
saying they were suffering.
pleading for help.

380
00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:45.010
made me worry
if they were sick in the head.

381
00:23:46.260 --> 00:23:49.986
After nearly putting me to sleep
with their personal stories.

382
00:23:50.010 --> 00:23:51.696
they would bow to me.

383
00:23:51.720 --> 00:23:54.350
asking to be guided to paradise.

384
00:23:54.850 --> 00:23:56.140
I cried.

385
00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:59.520
"You poor things." I thought.

386
00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:02.070
"Paradise doesn't even exist.

387
00:24:02.730 --> 00:24:06.860
It's just a fairy tale
concocted by deluded humans.

388
00:24:07.950 --> 00:24:10.450
There are no gods or Buddhas."

389
00:24:11.080 --> 00:24:13.596
These people had lived for decades.

390
00:24:13.620 --> 00:24:16.790
yet they still couldn't grasp
that simple truth.

391
00:24:17.330 --> 00:24:20.476
When you die.
you return to nothingness.

392
00:24:20.500 --> 00:24:22.630
All feeling ceases.

393
00:24:23.380 --> 00:24:25.106
Your heart stops.

394
00:24:25.130 --> 00:24:26.896
Your brain stops.

395
00:24:26.920 --> 00:24:29.220
You rot and return to the earth.

396
00:24:29.720 --> 00:24:32.890
Such is the fate of every living creature.

397
00:24:35.060 --> 00:24:38.310
To be too foolish to accept reality.

398
00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:41.110
what a hard life that must be.

399
00:24:42.110 --> 00:24:45.320
I want to bring happiness
to these pitiful people.

400
00:24:45.820 --> 00:24:47.490
I want to save them.

401
00:24:48.360 --> 00:24:52.740
I truly believe that is my purpose here.

402
00:24:56.750 --> 00:24:57.727
[squelches]

403
00:24:57.751 --> 00:24:58.886
[blade rasps]

404
00:24:58.910 --> 00:25:01.606
- Aw. Still nothing.
- [metallic rattling]

405
00:25:01.630 --> 00:25:03.316
And that was number five.

406
00:25:03.340 --> 00:25:04.840
What will you do?

407
00:25:05.380 --> 00:25:07.840
The toxin's getting less effective.

408
00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:11.010
How many more times
do you think you can adapt it?

409
00:25:11.590 --> 00:25:13.930
- Oh! Are you out of breath now?
- [panting]

410
00:25:14.470 --> 00:25:16.116
Look at all that sweat.

411
00:25:16.140 --> 00:25:17.480
Are you all right?

412
00:25:18.100 --> 00:25:21.150
[SHINOBU] So. this is the power
of an Upper Rank.

413
00:25:21.850 --> 00:25:23.900
None of my poisons are working.

414
00:25:24.810 --> 00:25:27.990
He's adapting too fast to keep up with.

415
00:25:30.150 --> 00:25:32.546
Your alveoli must be dead now.

416
00:25:32.570 --> 00:25:34.676
[crystals tinkling]

417
00:25:34.700 --> 00:25:36.096
Painful.

418
00:25:36.120 --> 00:25:39.460
You did breathe it in.
my Blood Demon Art.

419
00:25:41.620 --> 00:25:44.476
[SHINOBU] He turns
his frozen blood into mist

420
00:25:44.500 --> 00:25:46.856
and disperses it with his fans.

421
00:25:46.880 --> 00:25:49.970
Even breathing around him
is dangerous now.

422
00:25:55.720 --> 00:25:56.866
[clangs]

423
00:25:56.890 --> 00:25:57.930
[ratchets. clicks]

424
00:25:58.390 --> 00:26:01.980
This time. I'll increase
the dose with multiple strikes!

425
00:26:02.810 --> 00:26:06.036
Insect Breathing.
Dance of the Dragonfly:

426
00:26:06.060 --> 00:26:07.690
♪

427
00:26:12.860 --> 00:26:15.160
Compound Eye Hexagon!

428
00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:19.096
I can't believe it!

429
00:26:19.120 --> 00:26:21.096
Such blazing speed!

430
00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:24.630
You might be the fastest Hashira
I've ever met.

431
00:26:27.000 --> 00:26:28.420
- [blood squelches]
- [gasps]

432
00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:31.356
[SHINOBU] He... got me.

433
00:26:31.380 --> 00:26:32.656
[grunts]

434
00:26:32.680 --> 00:26:34.446
Forget the poison.

435
00:26:34.470 --> 00:26:36.640
Why not try to decapitate me?

436
00:26:37.180 --> 00:26:39.600
With your speed.
you might have won.

437
00:26:40.560 --> 00:26:42.786
[laughs sarcastically]
Maybe not.

438
00:26:42.810 --> 00:26:45.020
I mean. you are small.

439
00:26:45.520 --> 00:26:47.060
[gasps. breathing shakily]

440
00:26:48.860 --> 00:26:51.940
[SHINOBU] Why are my hands
so small? I wonder.

441
00:26:53.700 --> 00:26:56.870
How come I was never able
to grow taller?

442
00:26:58.780 --> 00:27:01.620
If my stature were just a little bigger.

443
00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:05.500
could I have been able to behead
and defeat a demon?

444
00:27:06.330 --> 00:27:08.856
The longer your arms and legs are.

445
00:27:08.880 --> 00:27:10.736
the more muscles you have.

446
00:27:10.760 --> 00:27:13.340
which means more strength
in your attacks.

447
00:27:14.800 --> 00:27:16.486
[♪ tender music playing]

448
00:27:16.510 --> 00:27:19.446
My sister was also of small frame.

449
00:27:19.470 --> 00:27:21.350
but she was taller than I.

450
00:27:23.480 --> 00:27:26.100
How I envy Mr. Himejima.

451
00:27:26.690 --> 00:27:29.206
Seeing someone like him
come to the rescue

452
00:27:29.230 --> 00:27:31.020
would give anyone relief.

453
00:27:34.860 --> 00:27:37.990
I know what my sister
really wanted to say.

454
00:27:38.700 --> 00:27:40.790
but didn't have the heart to.

455
00:27:44.200 --> 00:27:45.726
[DOMA] Oh. no!

456
00:27:45.750 --> 00:27:47.790
Have our games come to an end?

457
00:27:48.170 --> 00:27:49.710
That's too bad.

458
00:27:50.670 --> 00:27:52.710
[metallic rattling]

459
00:27:53.300 --> 00:27:56.380
[SHINOBU] "I don't think
you'll win against that demon."

460
00:27:56.930 --> 00:27:59.196
[voice breaking] That's what
you were going to say.

461
00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:01.680
But you stopped yourself.
didn't you?

462
00:28:02.180 --> 00:28:03.970
[KANAE] Pull yourself together.

463
00:28:09.610 --> 00:28:11.570
This is no time for tears.

464
00:28:13.230 --> 00:28:14.280
[SHINOBU] Sister.

465
00:28:15.240 --> 00:28:16.466
[KANAE] Stand up.

466
00:28:16.490 --> 00:28:19.926
[SHINOBU] I can't.
I've lost so much blood.

467
00:28:19.950 --> 00:28:23.240
My left lung is punctured
and I can't even breathe.

468
00:28:23.790 --> 00:28:25.450
You can and you will.

469
00:28:26.040 --> 00:28:29.500
Stand up.
You are a Hashira. Shinobu.

470
00:28:29.920 --> 00:28:31.710
[grunting softly]

471
00:28:32.340 --> 00:28:35.316
If you've made up your mind
to defeat him. then do so.

472
00:28:35.340 --> 00:28:37.010
No excuses.

473
00:28:38.380 --> 00:28:40.850
Win by whatever means you can.

474
00:28:41.390 --> 00:28:43.486
Remember your promise.

475
00:28:43.510 --> 00:28:45.180
to me and Kanao.

476
00:28:47.690 --> 00:28:48.940
[SHINOBU] Kanao.

477
00:28:51.940 --> 00:28:53.836
[DOMA] Forgive me.

478
00:28:53.860 --> 00:28:56.296
You must be suffering right now.

479
00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:58.450
[whimpering softly]

480
00:29:00.030 --> 00:29:01.216
[gasps]

481
00:29:01.240 --> 00:29:03.330
I know that you have it in you.

482
00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:05.080
Do your best.

483
00:29:06.040 --> 00:29:07.960
- Huh?
- [metallic rattling]

484
00:29:09.120 --> 00:29:10.210
[quivers]

485
00:29:11.330 --> 00:29:16.026
Wait. Are you... standing up?
[exclaims in amazement]

486
00:29:16.050 --> 00:29:17.646
Scary.

487
00:29:17.670 --> 00:29:19.986
Are you actually a human?

488
00:29:20.010 --> 00:29:24.100
I slashed your collarbone.
your lungs. and your ribs.

489
00:29:25.220 --> 00:29:27.286
At your diminutive size

490
00:29:27.310 --> 00:29:29.616
and the amount of blood you've lost.

491
00:29:29.640 --> 00:29:31.706
how are you not dead right now?

492
00:29:31.730 --> 00:29:32.786
[coughs]

493
00:29:32.810 --> 00:29:34.376
See? Right there.

494
00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:37.376
There clearly is blood
gurgling in your lungs.

495
00:29:37.400 --> 00:29:39.990
The pain must be unimaginable.

496
00:29:40.450 --> 00:29:43.216
Surrender and I'll put an end
to your suffering.

497
00:29:43.240 --> 00:29:44.530
It'll be quick.

498
00:29:45.450 --> 00:29:47.386
It's too late for you.

499
00:29:47.410 --> 00:29:49.176
So. just let go.

500
00:29:49.200 --> 00:29:51.936
[SHINOBU] I'll make a go
for his neck this time

501
00:29:51.960 --> 00:29:55.380
and put everything I have left
into this strike!

502
00:29:56.000 --> 00:29:59.800
Insect Breathing.
Dance of the Centipede.

503
00:30:00.300 --> 00:30:01.446
[DOMA] Hmm?

504
00:30:01.470 --> 00:30:03.470
[SHINOBU] Hundred-Legged Zigzag.

505
00:30:04.300 --> 00:30:06.180
[♪ dramatic music playing]

506
00:30:08.270 --> 00:30:09.390
[groans]

507
00:30:26.410 --> 00:30:29.240
[DOMA] It feels like
she's everywhere at once.

508
00:30:30.080 --> 00:30:32.580
Just her movement destroyed the bridge.

509
00:30:33.420 --> 00:30:35.226
[squeaking]

510
00:30:35.250 --> 00:30:37.540
So fast. I can't follow her.

511
00:30:38.420 --> 00:30:39.630
[impact grunts]

512
00:30:43.880 --> 00:30:44.946
From below?

513
00:30:44.970 --> 00:30:46.220
[gasps]

514
00:30:49.010 --> 00:30:50.520
[Shinobu grunts]

515
00:30:54.190 --> 00:30:57.270
- [glass shatters]
- [♪ music swells. fades]

516
00:30:58.900 --> 00:31:00.570
[SHINOBU] Back when I was a child...

517
00:31:02.070 --> 00:31:04.086
I thought of happiness like a road.

518
00:31:04.110 --> 00:31:06.636
one that stretched on into the distance

519
00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:08.756
with no end in sight.

520
00:31:08.780 --> 00:31:10.386
[laughter]

521
00:31:10.410 --> 00:31:11.750
[blood splatters]

522
00:31:12.410 --> 00:31:15.056
It wasn't until it was destroyed

523
00:31:15.080 --> 00:31:17.226
that I finally realized

524
00:31:17.250 --> 00:31:21.226
the road beneath my feet
was but a thin sheet of glass.

525
00:31:21.250 --> 00:31:23.646
♪

526
00:31:23.670 --> 00:31:28.260
However. some haven't had
the glass broken yet.

527
00:31:29.100 --> 00:31:33.600
All I wanted after being saved
was to become stronger...

528
00:31:34.600 --> 00:31:38.770
so that some day.
I could protect those people.

529
00:31:40.190 --> 00:31:44.030
So... we made a promise.

530
00:31:46.240 --> 00:31:51.740
To vanquish the demons
as many as we could. together.

531
00:31:52.410 --> 00:31:54.000
[♪ poignant music playing]

532
00:31:54.870 --> 00:31:57.766
In hopes that the pain we suffered

533
00:31:57.790 --> 00:32:00.380
would never be felt by another.

534
00:32:08.930 --> 00:32:10.760
Even if I'm weak...

535
00:32:14.390 --> 00:32:17.616
even if I can't decapitate demons.

536
00:32:17.640 --> 00:32:19.916
if I can take down just one.

537
00:32:19.940 --> 00:32:22.206
I can save dozens of lives.

538
00:32:22.230 --> 00:32:24.320
And if that demon's an Upper Rank.

539
00:32:24.990 --> 00:32:27.240
it could mean saving hundreds.

540
00:32:28.820 --> 00:32:32.030
It's not a matter of can or cannot.

541
00:32:32.620 --> 00:32:35.080
This is something I have to do.

542
00:32:40.290 --> 00:32:41.840
Are you angry?

543
00:32:43.800 --> 00:32:47.316
[SHINOBU] Yes. I am angry. Tanjiro.

544
00:32:47.340 --> 00:32:48.720
I'm furious.

545
00:32:49.470 --> 00:32:50.640
In fact...

546
00:32:51.600 --> 00:32:53.986
I'm always angry.

547
00:32:54.010 --> 00:32:55.850
How could I not be?

548
00:32:58.140 --> 00:33:00.150
My parents were killed.

549
00:33:01.560 --> 00:33:03.980
My older sister was killed.

550
00:33:04.980 --> 00:33:08.530
My Tsuguko. other than Kanao.
were killed.

551
00:33:09.530 --> 00:33:11.360
And those poor girls.

552
00:33:12.030 --> 00:33:13.700
If it weren't for the demons...

553
00:33:14.200 --> 00:33:17.120
If it weren't for the demons
that killed their loved ones.

554
00:33:17.790 --> 00:33:20.920
they'd be living happily
with their families.

555
00:33:22.420 --> 00:33:23.436
[♪ discordant music playing]

556
00:33:23.460 --> 00:33:26.646
It's all so infuriating!

557
00:33:26.670 --> 00:33:29.050
Stop messing with me. damn it!

558
00:33:29.840 --> 00:33:33.640
Why the hell isn't my poison
working on this prick?

559
00:33:34.430 --> 00:33:36.246
You bastard!

560
00:33:36.270 --> 00:33:37.656
[exhales]

561
00:33:37.680 --> 00:33:39.770
[ice crackling]

562
00:33:47.440 --> 00:33:50.086
I'm moved! You did your best!

563
00:33:50.110 --> 00:33:52.386
Even though you're so weak.

564
00:33:52.410 --> 00:33:54.546
You must have worked so incredibly hard

565
00:33:54.570 --> 00:33:56.636
to get to this point. [sobbing]

566
00:33:56.660 --> 00:33:58.806
You're weaker than your sister.

567
00:33:58.830 --> 00:34:01.290
and yet. you somehow outlived her.

568
00:34:01.790 --> 00:34:04.896
[sniffles] It's a miracle
you survived this long.

569
00:34:04.920 --> 00:34:06.066
[body cracking]

570
00:34:06.090 --> 00:34:07.526
[coughs]

571
00:34:07.550 --> 00:34:08.856
Even when hope is gone.

572
00:34:08.880 --> 00:34:11.340
humans always fight to the bitter end.

573
00:34:11.880 --> 00:34:13.816
Humans are so foolish.

574
00:34:13.840 --> 00:34:16.470
But that's what makes them so beautiful.

575
00:34:17.350 --> 00:34:19.980
I deem you worthy
of becoming part of me.

576
00:34:20.480 --> 00:34:23.560
[sobbing] You and I shall share eternity!

577
00:34:26.900 --> 00:34:28.860
Do you have any last words?

578
00:34:29.440 --> 00:34:30.690
I'm listening.

579
00:34:35.490 --> 00:34:38.330
Rot in hell. you bastard!

580
00:34:42.330 --> 00:34:44.620
[exclaims in horror] Master!

581
00:34:47.630 --> 00:34:49.050
[bones crunching]

582
00:34:49.880 --> 00:34:52.856
[exclaims in anguish]

583
00:34:52.880 --> 00:34:55.010
[bones crunching]

584
00:35:00.640 --> 00:35:02.020
[clangs]

585
00:35:04.900 --> 00:35:06.480
[clatters]

586
00:35:07.190 --> 00:35:08.820
[quivering]

587
00:35:09.650 --> 00:35:12.610
[screaming in agony]

588
00:35:13.320 --> 00:35:15.320
♪

589
00:35:16.320 --> 00:35:19.056
[ZENITSU] I can't shake
the feeling he's here.

590
00:35:19.080 --> 00:35:20.450
He must be.

591
00:35:20.910 --> 00:35:23.500
He's got a score to settle with me. too.

592
00:35:30.800 --> 00:35:32.186
The people we love.

593
00:35:32.210 --> 00:35:35.680
the people we hold dear are so precious.

594
00:35:36.130 --> 00:35:38.720
We take for granted
that they'll always be there.

595
00:35:39.180 --> 00:35:43.156
However. that's just a selfish delusion.

596
00:35:43.180 --> 00:35:45.100
Flower Breathing...

597
00:35:45.600 --> 00:35:47.746
[ZENITSU] Because the thought
of living without them

598
00:35:47.770 --> 00:35:49.706
is simply unbearable.

599
00:35:49.730 --> 00:35:50.980
Fourth Form:

600
00:35:51.650 --> 00:35:53.876
Crimson Hanagoromo!

601
00:35:53.900 --> 00:35:55.700
[shatters]

602
00:35:56.860 --> 00:35:57.950
[grunts]

603
00:36:00.580 --> 00:36:03.620
[DOMA] Wow!
You nearly got me there.

604
00:36:07.170 --> 00:36:09.960
[ZENITSU] "They'll always be
alive and close by."

605
00:36:11.090 --> 00:36:13.760
It's a naive thought. I know.

606
00:36:14.340 --> 00:36:16.220
but we all wanna believe it.

607
00:36:19.430 --> 00:36:22.866
Would you mind holding off
your attacks for just a second?

608
00:36:22.890 --> 00:36:25.930
- I'm trying to absorb her.
- [flesh squelching]

609
00:36:28.730 --> 00:36:30.860
[seething]

610
00:36:33.360 --> 00:36:34.876
[DOMA] How strange.

611
00:36:34.900 --> 00:36:37.570
You're not taking the bait. are you?

612
00:36:38.240 --> 00:36:40.296
What she did earlier.

613
00:36:40.320 --> 00:36:42.910
that motion she made with her fingers.

614
00:36:43.370 --> 00:36:46.330
Was that her warning you of my powers?

615
00:36:46.830 --> 00:36:49.670
I'm impressed she thought
to do that so quickly.

616
00:36:50.130 --> 00:36:51.880
Good job you did it.

617
00:36:52.420 --> 00:36:54.300
Too bad it doesn't matter.

618
00:36:54.800 --> 00:36:56.816
- [flesh squelching]
- [clatters]

619
00:36:56.840 --> 00:37:00.010
Well. in case you were wondering.

620
00:37:00.550 --> 00:37:03.736
your master was tastier than I imagined.

621
00:37:03.760 --> 00:37:05.020
[slurps]

622
00:37:05.560 --> 00:37:07.326
And now. you're here.

623
00:37:07.350 --> 00:37:10.770
It's just one feast
after another. it seems.

624
00:37:11.560 --> 00:37:14.690
Ah. this truly is...

625
00:37:15.280 --> 00:37:17.740
a wonderful night.

626
00:37:18.320 --> 00:37:21.490
[seething]

627
00:37:31.080 --> 00:37:32.420
You can't hide.

628
00:37:33.000 --> 00:37:34.340
Come out.

629
00:37:35.170 --> 00:37:37.550
Have some dignity and face me.

630
00:37:40.090 --> 00:37:42.986
[DEMON] Sounds like someone
ought to teach you some manners.

631
00:37:43.010 --> 00:37:45.260
Did you forget that I'm your senior?

632
00:37:45.850 --> 00:37:49.310
You look a little stronger
than the last time I saw ya.

633
00:37:50.020 --> 00:37:53.980
It's too bad you still reek
of being a pathetic weakling.

634
00:37:56.610 --> 00:37:57.587
[clatters]

635
00:37:57.611 --> 00:37:58.966
UPPER SIX

636
00:37:58.990 --> 00:38:03.216
It's been a while.
hasn't it... Zenitsu?

637
00:38:03.240 --> 00:38:05.030
[chuckles]

638
00:38:05.990 --> 00:38:07.426
[ZENITSU] Kaigaku.

639
00:38:07.450 --> 00:38:09.830
You don't get my respect.

640
00:38:10.210 --> 00:38:11.766
You're a demon.

641
00:38:11.790 --> 00:38:13.670
You'll be treated as such.

642
00:38:21.430 --> 00:38:22.486
[Nakime plucking biwa strings]

643
00:38:22.510 --> 00:38:23.946
- [rumbles]
- [Tanjiro gasps]

644
00:38:23.970 --> 00:38:25.010
[grunts]

645
00:38:27.060 --> 00:38:29.560
Water Breathing. Ninth Form:

646
00:38:31.350 --> 00:38:33.730
Splashing Water Flow. Turbulent!

647
00:38:34.810 --> 00:38:36.166
[grunts]

648
00:38:36.190 --> 00:38:37.416
Stay focused!

649
00:38:37.440 --> 00:38:38.690
All right!

650
00:38:39.900 --> 00:38:42.006
This place is insane.

651
00:38:42.030 --> 00:38:44.636
The building keeps shifting
and rearranging itself

652
00:38:44.660 --> 00:38:46.346
as if it's alive.

653
00:38:46.370 --> 00:38:49.200
I can tell that it's trying to separate us.

654
00:38:50.290 --> 00:38:52.976
We have to regroup
with the other Corps members

655
00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:55.380
and stay together till we reach Muzan!

656
00:38:59.250 --> 00:39:01.170
[cawing]

657
00:39:01.590 --> 00:39:03.316
[cawing]

658
00:39:03.340 --> 00:39:04.986
Attention!

659
00:39:05.010 --> 00:39:07.220
Shinobu Kocho is dead!

660
00:39:07.890 --> 00:39:10.326
She fought valiantly against Upper Two

661
00:39:10.350 --> 00:39:12.060
but was defeated!

662
00:39:19.270 --> 00:39:21.530
- [gasps]
- [muted silence]

663
00:39:24.950 --> 00:39:27.120
[♪ poignant music playing]

664
00:39:28.490 --> 00:39:30.620
[inaudible laughter]

665
00:39:43.760 --> 00:39:45.550
[seething]

666
00:39:49.140 --> 00:39:51.060
[cawing]

667
00:39:53.310 --> 00:39:54.616
[GIYU] Strange.

668
00:39:54.640 --> 00:39:57.190
There's a piece of paper
wrapped around its neck.

669
00:39:57.690 --> 00:39:59.520
How are the crows already here?

670
00:40:00.520 --> 00:40:03.320
[♪ epic dramatic music playing]

671
00:40:03.990 --> 00:40:05.796
Shinobu is dead.

672
00:40:05.820 --> 00:40:07.910
but we must push forward.

673
00:40:08.280 --> 00:40:10.870
Think only of what must be done
for victory.

674
00:40:11.370 --> 00:40:12.490
[KUINA. KANATA] Right.

675
00:40:14.790 --> 00:40:16.186
And what about the others?

676
00:40:16.210 --> 00:40:18.580
I need reports on their whereabouts.

677
00:40:20.080 --> 00:40:21.816
[KANATA] Center of the 40th vertical

678
00:40:21.840 --> 00:40:23.686
and 12th horizontal levels.

679
00:40:23.710 --> 00:40:25.356
[fight grunts]

680
00:40:25.380 --> 00:40:27.356
The Corps members are fighting off

681
00:40:27.380 --> 00:40:30.300
what appears to be at least ten demons.

682
00:40:32.100 --> 00:40:35.430
[fight grunts]

683
00:40:37.190 --> 00:40:40.206
However. more than 30 demons
are moving in their direction

684
00:40:40.230 --> 00:40:41.690
from behind the walls.

685
00:40:47.900 --> 00:40:49.966
[KIRIYA] Using Mr. Yushiro's eyes.

686
00:40:49.990 --> 00:40:52.506
we're able to see Blood Demon Arts.

687
00:40:52.530 --> 00:40:55.740
something that isn't possible
to do with the human eye.

688
00:40:56.660 --> 00:40:58.896
Each red light is a Blood Demon Art.

689
00:40:58.920 --> 00:41:02.210
The more intense they glow.
the more potent their power.

690
00:41:03.090 --> 00:41:05.726
In this place. the entire area.

691
00:41:05.750 --> 00:41:09.050
buildings and all. must also be
a Blood Demon Art.

692
00:41:09.800 --> 00:41:12.800
There's seemingly no end in sight to it.

693
00:41:15.220 --> 00:41:17.230
What incredible power!

694
00:41:18.560 --> 00:41:20.076
A demon labyrinth

695
00:41:20.100 --> 00:41:22.560
with the ability to branch out endlessly.

696
00:41:25.860 --> 00:41:27.666
And here we lie at its center.

697
00:41:27.690 --> 00:41:30.570
trapped within the walls
of this infinite castle.

698
00:41:31.280 --> 00:41:32.870
[KAKUSHI 1] This one's finished.

699
00:41:34.740 --> 00:41:38.136
[KIRIYA] However. it's not as if
we've been caught off guard.

700
00:41:38.160 --> 00:41:39.160
KAKUSHI

701
00:41:39.410 --> 00:41:42.580
My father prepared
for this day meticulously.

702
00:41:43.330 --> 00:41:45.526
With Gyomei's cooperation.

703
00:41:45.550 --> 00:41:47.566
he had the Hashira within arm's reach

704
00:41:47.590 --> 00:41:49.146
to mobilize at any time.

705
00:41:49.170 --> 00:41:52.156
To prevent the Corps members
from being isolated.

706
00:41:52.180 --> 00:41:54.946
he sent the Kasugai Crows
to gather them into groups

707
00:41:54.970 --> 00:41:55.970
and waited.

708
00:41:57.060 --> 00:42:00.666
He enlisted the aid
of Ms. Tamayo and Mr. Yushiro.

709
00:42:00.690 --> 00:42:01.890
And finally.

710
00:42:02.520 --> 00:42:04.810
to ensure that their plan would succeed.

711
00:42:05.320 --> 00:42:07.900
my sisters and our parents

712
00:42:08.400 --> 00:42:10.570
readily sacrificed their lives.

713
00:42:13.910 --> 00:42:15.410
We cannot lose.

714
00:42:15.950 --> 00:42:17.370
no matter what!

715
00:42:20.580 --> 00:42:23.210
[♪ music intensifies]

716
00:42:23.870 --> 00:42:25.686
Amongst the Blood Demon Arts.

717
00:42:25.710 --> 00:42:28.986
there are five traces of power
that tower over the rest

718
00:42:29.010 --> 00:42:31.010
as if flaunting their strength.

719
00:42:31.630 --> 00:42:34.010
These must be Upper Ranks.

720
00:42:34.720 --> 00:42:36.276
One of them is at the same spot

721
00:42:36.300 --> 00:42:38.600
where Shinobu was last seen fighting.

722
00:42:39.180 --> 00:42:40.656
Found another!

723
00:42:40.680 --> 00:42:43.666
Upper Six and Zenitsu have just
encountered each other!

724
00:42:43.690 --> 00:42:45.286
An Upper Rank!

725
00:42:45.310 --> 00:42:46.496
Is he alone?

726
00:42:46.520 --> 00:42:49.086
[KUINA] He is.
It looks to be a one-on-one!

727
00:42:49.110 --> 00:42:52.006
[KIRIYA] A Hinoe can't beat
an Upper Rank by themself.

728
00:42:52.030 --> 00:42:53.150
Send backup!

729
00:42:58.790 --> 00:43:00.056
[KAIGAKU] Hmm.

730
00:43:00.080 --> 00:43:02.186
What. you're frozen in fear?

731
00:43:02.210 --> 00:43:04.306
Guess some things never change.

732
00:43:04.330 --> 00:43:06.580
Once a coward. always a coward.

733
00:43:07.590 --> 00:43:09.646
Did you ever become a Hashira?

734
00:43:09.670 --> 00:43:11.736
[scoffs] Guess not.

735
00:43:11.760 --> 00:43:13.050
That's too bad.

736
00:43:13.550 --> 00:43:17.720
Got any new techniques?
Or still just First Form?

737
00:43:18.760 --> 00:43:20.406
For an Upper Rank bottom feeder

738
00:43:20.430 --> 00:43:22.576
who's nothing more than a spare blade.

739
00:43:22.600 --> 00:43:24.850
you're sure acting awfully proud.

740
00:43:25.730 --> 00:43:28.586
[Kaigaku sarcastically]
Wow! [laughs]

741
00:43:28.610 --> 00:43:31.740
Who taught you to talk
like that? New friends?

742
00:43:32.240 --> 00:43:34.570
[ZENITSU] Why the hell
did you become a demon?

743
00:43:35.070 --> 00:43:37.256
[laughs] You'd never understand.

744
00:43:37.280 --> 00:43:39.806
You were supposed to succeed
Thunder Breathing!

745
00:43:39.830 --> 00:43:41.290
But you tarnished it!

746
00:43:42.750 --> 00:43:43.886
Huh?

747
00:43:43.910 --> 00:43:46.186
[ZENITSU] After you became a demon.

748
00:43:46.210 --> 00:43:47.420
he...

749
00:43:49.090 --> 00:43:50.800
He committed seppuku!

750
00:43:51.300 --> 00:43:52.566
[♪ poignant music playing]

751
00:43:52.590 --> 00:43:53.960
[voice breaking] Even worse.

752
00:43:54.510 --> 00:43:56.220
he did it by himself.

753
00:43:57.430 --> 00:43:59.470
He was all alone!

754
00:44:00.680 --> 00:44:02.406
Because of that. no one was there

755
00:44:02.430 --> 00:44:04.076
to put him out of his misery.

756
00:44:04.100 --> 00:44:07.326
He bled out and died a painful death.

757
00:44:07.350 --> 00:44:09.166
It's your fault!

758
00:44:09.190 --> 00:44:12.376
Gramps died the most
agonizing death possible

759
00:44:12.400 --> 00:44:14.546
all because the Thunder Breathing rights

760
00:44:14.570 --> 00:44:15.740
produced a demon!

761
00:44:17.450 --> 00:44:19.620
Why the hell should I care?

762
00:44:20.070 --> 00:44:22.516
Gramps died? So what?

763
00:44:22.540 --> 00:44:23.966
Want me to cry?

764
00:44:23.990 --> 00:44:26.516
Did you expect me to give it to him?

765
00:44:26.540 --> 00:44:27.790
Well. I don't.

766
00:44:28.080 --> 00:44:31.396
In fact. I don't care for anyone
who doesn't appreciate me.

767
00:44:31.420 --> 00:44:33.276
No matter what.

768
00:44:33.300 --> 00:44:35.146
this is who I am.

769
00:44:35.170 --> 00:44:38.276
Take the side
of whoever knows my worth.

770
00:44:38.300 --> 00:44:39.470
[laughs]

771
00:44:40.390 --> 00:44:42.696
If the old geezer really did die in agony.

772
00:44:42.720 --> 00:44:44.446
then I couldn't be happier.

773
00:44:44.470 --> 00:44:47.666
I slaved away for that ungrateful bastard.

774
00:44:47.690 --> 00:44:49.956
And what does he do to repay me?

775
00:44:49.980 --> 00:44:51.836
He makes you my co-successor

776
00:44:51.860 --> 00:44:53.876
instead of just letting me carry the torch!

777
00:44:53.900 --> 00:44:55.440
I hope he rots!

778
00:44:55.980 --> 00:44:58.126
Former Hashira or not.

779
00:44:58.150 --> 00:45:01.596
I would never shed a tear
over some senile geezer.

780
00:45:01.620 --> 00:45:04.410
[laughs boorishly]

781
00:45:06.750 --> 00:45:09.420
[ZENITSU] Gramps knew
exactly what he was doing.

782
00:45:09.920 --> 00:45:13.146
We were made co-successors
because we're weak.

783
00:45:13.170 --> 00:45:15.526
I was only able to use the First Form

784
00:45:15.550 --> 00:45:18.380
while you could use
everything but First Form.

785
00:45:19.010 --> 00:45:21.066
I can't help but feel sorry for Gramps

786
00:45:21.090 --> 00:45:23.526
that he has two useless successors!

787
00:45:23.550 --> 00:45:25.406
[KAIGAKU] Don't lump us together!

788
00:45:25.430 --> 00:45:27.520
I'm nothing like you!

789
00:45:28.020 --> 00:45:32.336
Thunder Breathing. Fourth Form:
Distant Thunder!

790
00:45:32.360 --> 00:45:34.520
[♪ intense dramatic music playing]

791
00:45:35.820 --> 00:45:37.190
[gasps]

792
00:45:40.030 --> 00:45:42.346
You're so slow. scum.

793
00:45:42.370 --> 00:45:43.950
- [groans]
- [blood splatters]

794
00:45:47.910 --> 00:45:50.646
[KAIGAKU] What the hell? He got me.

795
00:45:50.670 --> 00:45:52.306
His speed is unreal.

796
00:45:52.330 --> 00:45:54.896
He never moved like that.

797
00:45:54.920 --> 00:45:56.630
He's changed.

798
00:45:58.170 --> 00:46:00.470
But he's not the only one.

799
00:46:04.390 --> 00:46:06.510
[wet squelching]

800
00:46:10.940 --> 00:46:14.206
There's no shame in kneeling
down before the powerful

801
00:46:14.230 --> 00:46:15.730
if it means surviving.

802
00:46:16.230 --> 00:46:18.126
As long as you're alive.

803
00:46:18.150 --> 00:46:19.940
you can still win.

804
00:46:21.320 --> 00:46:24.490
Only once you die have you lost.

805
00:46:24.990 --> 00:46:28.290
Even if you have to beg
on your hands and knees.

806
00:46:28.830 --> 00:46:32.120
Even if you're without a home
and have to drink from a puddle.

807
00:46:32.580 --> 00:46:36.080
Even if they condemn you
for stealing money.

808
00:46:37.090 --> 00:46:38.436
As long as you're alive.

809
00:46:38.460 --> 00:46:40.840
there's still a future where you can win.

810
00:46:41.340 --> 00:46:44.970
Believing that is all that's kept me going.

811
00:46:46.930 --> 00:46:49.366
[KOKUSHIBO] Forfeit your humanity

812
00:46:49.390 --> 00:46:52.940
and limitless power will be within reach.

813
00:46:53.440 --> 00:46:56.626
Should my Lord
choose to acknowledge you.

814
00:46:56.650 --> 00:47:00.070
demon blood
shall course through your veins.

815
00:47:01.860 --> 00:47:03.200
[Kaigaku quivers]

816
00:47:03.860 --> 00:47:05.756
The stronger the swordsman.

817
00:47:05.780 --> 00:47:09.080
the longer it takes for him
to become a demon.

818
00:47:09.870 --> 00:47:13.540
It took me three days to fully transform.

819
00:47:14.040 --> 00:47:16.896
Turning a breathing technique
user into a demon

820
00:47:16.920 --> 00:47:18.646
is no small feat.

821
00:47:18.670 --> 00:47:20.476
Doing such a thing will require

822
00:47:20.500 --> 00:47:23.340
an exorbitant amount of my Lord's blood.

823
00:47:24.090 --> 00:47:26.066
And though it is rare.

824
00:47:26.090 --> 00:47:27.986
some people.
for whatever reason.

825
00:47:28.010 --> 00:47:30.536
are physically incapable
of becoming demons.

826
00:47:30.560 --> 00:47:31.560
Huh?

827
00:47:32.180 --> 00:47:35.166
[KOKUSHIBO] I'm curious to see
how you will fare.

828
00:47:35.190 --> 00:47:36.850
UPPER ONE

829
00:47:37.350 --> 00:47:38.536
[quivers]

830
00:47:38.560 --> 00:47:41.256
You must appreciate this blood.

831
00:47:41.280 --> 00:47:46.386
Even holding it as you are now
is an honor you cannot fathom.

832
00:47:46.410 --> 00:47:48.756
Should you spill a single drop.

833
00:47:48.780 --> 00:47:51.806
I'll have you dismembered in an instant

834
00:47:51.830 --> 00:47:54.056
before it touches the ground.

835
00:47:54.080 --> 00:47:55.460
[gasps in horror]

836
00:47:56.160 --> 00:47:57.790
[breathing shakily]

837
00:47:59.290 --> 00:48:03.606
[KAIGAKU] Even now.
I remember the terror I felt.

838
00:48:03.630 --> 00:48:07.680
Like every cell in my body
was screaming in anguish.

839
00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:12.536
Compared to what I felt then.

840
00:48:12.560 --> 00:48:14.116
this is nothing.

841
00:48:14.140 --> 00:48:16.666
- He's just a punk.
- [clatters]

842
00:48:16.690 --> 00:48:18.126
He might be stronger.

843
00:48:18.150 --> 00:48:20.230
but he's not on par with an Upper Rank.

844
00:48:21.110 --> 00:48:25.376
Zenitsu Agatsuma
is and always will be trash.

845
00:48:25.400 --> 00:48:27.336
He's a despicable crybaby

846
00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:29.886
without a shred of dignity or valor!

847
00:48:29.910 --> 00:48:31.926
Somebody. help!

848
00:48:31.950 --> 00:48:36.460
I fell in a pitfall and twisted my ankle!

849
00:48:37.120 --> 00:48:38.936
[KAIGAKU] The disrespect!

850
00:48:38.960 --> 00:48:42.670
As if I'd be co-successor
with that sniveling loser!

851
00:48:43.210 --> 00:48:45.130
[JIGORO] Here you are. Kaigaku.

852
00:48:45.670 --> 00:48:48.236
- [ZENITSU] Hey. Gramps?
- [KAIGAKU] Hmm?

853
00:48:48.260 --> 00:48:51.526
It looks a little big on me.
don't you think?

854
00:48:51.550 --> 00:48:53.826
- Maybe I'll grow into it...
- [KAIGAKU] I'm supposed to be

855
00:48:53.850 --> 00:48:56.390
- that idiot's equal?
- [both laughing]

856
00:48:57.520 --> 00:49:00.076
That's gotta be some kind of sick joke!

857
00:49:00.100 --> 00:49:01.400
[seething]

858
00:49:01.900 --> 00:49:04.376
The old bastard deserved to die!

859
00:49:04.400 --> 00:49:06.666
And if you miss him so dearly.

860
00:49:06.690 --> 00:49:09.160
then I'll see to it you join him!

861
00:49:10.450 --> 00:49:13.426
[ZENITSU] I was only ever able
to learn the First Form.

862
00:49:13.450 --> 00:49:17.290
However. you were able to learn
everything but the First Form.

863
00:49:18.500 --> 00:49:19.936
[♪ tender music playing]

864
00:49:19.960 --> 00:49:21.210
Gramps knew that.

865
00:49:21.750 --> 00:49:24.816
His solution was having us both succeed

866
00:49:24.840 --> 00:49:26.590
the Thunder Breathing technique.

867
00:49:29.180 --> 00:49:30.890
But you denied him that.

868
00:49:31.510 --> 00:49:33.866
You became a demon

869
00:49:33.890 --> 00:49:35.890
purely to reject him.

870
00:49:36.850 --> 00:49:39.116
- [crackling]
- It's coming!

871
00:49:39.140 --> 00:49:41.980
Thunder Breathing. Second Form:

872
00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:43.956
Rice Spirit!

873
00:49:43.980 --> 00:49:46.086
[♪ dramatic synth music playing]

874
00:49:46.110 --> 00:49:48.860
[ZENITSU] He attacked five times
in one breath.

875
00:49:49.490 --> 00:49:51.756
- [Kaigaku yells]
- [effort grunts. strains]

876
00:49:51.780 --> 00:49:53.716
How many people have you devoured?

877
00:49:53.740 --> 00:49:56.846
You can't even tell right
from wrong anymore!

878
00:49:56.870 --> 00:49:59.870
I'm more aware of those
than I've ever been!

879
00:50:01.080 --> 00:50:02.476
What's the matter?

880
00:50:02.500 --> 00:50:05.710
Aren't you supposed to be
the old geezer's favorite?

881
00:50:06.210 --> 00:50:07.816
- [grunts]
- If you are.

882
00:50:07.840 --> 00:50:09.986
then show me
what he passed down to you!

883
00:50:10.010 --> 00:50:13.526
It's the only technique
you've got. so use it!

884
00:50:13.550 --> 00:50:14.720
[Zenitsu grunts]

885
00:50:16.100 --> 00:50:19.206
Go all out. Use everything you got.

886
00:50:19.230 --> 00:50:21.116
- [groans angrily]
- And don't you dare hold back

887
00:50:21.140 --> 00:50:23.480
- for a second!
- [determined grunt]

888
00:50:28.280 --> 00:50:29.860
[ZENITSU] Thunder Breathing...

889
00:50:32.240 --> 00:50:33.660
First Form...

890
00:50:34.030 --> 00:50:35.030
[scoffs]

891
00:50:35.620 --> 00:50:37.530
Thunderclap and Flash.

892
00:50:40.410 --> 00:50:41.886
[effort grunts]

893
00:50:41.910 --> 00:50:43.516
[laughs boisterously]

894
00:50:43.540 --> 00:50:46.896
As if a basic attack
like charging me head-on

895
00:50:46.920 --> 00:50:48.646
would ever find its mark.

896
00:50:48.670 --> 00:50:50.420
Don't make me laugh!

897
00:50:52.220 --> 00:50:53.906
Thunder Breathing.

898
00:50:53.930 --> 00:50:57.260
Third Form: Thunder Swarm!

899
00:50:59.470 --> 00:51:01.520
[grunting]

900
00:51:02.770 --> 00:51:05.206
[ZENITSU] He's attacking me
from every angle at once.

901
00:51:05.230 --> 00:51:06.666
[KAIGAKU] What's the matter?

902
00:51:06.690 --> 00:51:08.900
Don't tell me you're done already!

903
00:51:10.110 --> 00:51:11.916
[ZENITSU]
Thunder Breathing. First Form:

904
00:51:11.940 --> 00:51:14.570
Thunderclap and Flash:
Eight Fold!

905
00:51:19.040 --> 00:51:21.620
- That's not gonna work!
- [Zenitsu grunts]

906
00:51:22.120 --> 00:51:25.250
Thunder Breathing. Fifth Form:

907
00:51:27.630 --> 00:51:29.170
Heat Lightning!

908
00:51:29.670 --> 00:51:32.130
- Ah!
- Gotcha!

909
00:51:32.800 --> 00:51:36.316
How does the bite of my Blood
Demon Art-enhanced sword feel?

910
00:51:36.340 --> 00:51:39.156
- [electricity crackling]
- Each strike on contact

911
00:51:39.180 --> 00:51:41.810
leaves a wound that burns your skin.

912
00:51:42.390 --> 00:51:46.020
This proves those who recognize
my talents and value are right!

913
00:51:46.560 --> 00:51:49.820
And those that dismiss
or condemn me are wrong!

914
00:51:50.360 --> 00:51:54.110
Do you get it now?
This is the power I have!

915
00:51:54.610 --> 00:51:56.780
My power as a demon that is!

916
00:51:57.240 --> 00:51:59.466
All you know how to do
is use First Form.

917
00:51:59.490 --> 00:52:02.556
yet that geezer chose
to make you his successor!

918
00:52:02.580 --> 00:52:05.290
And. boy.
what a mistake that was!

919
00:52:11.590 --> 00:52:12.936
So. that's it.

920
00:52:12.960 --> 00:52:15.670
This is the path
that you've chosen to take.

921
00:52:17.180 --> 00:52:18.720
[weakly] I already knew.

922
00:52:19.390 --> 00:52:20.890
I knew. but...

923
00:52:22.810 --> 00:52:24.470
[sword scraping]

924
00:52:26.060 --> 00:52:29.036
With this strike. I'll end this.

925
00:52:29.060 --> 00:52:30.536
You're finished!

926
00:52:30.560 --> 00:52:32.256
- [crackling]
- Thunder Breathing...

927
00:52:32.280 --> 00:52:35.280
- [rumbling]
- Sixth Form:

928
00:52:39.120 --> 00:52:42.410
- [crackling]
- [♪ music intensifies]

929
00:52:43.450 --> 00:52:46.136
Rumble and Flash!

930
00:52:46.160 --> 00:52:50.106
That strike I landed will keep
crackling through your flesh!

931
00:52:50.130 --> 00:52:54.106
This is the power that I gained
by becoming a demon.

932
00:52:54.130 --> 00:52:55.686
Get it now?

933
00:52:55.710 --> 00:52:58.220
I've long surpassed Thunder Breathing!

934
00:53:00.010 --> 00:53:02.196
[laughs boisterously]

935
00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:03.946
You and I aren't equals.

936
00:53:03.970 --> 00:53:05.350
And we never have been.

937
00:53:05.890 --> 00:53:07.640
I'm better than all of you.

938
00:53:08.640 --> 00:53:09.916
Guess the old bastard

939
00:53:09.940 --> 00:53:12.086
shouldn't have put
his trust in you after all.

940
00:53:12.110 --> 00:53:14.900
[laughs boisterously]

941
00:53:16.610 --> 00:53:19.110
[JIGORO] Come on.
be more like Kaigaku!

942
00:53:19.610 --> 00:53:23.216
He's your senior.
so follow his example. you hear?

943
00:53:23.240 --> 00:53:25.466
Hang on. Isn't the First Form

944
00:53:25.490 --> 00:53:28.096
pretty much the entire basis
of Thunder Breathing?

945
00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:30.726
Yeah. and it's the only one he can't do.

946
00:53:30.750 --> 00:53:33.016
You know what that means. don't ya?

947
00:53:33.040 --> 00:53:35.356
That even though
he's mastered other forms.

948
00:53:35.380 --> 00:53:36.896
he's still a weakling.

949
00:53:36.920 --> 00:53:38.316
Yep. exactly.

950
00:53:38.340 --> 00:53:40.986
The way he shows off. though?
He's got such an ego.

951
00:53:41.010 --> 00:53:43.576
[BOY 1] No way he becomes a Hashira.

952
00:53:43.600 --> 00:53:45.696
[BOY 2] Yeah. he'll die before then.

953
00:53:45.720 --> 00:53:46.826
[♪ gentle music playing]

954
00:53:46.850 --> 00:53:48.930
What did I do to deserve that?

955
00:53:50.390 --> 00:53:53.270
I heard you went and punched
someone from a higher rank.

956
00:53:53.730 --> 00:53:56.666
Don't go around making trouble.
you trash!

957
00:53:56.690 --> 00:54:00.240
It's embarrassing even being
seen in the same room as you.

958
00:54:02.780 --> 00:54:06.056
[ZENITSU] I was fully aware
that you hated me. Kaigaku.

959
00:54:06.080 --> 00:54:09.870
And to be perfectly honest.
I hated you. too.

960
00:54:11.000 --> 00:54:15.000
Even so. I couldn't help
but respect you as well.

961
00:54:15.500 --> 00:54:18.670
You never stopped
working towards your goals.

962
00:54:19.510 --> 00:54:21.566
Despite our differences.

963
00:54:21.590 --> 00:54:24.010
I looked up to you as an example.

964
00:54:24.510 --> 00:54:26.930
You really were a special guy.

965
00:54:28.520 --> 00:54:30.246
It wasn't just me.

966
00:54:30.270 --> 00:54:32.770
Gramps thought
you were remarkable. too.

967
00:54:33.770 --> 00:54:37.320
But I guess you weren't
satisfied with that. were you?

968
00:54:38.030 --> 00:54:39.716
No matter the day.

969
00:54:39.740 --> 00:54:43.796
the only sound that came
from you was discontent.

970
00:54:43.820 --> 00:54:45.046
[soft tinkling]

971
00:54:45.070 --> 00:54:48.056
It was like the box
where you kept your joy

972
00:54:48.080 --> 00:54:49.500
had a hole in it.

973
00:54:51.120 --> 00:54:53.710
And that joy kept leaking out.

974
00:54:55.130 --> 00:54:57.130
If the hole isn't mended.

975
00:54:57.590 --> 00:55:00.210
happiness will always be out of reach.

976
00:55:02.630 --> 00:55:05.800
Gramps. I'm sorry we're fighting...

977
00:55:06.760 --> 00:55:08.180
but he and I

978
00:55:08.810 --> 00:55:11.230
must walk separate paths.

979
00:55:17.360 --> 00:55:19.530
- [clangs]
- [crackling]

980
00:55:20.730 --> 00:55:21.900
[KAIGAKU] Huh?

981
00:55:22.450 --> 00:55:24.546
He's still holding on?

982
00:55:24.570 --> 00:55:25.676
[electricity crackling]

983
00:55:25.700 --> 00:55:28.370
[♪ synth music playing]

984
00:55:32.580 --> 00:55:33.806
[power surging]

985
00:55:33.830 --> 00:55:35.250
What the hell?

986
00:55:43.840 --> 00:55:45.010
[ZENITSU] Brother...

987
00:55:45.880 --> 00:55:48.100
- I'm sorry.
- [gasps]

988
00:55:48.680 --> 00:55:50.850
[♪ music intensifies]

989
00:56:06.950 --> 00:56:10.676
Thunder Breathing. Seventh Form:

990
00:56:10.700 --> 00:56:12.330
[roaring]

991
00:56:13.580 --> 00:56:15.830
God of Fire Thunder.

992
00:56:23.010 --> 00:56:24.510
[KAIGAKU] That...

993
00:56:24.840 --> 00:56:26.590
was so fast.

994
00:56:27.090 --> 00:56:29.470
That move. What was it?

995
00:56:29.850 --> 00:56:31.486
Unbelievable.

996
00:56:31.510 --> 00:56:34.390
How come I've never seen
that technique until now?

997
00:56:35.310 --> 00:56:37.956
Damn you. Damn you!

998
00:56:37.980 --> 00:56:41.166
I always knew that stupid geezer
liked you more than me!

999
00:56:41.190 --> 00:56:44.166
Why else would he only
teach you that technique?!

1000
00:56:44.190 --> 00:56:46.046
You're wrong.

1001
00:56:46.070 --> 00:56:47.176
[gasps]

1002
00:56:47.200 --> 00:56:48.200
[♪ gentle music playing]

1003
00:56:48.490 --> 00:56:50.620
[ZENITSU] Gramps was never
that kind of person.

1004
00:56:51.700 --> 00:56:54.330
This technique is something I made.

1005
00:56:54.950 --> 00:56:58.000
I created it all by myself.

1006
00:56:58.920 --> 00:57:00.210
My hope was...

1007
00:57:01.210 --> 00:57:06.260
that one day. I'd be able
to use it to fight by your side.

1008
00:57:09.720 --> 00:57:12.430
[KAIGAKU] How is this even possible?

1009
00:57:12.970 --> 00:57:15.656
Thunder Breathing
only has six techniques.

1010
00:57:15.680 --> 00:57:18.640
and yet he was able to create a seventh?

1011
00:57:19.400 --> 00:57:23.150
Him? The one who can only
use the First Form?

1012
00:57:24.440 --> 00:57:27.466
He's inferior to me in every way!

1013
00:57:27.490 --> 00:57:28.876
[groans angrily]

1014
00:57:28.900 --> 00:57:31.966
I can't accept it.
I won't accept it!

1015
00:57:31.990 --> 00:57:34.846
This must be some kind of twisted joke!

1016
00:57:34.870 --> 00:57:38.500
Someone like me losing to him?

1017
00:57:39.420 --> 00:57:42.040
I must be going insane!

1018
00:57:43.670 --> 00:57:44.840
Wait!

1019
00:57:45.750 --> 00:57:47.696
With his strength depleted.

1020
00:57:47.720 --> 00:57:50.106
I can still have the last laugh.

1021
00:57:50.130 --> 00:57:52.930
This fall will kill him
and he can't stop it.

1022
00:57:53.640 --> 00:57:57.746
I'll be taking him to hell
with me. [laughs maliciously]

1023
00:57:57.770 --> 00:57:59.536
[YUSHIRO]
Those who never give to others

1024
00:57:59.560 --> 00:58:01.996
are never able to receive in return.

1025
00:58:02.020 --> 00:58:03.150
Huh?

1026
00:58:03.860 --> 00:58:05.746
People who have nothing but desire

1027
00:58:05.770 --> 00:58:08.320
are no different than those
who have nothing at all.

1028
00:58:08.820 --> 00:58:12.200
And one cannot create anything
out of nothing.

1029
00:58:13.160 --> 00:58:16.030
Dying alone is pathetic.
wouldn't you say?

1030
00:58:22.210 --> 00:58:23.936
[screaming in anguish]

1031
00:58:23.960 --> 00:58:25.710
[fizzles out]

1032
00:58:34.220 --> 00:58:35.616
[gasps]

1033
00:58:35.640 --> 00:58:37.680
- [birds chirping]
- [leaves rustling]

1034
00:58:38.350 --> 00:58:39.456
Where am I?

1035
00:58:39.480 --> 00:58:41.600
- [stream trickling]
- [birds chirping]

1036
00:58:46.650 --> 00:58:47.956
[gasps]

1037
00:58:47.980 --> 00:58:49.400
Gramps!

1038
00:58:49.990 --> 00:58:52.126
[♪ tender music playing]

1039
00:58:52.150 --> 00:58:53.336
I'm sorry!

1040
00:58:53.360 --> 00:58:56.006
I... I couldn't get along with Kaigaku!

1041
00:58:56.030 --> 00:58:59.056
I even tried writing him letters. but...

1042
00:58:59.080 --> 00:59:01.766
But he never wrote me back.
And... [sobs]

1043
00:59:01.790 --> 00:59:03.226
if it weren't for me.

1044
00:59:03.250 --> 00:59:05.380
he might not have ended up
the way he did.

1045
00:59:05.830 --> 00:59:07.316
I'm really sorry!

1046
00:59:07.340 --> 00:59:08.606
Forgive me!

1047
00:59:08.630 --> 00:59:11.696
I wasn't able to pay you back
for everything!

1048
00:59:11.720 --> 00:59:14.776
I really wanted you
to see me as a Hashira.

1049
00:59:14.800 --> 00:59:16.616
to make you proud.

1050
00:59:16.640 --> 00:59:18.026
I'm sorry.

1051
00:59:18.050 --> 00:59:19.810
I failed you. Gramps!

1052
00:59:22.730 --> 00:59:25.770
[sobbing] I understand
if you hate me now.

1053
00:59:26.400 --> 00:59:29.086
Please. just say something.
Anything!

1054
00:59:29.110 --> 00:59:30.440
[effort grunting]

1055
00:59:30.980 --> 00:59:34.150
Damn it! What's this grabbing my leg?

1056
00:59:35.410 --> 00:59:37.466
Gramps! I just...

1057
00:59:37.490 --> 00:59:39.830
I need... [grunts]

1058
00:59:41.290 --> 00:59:42.476
Damn it!

1059
00:59:42.500 --> 00:59:44.556
[effort grunting]

1060
00:59:44.580 --> 00:59:46.096
[JIGORO] Zenitsu.

1061
00:59:46.120 --> 00:59:47.170
[Zenitsu gasps softly]

1062
00:59:53.670 --> 00:59:57.590
Listen to me. lad.
You are my pride and joy.

1063
01:00:16.070 --> 01:00:17.570
[♪ music fades]

1064
01:00:20.740 --> 01:00:23.176
[MURATA] Well? Can you save him?

1065
01:00:23.200 --> 01:00:24.976
He's someone that I know.

1066
01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:28.016
I can't watch him die.
Please tell me there's a way!

1067
01:00:28.040 --> 01:00:30.316
Keep your voice down.
You're not helping.

1068
01:00:30.340 --> 01:00:33.026
Just watch out for enemy ambushes.

1069
01:00:33.050 --> 01:00:35.446
At least then you'll actually be
doing something useful.

1070
01:00:35.470 --> 01:00:36.856
[grunting angrily]

1071
01:00:36.880 --> 01:00:39.826
Excuse me? And just
who the hell are you. huh?

1072
01:00:39.850 --> 01:00:42.446
I better not find out
you're a lower rank than I am!

1073
01:00:42.470 --> 01:00:46.100
I'm a demon. I don't care
about your hierarchy.

1074
01:00:46.890 --> 01:00:49.166
This'll slow the Blood Demon Art.

1075
01:00:49.190 --> 01:00:51.086
But if these cracks keep spreading.

1076
01:00:51.110 --> 01:00:53.570
it'll travel all the way to his eyes.

1077
01:00:54.280 --> 01:00:55.820
Hey. can you hear me?

1078
01:00:56.320 --> 01:00:57.530
[groans]

1079
01:00:58.240 --> 01:00:59.966
[all three exclaim]

1080
01:00:59.990 --> 01:01:02.766
Your bedside manner
really sucks. you know that?

1081
01:01:02.790 --> 01:01:04.516
I'm also using a hemostatic.

1082
01:01:04.540 --> 01:01:06.436
but I still can't get the bleeding to stop.

1083
01:01:06.460 --> 01:01:07.460
What did I say?!

1084
01:01:07.620 --> 01:01:09.806
Don't listen to him.
You're gonna be fine.

1085
01:01:09.830 --> 01:01:11.266
I swear you'll pull through this!

1086
01:01:11.290 --> 01:01:12.646
Yeah. you can do it!

1087
01:01:12.670 --> 01:01:14.686
Fight on! Fight on!

1088
01:01:14.710 --> 01:01:16.696
The only reason you're alive right now

1089
01:01:16.720 --> 01:01:18.276
is because the Upper Rank you fought

1090
01:01:18.300 --> 01:01:20.640
still hadn't mastered his own techniques.

1091
01:01:21.140 --> 01:01:23.100
That was lucky for you.

1092
01:01:23.640 --> 01:01:25.286
If you'd fought him a year from now.

1093
01:01:25.310 --> 01:01:27.140
you would have died instantly.

1094
01:01:27.810 --> 01:01:29.036
[Murata groaning]

1095
01:01:29.060 --> 01:01:30.916
Could you stop
with the doom and gloom?

1096
01:01:30.940 --> 01:01:33.036
Consider his feelings!

1097
01:01:33.060 --> 01:01:35.400
[breathing heavily]

1098
01:01:39.570 --> 01:01:42.740
Hey. don't pretend like
I'm the one in the wrong here.

1099
01:01:44.660 --> 01:01:46.386
What? What are you pointing at?

1100
01:01:46.410 --> 01:01:48.976
[YUSHIRO] Your screaming let
the demons know we're here.

1101
01:01:49.000 --> 01:01:50.936
[all screaming]

1102
01:01:50.960 --> 01:01:52.476
Don't say I didn't warn you.

1103
01:01:52.500 --> 01:01:53.936
[snarling]

1104
01:01:53.960 --> 01:01:57.840
Hey. it was Yushiro. right?
Take care of Agatsuma!

1105
01:01:58.380 --> 01:02:00.180
- Charge!
- [all grunting]

1106
01:02:01.970 --> 01:02:04.986
Murata. please take care of them
quickly. okay?

1107
01:02:05.010 --> 01:02:07.196
I'm gonna give you such an earful later!

1108
01:02:07.220 --> 01:02:09.480
- Damn.
- [demon snarling]

1109
01:02:10.190 --> 01:02:12.576
Water Breathing. Second Form:

1110
01:02:12.600 --> 01:02:15.690
Water Wheel! [yells]

1111
01:02:17.070 --> 01:02:18.546
We're gonna head them off.

1112
01:02:18.570 --> 01:02:20.176
Follow my lead. everyone!

1113
01:02:20.200 --> 01:02:22.426
[all yelling]

1114
01:02:22.450 --> 01:02:24.070
- [footsteps receding]
- [grunts]

1115
01:02:30.160 --> 01:02:32.330
[♪ foreboding music playing]

1116
01:02:37.090 --> 01:02:38.526
This is bad.

1117
01:02:38.550 --> 01:02:40.260
They're gonna run into "him."

1118
01:02:43.470 --> 01:02:45.760
[TANJIRO] We haven't encountered
any Upper Ranks.

1119
01:02:46.220 --> 01:02:48.696
Are we still that far from Muzan?

1120
01:02:48.720 --> 01:02:50.770
I hope the others are all right.

1121
01:02:53.980 --> 01:02:55.480
Miss Shinobu...

1122
01:02:56.310 --> 01:02:58.506
we're going to win this battle.

1123
01:02:58.530 --> 01:03:01.280
For you. For everyone!

1124
01:03:02.450 --> 01:03:04.046
- [loud crash]
- [gasps]

1125
01:03:04.070 --> 01:03:06.070
That jolt! What was that?

1126
01:03:06.580 --> 01:03:07.806
Mr. Giyu!

1127
01:03:07.830 --> 01:03:08.830
Stay there!

1128
01:03:09.240 --> 01:03:11.080
- Keep calm.
- [grunts]

1129
01:03:12.460 --> 01:03:14.436
[TANJIRO] Is someone else fighting?

1130
01:03:14.460 --> 01:03:16.606
Are we about to lose another comrade?

1131
01:03:16.630 --> 01:03:18.840
- [♪ intriguing music playing]
- [loud thuds]

1132
01:03:22.510 --> 01:03:25.486
No. it's something else.

1133
01:03:25.510 --> 01:03:27.050
And it's coming this way.

1134
01:03:28.060 --> 01:03:29.180
[sniffs]

1135
01:03:29.640 --> 01:03:32.060
This... This scent.

1136
01:03:40.690 --> 01:03:42.990
[GIYU] Above us!
Get back. Tanjiro!

1137
01:03:43.860 --> 01:03:44.990
[grunts]

1138
01:03:47.070 --> 01:03:49.080
[DEMON] Long time no see.

1139
01:03:50.700 --> 01:03:53.540
It's commendable you got this far.

1140
01:03:54.120 --> 01:03:56.646
Especially for a puny insect.

1141
01:03:56.670 --> 01:03:57.750
UPPER THREE

1142
01:03:58.250 --> 01:04:01.146
Don't you agree. Tanjiro?!

1143
01:04:01.170 --> 01:04:02.420
[Tanjiro seething]

1144
01:04:03.550 --> 01:04:06.300
Akaza!

1145
01:04:08.300 --> 01:04:10.470
[♪ low tense music playing]

1146
01:04:13.980 --> 01:04:15.520
[heavy burbling]

1147
01:04:31.990 --> 01:04:34.120
[breathing heavily]

1148
01:04:38.880 --> 01:04:41.646
[TAMAYO] This place...
If I had to guess.

1149
01:04:41.670 --> 01:04:43.816
this fleshy cocoon is breaking down

1150
01:04:43.840 --> 01:04:45.106
and disposing the drug

1151
01:04:45.130 --> 01:04:48.140
that's rescinding his demon form.

1152
01:04:48.760 --> 01:04:50.616
Muzan Kibutsuji.

1153
01:04:50.640 --> 01:04:55.310
I had sworn to destroy you
by any means necessary.

1154
01:04:55.890 --> 01:05:00.150
Yet. at this moment.
I am powerless to do so.

1155
01:05:00.860 --> 01:05:02.206
[loud thump]

1156
01:05:02.230 --> 01:05:03.900
[grunting]

1157
01:05:07.400 --> 01:05:11.370
Soon enough.
I'll be absorbed as well.

1158
01:05:12.160 --> 01:05:14.886
Please. someone. Anyone!

1159
01:05:14.910 --> 01:05:16.580
Come quickly!

1160
01:05:17.290 --> 01:05:18.920
I beg you!

1161
01:05:21.920 --> 01:05:24.050
[fight grunts]

1162
01:05:25.840 --> 01:05:28.010
[♪ intense music playing]

1163
01:05:33.220 --> 01:05:36.326
[KIRIYA] According to Father.
if Muzan should die.

1164
01:05:36.350 --> 01:05:38.810
the other demons will also perish.

1165
01:05:40.020 --> 01:05:43.980
By that logic. it's clear
that Muzan is still alive.

1166
01:05:45.270 --> 01:05:46.796
At this very moment.

1167
01:05:46.820 --> 01:05:49.740
Ms. Tamayo must be
suppressing his powers.

1168
01:05:50.660 --> 01:05:51.990
If she weren't.

1169
01:05:52.530 --> 01:05:55.450
he would surely be aware
of Yushiro's watchful gaze.

1170
01:05:56.490 --> 01:05:59.136
Before Muzan's powers
are fully restored.

1171
01:05:59.160 --> 01:06:02.540
we must do whatever it takes
to see that he's defeated.

1172
01:06:04.380 --> 01:06:05.816
I have to wonder. though.

1173
01:06:05.840 --> 01:06:09.260
inside of this infinite castle...

1174
01:06:10.220 --> 01:06:12.616
will we really be able to find him

1175
01:06:12.640 --> 01:06:14.390
and put an end to it all?

1176
01:06:19.730 --> 01:06:21.730
No need to be nervous.

1177
01:06:22.310 --> 01:06:24.690
You're doing a fine job. my child.

1178
01:06:26.650 --> 01:06:29.860
Muzan will surely reveal himself
once more.

1179
01:06:30.570 --> 01:06:33.070
just as he did when he found me.

1180
01:06:35.280 --> 01:06:40.000
When it comes to this man.
that's simply his nature.

1181
01:06:40.750 --> 01:06:42.080
[gasps]

1182
01:06:45.540 --> 01:06:47.340
[KIRIYA] I understand. Father.

1183
01:06:48.050 --> 01:06:50.720
I will see to it our plan succeeds.

1184
01:06:52.130 --> 01:06:54.776
We must find him before
the Corps members' strength

1185
01:06:54.800 --> 01:06:55.986
is fully depleted.

1186
01:06:56.010 --> 01:06:58.390
and settle this once and for all.

1187
01:06:58.770 --> 01:06:59.930
[Gyomei grunts]

1188
01:07:04.480 --> 01:07:05.610
[distorted grunting]

1189
01:07:08.780 --> 01:07:10.966
- [grunting]
- [KAKUSHI 1] Protect them!

1190
01:07:10.990 --> 01:07:12.466
[KAKUSHI 2] Everybody. group up!

1191
01:07:12.490 --> 01:07:13.886
We have to form a wall!

1192
01:07:13.910 --> 01:07:15.926
Get their attention off the Hashira!

1193
01:07:15.950 --> 01:07:18.370
Please. sir!
Go on ahead without us!

1194
01:07:18.910 --> 01:07:20.976
You as well! We got this!

1195
01:07:21.000 --> 01:07:22.290
Are you certain?

1196
01:07:22.910 --> 01:07:25.290
- [both grunting]
- [groans]

1197
01:07:26.880 --> 01:07:28.170
[thuds]

1198
01:07:30.630 --> 01:07:33.356
We are! Just defeat Kibutsuji!

1199
01:07:33.380 --> 01:07:34.720
Please. sir!

1200
01:07:35.300 --> 01:07:36.736
Very well. then.

1201
01:07:36.760 --> 01:07:39.576
I will put my faith in your efforts here.

1202
01:07:39.600 --> 01:07:40.770
Tokito!

1203
01:07:42.430 --> 01:07:43.690
[KAKUSHI 1] All right!

1204
01:07:43.810 --> 01:07:46.706
Let's show them the fruits
of our Hashira training!

1205
01:07:46.730 --> 01:07:48.036
[ALL] Right!

1206
01:07:48.060 --> 01:07:50.190
[♪ epic cinematic music playing]

1207
01:07:51.650 --> 01:07:53.820
[fight grunts]

1208
01:07:55.160 --> 01:07:57.490
[KIRIYA] Everyone. thank you.

1209
01:07:57.990 --> 01:08:01.160
I know Father would be proud
to see you giving it your all.

1210
01:08:06.790 --> 01:08:08.960
[♪ melancholic music playing]

1211
01:08:11.630 --> 01:08:13.880
- [whimpering]
- [KIRIYA] Stop that!

1212
01:08:14.590 --> 01:08:16.510
You must keep your hands moving.

1213
01:08:17.090 --> 01:08:19.300
Right now. we need to focus.

1214
01:08:21.060 --> 01:08:22.180
[KANATA] Yes.

1215
01:08:25.430 --> 01:08:28.690
Master Kiriya is quite impressive.

1216
01:08:29.810 --> 01:08:31.586
It's clear he's still in mourning

1217
01:08:31.610 --> 01:08:33.416
over the loss of the Master.

1218
01:08:33.440 --> 01:08:35.650
yet his duty is unwavering.

1219
01:08:36.320 --> 01:08:39.700
He's led the Demon Slayer Corps
rather splendidly.

1220
01:08:41.160 --> 01:08:44.040
Wouldn't you agree. Mr. Rengoku?

1221
01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:46.620
I would. indeed.

1222
01:08:48.000 --> 01:08:50.766
These children are still young in years.

1223
01:08:50.790 --> 01:08:53.920
but their resolve is anything but childish.

1224
01:08:55.090 --> 01:08:57.130
I swear to protect them.

1225
01:08:57.680 --> 01:09:00.140
Just as Kyojuro did before me.

1226
01:09:00.640 --> 01:09:03.180
I will risk my own life to do so.

1227
01:09:07.480 --> 01:09:09.850
[Nezuko whimpers in pain]

1228
01:09:16.490 --> 01:09:19.530
[SAKONJI] I didn't think
she would suffer this much.

1229
01:09:20.620 --> 01:09:24.096
The Master was working
with a demon named Tamayo

1230
01:09:24.120 --> 01:09:26.596
who delivered this antidote.

1231
01:09:26.620 --> 01:09:29.620
I've administered it as she instructed.

1232
01:09:30.880 --> 01:09:32.396
Even so.

1233
01:09:32.420 --> 01:09:36.760
will Nezuko be able to turn
back into a human. I wonder?

1234
01:09:37.260 --> 01:09:40.486
If Nezuko does become human again.

1235
01:09:40.510 --> 01:09:43.866
Muzan's grand scheme will collapse.

1236
01:09:43.890 --> 01:09:45.366
His thousand-year quest

1237
01:09:45.390 --> 01:09:47.956
for a vessel which can resist the sun

1238
01:09:47.980 --> 01:09:49.600
will be no more.

1239
01:09:50.100 --> 01:09:52.956
And all of the progress he's made

1240
01:09:52.980 --> 01:09:55.610
will be wound back like a clock.

1241
01:09:57.150 --> 01:10:01.176
In the many years that we've had
to endure this nightmare.

1242
01:10:01.200 --> 01:10:03.256
Nezuko is the only demon

1243
01:10:03.280 --> 01:10:06.176
who has been able to live in the sunlight.

1244
01:10:06.200 --> 01:10:08.370
[♪ melancholic music playing]

1245
01:10:11.460 --> 01:10:13.580
[heart beating]

1246
01:10:14.880 --> 01:10:16.380
[inhales deeply]

1247
01:10:17.630 --> 01:10:19.090
[sighs wearily]

1248
01:10:21.880 --> 01:10:23.946
"The final battle."

1249
01:10:23.970 --> 01:10:27.140
These words echo in my mind.

1250
01:10:28.980 --> 01:10:30.270
[gulps. sighs]

1251
01:10:30.810 --> 01:10:32.576
And each time they do.

1252
01:10:32.600 --> 01:10:35.980
I can't help but tremble
as my heart beats louder.

1253
01:10:36.980 --> 01:10:41.360
This battle may finally
reach its conclusion tonight.

1254
01:10:42.240 --> 01:10:46.910
I never dreamed that I'd be
alive to witness it myself.

1255
01:10:48.120 --> 01:10:49.596
Tanjiro.

1256
01:10:49.620 --> 01:10:52.096
I sometimes think back to the day

1257
01:10:52.120 --> 01:10:54.920
when you brought
your demon sister to me.

1258
01:10:55.340 --> 01:10:57.226
Ever since then.

1259
01:10:57.250 --> 01:11:01.670
it feels like a giant wheel
of fate has been slowly turning.

1260
01:11:02.760 --> 01:11:06.776
Perhaps it would be best to
compare the sum of our battles

1261
01:11:06.800 --> 01:11:09.616
to a giant dormant machine.

1262
01:11:09.640 --> 01:11:13.746
You and Nezuko are the small
cogs that have joined together

1263
01:11:13.770 --> 01:11:15.730
and awoken it from its slumber.

1264
01:11:16.310 --> 01:11:21.296
What was once frozen in place
has now been set into motion.

1265
01:11:21.320 --> 01:11:23.490
[♪ intriguing music playing]

1266
01:11:23.990 --> 01:11:27.280
- [moaning]
- Don't give up. Nezuko.

1267
01:11:28.780 --> 01:11:31.370
Keep up the fight. Tanjiro.

1268
01:11:32.080 --> 01:11:35.250
You both have to pull through.
no matter what!

1269
01:11:35.790 --> 01:11:37.460
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1270
01:11:38.000 --> 01:11:39.066
Fire Wheel!

1271
01:11:39.090 --> 01:11:41.210
[♪ epic dramatic music playing]

1272
01:11:41.760 --> 01:11:43.170
Go through!

1273
01:11:43.300 --> 01:11:46.116
If I can't even sever his arm.
I'll never sever his head!

1274
01:11:46.140 --> 01:11:48.350
[yelling]

1275
01:11:49.140 --> 01:11:50.390
[flesh squelches]

1276
01:11:50.850 --> 01:11:52.366
[blood splatters]

1277
01:11:52.390 --> 01:11:53.367
DESTROY

1278
01:11:53.391 --> 01:11:54.520
I got one.

1279
01:11:54.690 --> 01:11:56.626
I was able to dodge his attack. too.

1280
01:11:56.650 --> 01:11:58.020
I can do this!

1281
01:11:58.520 --> 01:12:00.166
I couldn't aim for his head.

1282
01:12:00.190 --> 01:12:01.730
but this time. for sure!

1283
01:12:02.860 --> 01:12:05.386
Hinokami Kagura: Fake Rainbow!

1284
01:12:05.410 --> 01:12:06.450
[fizzles out]

1285
01:12:08.700 --> 01:12:10.540
[high-pitched ringing]

1286
01:12:12.660 --> 01:12:14.620
- [panting]
- [sword clatters]

1287
01:12:16.120 --> 01:12:18.106
[flesh squelching]

1288
01:12:18.130 --> 01:12:19.590
Huh?

1289
01:12:21.050 --> 01:12:22.260
[GIYU] Tanjiro.

1290
01:12:22.760 --> 01:12:25.260
You've really sharpened
your skills. haven't you?

1291
01:12:26.180 --> 01:12:27.946
It wouldn't be an exaggeration

1292
01:12:27.970 --> 01:12:30.680
to say he's at the level of a Hashira now.

1293
01:12:31.890 --> 01:12:36.076
To think that he'd do this well
against Upper Three.

1294
01:12:36.100 --> 01:12:38.270
[♪ enchanting folk music playing]

1295
01:12:41.360 --> 01:12:42.610
That day...

1296
01:12:43.570 --> 01:12:46.360
I remember a boy
who felt completely helpless

1297
01:12:46.820 --> 01:12:49.070
as he collapsed onto the cold snow.

1298
01:12:49.570 --> 01:12:52.370
begging through
tears for his sister's life.

1299
01:13:00.170 --> 01:13:02.300
But you are helpless no longer.

1300
01:13:02.800 --> 01:13:05.630
You have the strength
to fight not only for your life.

1301
01:13:06.130 --> 01:13:08.430
but also for what's precious to you.

1302
01:13:10.090 --> 01:13:12.656
[AKAZA] "This boy is not weak.

1303
01:13:12.680 --> 01:13:14.430
Don't insult him."

1304
01:13:15.220 --> 01:13:18.730
I must admit that Kyojuro
was right when he said that.

1305
01:13:19.230 --> 01:13:22.166
You are certainly not weak.

1306
01:13:22.190 --> 01:13:24.900
In fact. I commend you.

1307
01:13:27.650 --> 01:13:30.086
Technique Development...

1308
01:13:30.110 --> 01:13:32.280
[♪ intense rock music playing]

1309
01:13:34.240 --> 01:13:37.580
Now. let's kick things off.
shall we?

1310
01:13:38.210 --> 01:13:40.330
It's time we had some fun.

1311
01:13:45.920 --> 01:13:47.970
- [rumbling]
- [heavy creaking]

1312
01:14:08.780 --> 01:14:10.030
[exhales sharply]

1313
01:14:16.370 --> 01:14:17.950
[grunts]

1314
01:14:26.710 --> 01:14:29.776
[GIYU] Water Breathing. Third Form:

1315
01:14:29.800 --> 01:14:31.380
Flowing Dance!

1316
01:14:32.300 --> 01:14:34.276
You're a Water Hashira.

1317
01:14:34.300 --> 01:14:36.156
How lucky for me!

1318
01:14:36.180 --> 01:14:38.930
It's been 50 years since I fought one.

1319
01:14:43.190 --> 01:14:44.810
[debris clattering]

1320
01:14:46.690 --> 01:14:50.360
Destructive Death: Disorder!

1321
01:14:52.150 --> 01:14:54.870
Water Breathing. Eleventh Form:

1322
01:14:55.620 --> 01:14:57.030
Dead Calm.

1323
01:15:01.960 --> 01:15:04.670
[AKAZA] I've never seen
that move before.

1324
01:15:05.210 --> 01:15:07.436
Perhaps the last Water Hashira I killed

1325
01:15:07.460 --> 01:15:09.606
never had a chance to use it!

1326
01:15:09.630 --> 01:15:12.800
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:
Raging Sun!

1327
01:15:14.970 --> 01:15:16.260
He vanished!

1328
01:15:17.010 --> 01:15:18.236
Behind me!

1329
01:15:18.260 --> 01:15:19.810
Fake Rain Kagura!

1330
01:15:21.140 --> 01:15:25.480
[GIYU] Water Breathing.
Second Form: Water Wheel.

1331
01:15:28.940 --> 01:15:29.980
[yells]

1332
01:15:37.870 --> 01:15:39.910
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1333
01:15:41.040 --> 01:15:42.120
Flame Dance!

1334
01:15:42.500 --> 01:15:46.250
[AKAZA] Destructive Death.
Leg Type: Crown Splitter!

1335
01:15:46.920 --> 01:15:49.460
[TANJIRO] I blocked it with my sword.

1336
01:15:53.760 --> 01:15:55.946
His move barely grazed me

1337
01:15:55.970 --> 01:15:58.220
and still did this kind of damage?

1338
01:16:02.600 --> 01:16:04.440
[AKAZA] How marvelous!

1339
01:16:05.770 --> 01:16:09.546
That elegant sword skill
you're using is magnificent!

1340
01:16:09.570 --> 01:16:12.416
I must know now.
What is your name?

1341
01:16:12.440 --> 01:16:14.280
I want to remember you!

1342
01:16:16.360 --> 01:16:19.426
I don't have a name
to give to a demon like you.

1343
01:16:19.450 --> 01:16:22.330
I hate talking. so don't speak to me!

1344
01:16:23.120 --> 01:16:24.516
Is that so?

1345
01:16:24.540 --> 01:16:27.266
You're not much for small talk. are you?

1346
01:16:27.290 --> 01:16:31.500
Well. I happen to quite
enjoy it. so I'll ask you again.

1347
01:16:32.090 --> 01:16:33.606
What is your name?

1348
01:16:33.630 --> 01:16:35.760
[grunting]

1349
01:16:36.970 --> 01:16:39.050
- [impact grunts]
- [crumbles]

1350
01:16:39.890 --> 01:16:43.116
[AKAZA] Destructive Death. Leg Type:

1351
01:16:43.140 --> 01:16:45.390
Explosive Flurry!

1352
01:16:49.150 --> 01:16:51.520
[yelling]

1353
01:16:57.070 --> 01:16:59.490
- [impact grunts]
- [TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu!

1354
01:17:01.030 --> 01:17:03.676
I see. That's his name.

1355
01:17:03.700 --> 01:17:05.540
Thank you for letting me know.

1356
01:17:09.040 --> 01:17:10.686
Hinokami Kagura!

1357
01:17:10.710 --> 01:17:13.816
Destructive Death:
Eight-Layered Demon Core!

1358
01:17:13.840 --> 01:17:16.130
Burning Bones. Summer Sun!

1359
01:17:22.680 --> 01:17:24.520
[panting]

1360
01:17:31.060 --> 01:17:32.956
[AKAZA] Excellent form!

1361
01:17:32.980 --> 01:17:36.916
To improve this much in such
a short time is impressive.

1362
01:17:36.940 --> 01:17:39.006
I'll give you my praise.

1363
01:17:39.030 --> 01:17:40.796
It seems obvious to me

1364
01:17:40.820 --> 01:17:43.766
that Kyojuro must have
really inspired you.

1365
01:17:43.790 --> 01:17:48.096
The night we met. you were
merely a weak. mournful child.

1366
01:17:48.120 --> 01:17:49.766
crumpled on the ground.

1367
01:17:49.790 --> 01:17:52.226
Not even worthy of being killed.

1368
01:17:52.250 --> 01:17:54.316
- But just look at you now!
- [cracking]

1369
01:17:54.340 --> 01:17:58.446
This leap in your abilities.
it's like you've been reborn!

1370
01:17:58.470 --> 01:18:00.776
My heart won't stop racing.

1371
01:18:00.800 --> 01:18:03.156
I'm truly overjoyed!

1372
01:18:03.180 --> 01:18:04.930
[snickers]

1373
01:18:05.680 --> 01:18:09.560
The night Kyojuro died.
I was glad that it happened.

1374
01:18:10.690 --> 01:18:11.690
[exclaims in disbelief]

1375
01:18:12.190 --> 01:18:13.666
How tragic would it have been

1376
01:18:13.690 --> 01:18:15.860
if he had never gotten any stronger.

1377
01:18:16.530 --> 01:18:18.716
Such a stubborn man. not letting go

1378
01:18:18.740 --> 01:18:21.820
of those worthless values
of staying human.

1379
01:18:23.070 --> 01:18:24.830
How dare you!

1380
01:18:31.960 --> 01:18:34.920
Shut up! Just shut up!

1381
01:18:38.710 --> 01:18:41.760
Don't you dare even speak his name!

1382
01:18:42.840 --> 01:18:44.156
[AKAZA] What's the matter?

1383
01:18:44.180 --> 01:18:46.696
I'm only paying the man a compliment.

1384
01:18:46.720 --> 01:18:48.536
I'm being sincere.

1385
01:18:48.560 --> 01:18:50.496
These are high words of praise.

1386
01:18:50.520 --> 01:18:51.666
[TANJIRO] You're wrong.

1387
01:18:51.690 --> 01:18:53.956
All you're doing is insulting him!

1388
01:18:53.980 --> 01:18:56.546
You're just spitting on his memory!

1389
01:18:56.570 --> 01:18:58.190
On all of us!

1390
01:18:59.190 --> 01:19:01.926
You couldn't be more wrong. Tanjiro.

1391
01:19:01.950 --> 01:19:06.620
As you'll recall. the only thing
I despise is weak human beings.

1392
01:19:07.120 --> 01:19:10.056
Only a feeble weakling
is deserving of my scorn

1393
01:19:10.080 --> 01:19:11.370
and no one else.

1394
01:19:12.370 --> 01:19:14.056
That's right.

1395
01:19:14.080 --> 01:19:17.316
The mere sight of them
makes my skin crawl.

1396
01:19:17.340 --> 01:19:19.090
They make me retch!

1397
01:19:20.090 --> 01:19:22.356
Through the laws of nature.
they are weeded out

1398
01:19:22.380 --> 01:19:24.760
from this world just as they should be.

1399
01:19:25.680 --> 01:19:28.810
Everything you just said is wrong!

1400
01:19:29.810 --> 01:19:30.980
[AKAZA] Huh?

1401
01:19:32.230 --> 01:19:34.496
The fact you're even alive right now.

1402
01:19:34.520 --> 01:19:36.230
isn't that proof enough?

1403
01:19:37.570 --> 01:19:40.716
As an infant.
we're all helpless.

1404
01:19:40.740 --> 01:19:43.240
We can't live
without someone else's help.

1405
01:19:43.740 --> 01:19:45.780
You're no different. Akaza.

1406
01:19:46.780 --> 01:19:48.756
Even if you don't remember.

1407
01:19:48.780 --> 01:19:50.676
there was a time
when you were protected

1408
01:19:50.700 --> 01:19:52.306
and cared for by someone.

1409
01:19:52.330 --> 01:19:53.500
I know it!

1410
01:19:54.040 --> 01:19:55.670
That's why you're alive.

1411
01:20:00.500 --> 01:20:03.260
The strong should aid
and protect the weak.

1412
01:20:03.760 --> 01:20:05.946
And in turn.
the weak become strong

1413
01:20:05.970 --> 01:20:09.140
and aid and protect
those weaker than themselves!

1414
01:20:09.680 --> 01:20:11.810
That is the law of nature.

1415
01:20:12.350 --> 01:20:16.060
Akaza. I can't tolerate
your way of thinking.

1416
01:20:16.520 --> 01:20:18.126
Here on out.

1417
01:20:18.150 --> 01:20:20.650
I won't let you do as you please!

1418
01:20:25.650 --> 01:20:27.160
[AKAZA] I get it now.

1419
01:20:29.990 --> 01:20:34.330
I have a disgust for this boy
that's almost primal in nature.

1420
01:20:35.040 --> 01:20:38.790
Even if he's stronger.
that feeling hasn't faded.

1421
01:20:43.590 --> 01:20:45.696
[MAN] No matter who they are.

1422
01:20:45.720 --> 01:20:48.736
everyone begins life as a newborn.

1423
01:20:48.760 --> 01:20:52.260
We learn by getting help
from those around us.

1424
01:20:52.930 --> 01:20:55.706
We are not competing with others.

1425
01:20:55.730 --> 01:20:59.400
The only opponent
you have in life is yourself.

1426
01:21:00.020 --> 01:21:04.070
Just focus on becoming stronger
than you were yesterday.

1427
01:21:05.240 --> 01:21:08.886
If you can stay this path
for a decade or even two.

1428
01:21:08.910 --> 01:21:10.490
that would be commendable.

1429
01:21:10.990 --> 01:21:12.466
And before you know it.

1430
01:21:12.490 --> 01:21:15.330
you will be helping others in turn.

1431
01:21:16.000 --> 01:21:18.000
[breathing shakily]

1432
01:21:21.500 --> 01:21:22.540
[gasps]

1433
01:21:23.340 --> 01:21:24.340
[TANJIRO] What was that?

1434
01:21:24.460 --> 01:21:26.210
He just swung his fist at nothing.

1435
01:21:32.390 --> 01:21:34.180
Tanjiro.

1436
01:21:35.060 --> 01:21:37.666
You still repulse me to my core.

1437
01:21:37.690 --> 01:21:38.746
[♪ rock music playing]

1438
01:21:38.770 --> 01:21:41.416
Destructive Death.
Crushing Type:

1439
01:21:41.440 --> 01:21:43.820
Ten Thousand Leaves Flashing Willow!

1440
01:21:46.940 --> 01:21:48.926
[TANJIRO] This speed. it's blinding!

1441
01:21:48.950 --> 01:21:51.636
No. it's not just his speed.

1442
01:21:51.660 --> 01:21:54.950
It's his precision.
his aura. and also...

1443
01:21:57.750 --> 01:21:58.790
[grunts]

1444
01:21:59.870 --> 01:22:02.186
Destructive Death. Leg Type.

1445
01:22:02.210 --> 01:22:03.210
[TANJIRO] Below.

1446
01:22:05.380 --> 01:22:07.590
[AKAZA] Flying Planet
Thousand Wheels!

1447
01:22:13.510 --> 01:22:15.996
[TANJIRO] Even if I could
anticipate his strikes.

1448
01:22:16.020 --> 01:22:19.116
they're so powerful.
I can't completely deflect them.

1449
01:22:19.140 --> 01:22:21.286
His techniques are so precise.

1450
01:22:21.310 --> 01:22:24.610
they can pierce through any
opening. no matter how small.

1451
01:22:27.480 --> 01:22:29.966
It's like a magnet is
attracting his attacks

1452
01:22:29.990 --> 01:22:31.966
straight toward my weak points.

1453
01:22:31.990 --> 01:22:35.056
But how? What's happening?

1454
01:22:35.080 --> 01:22:37.450
What could be causing this behavior?

1455
01:22:37.870 --> 01:22:40.000
Come on. Think.

1456
01:22:41.290 --> 01:22:42.976
What's the answer?!

1457
01:22:43.000 --> 01:22:46.396
There must be a clue
in what Akaza's said or done.

1458
01:22:46.420 --> 01:22:48.670
[Akaza grunts] Hyah!

1459
01:22:49.720 --> 01:22:53.180
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:
Solar Heat Haze!

1460
01:23:00.940 --> 01:23:02.390
[blood spurts]

1461
01:23:02.940 --> 01:23:05.706
[chuckles]
What an interesting move.

1462
01:23:05.730 --> 01:23:09.456
I dodged it at first. but then
the blade seemed to extend.

1463
01:23:09.480 --> 01:23:12.006
I don't know what kind of swing
you put behind it.

1464
01:23:12.030 --> 01:23:13.716
but the tip of your blade wavered

1465
01:23:13.740 --> 01:23:16.990
like it was in a heat haze.
How fascinating!

1466
01:23:20.290 --> 01:23:22.290
- [grunts]
- [glass shattering]

1467
01:23:23.750 --> 01:23:25.880
[debris crumbling]

1468
01:23:27.670 --> 01:23:31.170
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1469
01:23:31.970 --> 01:23:33.276
[clangs]

1470
01:23:33.300 --> 01:23:34.510
My sword!

1471
01:23:35.510 --> 01:23:36.890
He'll break it!

1472
01:23:38.060 --> 01:23:40.430
[effort grunts]

1473
01:23:41.730 --> 01:23:43.520
That was a strong headbutt.

1474
01:23:45.190 --> 01:23:47.360
[TANJIRO] Damn you!
Let go of me!

1475
01:23:48.690 --> 01:23:50.256
No good. [straining]

1476
01:23:50.280 --> 01:23:52.440
I can't get him to loosen his grip.

1477
01:23:56.620 --> 01:23:58.280
[water splashing]

1478
01:24:03.290 --> 01:24:04.476
[grunts softly]

1479
01:24:04.500 --> 01:24:06.000
Mr. Giyu!

1480
01:24:06.500 --> 01:24:08.380
[Giyu sighs]

1481
01:24:09.750 --> 01:24:12.356
You're starting to get on my nerves.

1482
01:24:12.380 --> 01:24:15.220
Thanks to you.
my back is killing me now.

1483
01:24:15.760 --> 01:24:18.946
I'm not fond of being hurled
like a rag doll.

1484
01:24:18.970 --> 01:24:20.850
I'm gonna make you pay.

1485
01:24:21.680 --> 01:24:23.270
♪

1486
01:24:23.890 --> 01:24:27.900
Personally. I'd rather not draw
my sword if I can help it.

1487
01:24:28.400 --> 01:24:31.296
And I have a hard time
justifying using deadly force

1488
01:24:31.320 --> 01:24:32.690
if unnecessary.

1489
01:24:33.940 --> 01:24:35.796
But at this moment.

1490
01:24:35.820 --> 01:24:39.306
I'm against an opponent that
demands everything from me.

1491
01:24:39.330 --> 01:24:40.886
In the short time we fought.

1492
01:24:40.910 --> 01:24:43.500
my senses have been
pushed past their limits.

1493
01:24:44.540 --> 01:24:47.346
My dormant senses
have been rudely awakened

1494
01:24:47.370 --> 01:24:50.590
and are dragging me forward
towards the enemy.

1495
01:24:51.420 --> 01:24:55.066
I now know how much
it expands one's potential

1496
01:24:55.090 --> 01:24:57.156
to have one's back against the wall

1497
01:24:57.180 --> 01:24:58.946
with their sword raised

1498
01:24:58.970 --> 01:25:00.720
in the face of death.

1499
01:25:03.970 --> 01:25:05.180
Mr. Giyu.

1500
01:25:11.070 --> 01:25:12.650
[♪ intense music playing]

1501
01:25:22.240 --> 01:25:25.136
[AKAZA] A mark appeared
and his movements have gotten...

1502
01:25:25.160 --> 01:25:26.540
Faster!

1503
01:25:31.090 --> 01:25:34.590
[GIYU] Water Breathing.
Fourth Form: Striking Tide!

1504
01:25:35.590 --> 01:25:37.470
[grunts softly. chuckles]

1505
01:25:42.430 --> 01:25:43.560
[grunts]

1506
01:25:48.940 --> 01:25:50.626
[TANJIRO] They're both so fast.

1507
01:25:50.650 --> 01:25:53.336
Mr. Giyu's speed increased
with the mark.

1508
01:25:53.360 --> 01:25:55.570
but Akaza adapted to it instantly.

1509
01:25:58.030 --> 01:26:00.586
Don't tell me that's all you're capable of!

1510
01:26:00.610 --> 01:26:02.700
[Giyu groans angrily]

1511
01:26:04.660 --> 01:26:07.040
[both grunting]

1512
01:26:09.620 --> 01:26:13.420
Show me more!
Don't you dare hold back!

1513
01:26:42.240 --> 01:26:45.870
[GIYU] Tenth Form: Constant Flux!

1514
01:26:53.380 --> 01:26:54.960
[yelling]

1515
01:27:02.930 --> 01:27:06.326
Seventh Form: Drop Ripple Thrust!

1516
01:27:06.350 --> 01:27:09.100
Destructive Death: Disorder!

1517
01:27:19.730 --> 01:27:22.450
[TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu! Akaza!

1518
01:27:24.660 --> 01:27:26.070
Calm down!

1519
01:27:26.870 --> 01:27:28.910
[weapons clanging]

1520
01:27:29.950 --> 01:27:32.266
Think. Don't panic.

1521
01:27:32.290 --> 01:27:34.710
Whatever you do.
don't lose focus.

1522
01:27:35.330 --> 01:27:36.580
[grunts]

1523
01:27:36.790 --> 01:27:40.050
Why is it that Akaza's attacks
are always so accurate?

1524
01:27:40.960 --> 01:27:45.010
How is he able to respond
to attacks from his blind spots?

1525
01:27:45.890 --> 01:27:47.100
Think!

1526
01:27:51.640 --> 01:27:53.746
[AKAZA] Your fighting spirit
has been tempered

1527
01:27:53.770 --> 01:27:55.456
like quality steel.

1528
01:27:55.480 --> 01:27:56.940
Your name?

1529
01:27:57.610 --> 01:27:58.820
[gasps]

1530
01:27:59.820 --> 01:28:02.006
[TANJIRO]
Back when he fought Mr. Rengoku.

1531
01:28:02.030 --> 01:28:05.700
I remember Akaza using the words
"fighting spirit."

1532
01:28:07.070 --> 01:28:09.006
What did he mean by that?

1533
01:28:09.030 --> 01:28:11.910
Is he able to sense things
through fighting spirit?

1534
01:28:12.450 --> 01:28:15.210
The same way I can sense things
through scent?

1535
01:28:29.300 --> 01:28:31.536
Wherever the enemy's aiming at.

1536
01:28:31.560 --> 01:28:33.746
I get this weird tingling feeling.

1537
01:28:33.770 --> 01:28:37.326
So. that's how you knew Gyutaro
was attacking you from behind.

1538
01:28:37.350 --> 01:28:39.546
You sure are incredible. Inosuke.

1539
01:28:39.570 --> 01:28:41.416
[laughs boisterously]

1540
01:28:41.440 --> 01:28:44.506
Well. my skin is tougher
than most people's.

1541
01:28:44.530 --> 01:28:46.386
And whether it's from behind or not.

1542
01:28:46.410 --> 01:28:47.586
if someone's looking at me.

1543
01:28:47.610 --> 01:28:49.386
I know just where they're lookin'.

1544
01:28:49.410 --> 01:28:50.966
Could you show me?

1545
01:28:50.990 --> 01:28:53.450
[laughs] Sure thing!

1546
01:28:54.200 --> 01:28:55.750
[determined grunt]

1547
01:28:58.290 --> 01:29:00.016
- It's my right shoulder.
- [gasps]

1548
01:29:00.040 --> 01:29:01.840
You really got it.
That's amazing!

1549
01:29:02.380 --> 01:29:04.816
It's even easier to know
someone's looking at me

1550
01:29:04.840 --> 01:29:06.406
if they had killing intent.

1551
01:29:06.430 --> 01:29:09.866
Since anyone who can harm me
is bad news.

1552
01:29:09.890 --> 01:29:12.616
killing intent kind of
feels like it's stabbing me

1553
01:29:12.640 --> 01:29:14.100
through the skin. you know?

1554
01:29:15.020 --> 01:29:16.286
[TANJIRO] That's right.

1555
01:29:16.310 --> 01:29:18.996
Inosuke was able to sense the invisible

1556
01:29:19.020 --> 01:29:21.690
using only his honed sense of touch.

1557
01:29:22.400 --> 01:29:25.740
Think back.
What else did we talk about...

1558
01:29:26.450 --> 01:29:27.626
that day?

1559
01:29:27.650 --> 01:29:29.636
Where things get real tricky

1560
01:29:29.660 --> 01:29:32.676
is when someone who doesn't have
killing intent or hostility

1561
01:29:32.700 --> 01:29:33.926
is looking at me.

1562
01:29:33.950 --> 01:29:36.250
- like that tiny hag!
- Huh?

1563
01:29:36.830 --> 01:29:37.936
[INOSUKE] That old hag

1564
01:29:37.960 --> 01:29:39.936
from the house with the wisteria mark

1565
01:29:39.960 --> 01:29:41.266
was sneaky.

1566
01:29:41.290 --> 01:29:42.936
Before I knew it...

1567
01:29:42.960 --> 01:29:44.090
Huh?

1568
01:29:45.550 --> 01:29:48.930
She'd be sitting right
behind me holding rice balls.

1569
01:29:49.640 --> 01:29:52.736
Calling her a "hag" isn't nice.
She's elderly.

1570
01:29:52.760 --> 01:29:54.866
- Elderly hag!
- Stop that!

1571
01:29:54.890 --> 01:29:56.866
Well. that got me thinkin'.

1572
01:29:56.890 --> 01:30:00.496
If I could hide my killing
intent. then I'd be a ninja.

1573
01:30:00.520 --> 01:30:02.836
I'd be able to sneak up on anybody.

1574
01:30:02.860 --> 01:30:04.956
- [chuckles excitedly]
- Sure.

1575
01:30:04.980 --> 01:30:07.666
But. Inosuke. she was only sneaky

1576
01:30:07.690 --> 01:30:10.386
'cause she didn't have
the intent of harming you.

1577
01:30:10.410 --> 01:30:13.136
And I think beheading a demon
without killing intent

1578
01:30:13.160 --> 01:30:14.490
would be impossible.

1579
01:30:15.120 --> 01:30:16.500
[INOSUKE] Hmm.

1580
01:30:17.040 --> 01:30:19.056
Yeah. you're probably right.

1581
01:30:19.080 --> 01:30:22.056
A half-hearted strike
without any killing intent

1582
01:30:22.080 --> 01:30:25.630
would never be strong enough
to cut through a demon's neck.

1583
01:30:26.550 --> 01:30:28.776
[TANJIRO] It was a casual conversation

1584
01:30:28.800 --> 01:30:31.430
but I think Inosuke was on to something.

1585
01:30:33.640 --> 01:30:36.576
What is it that
Akaza supposedly senses?

1586
01:30:36.600 --> 01:30:39.036
What does he mean by "fighting spirit"?

1587
01:30:39.060 --> 01:30:40.866
Is it killing intent?

1588
01:30:40.890 --> 01:30:42.416
Is it the will to fight?

1589
01:30:42.440 --> 01:30:44.086
The time spent training?

1590
01:30:44.110 --> 01:30:45.650
Or maybe the amount?

1591
01:30:46.610 --> 01:30:47.836
Is it like the way

1592
01:30:47.860 --> 01:30:49.780
I can anticipate movements
through scent?

1593
01:30:51.110 --> 01:30:53.240
There must be something I can do

1594
01:30:53.740 --> 01:30:55.530
to disrupt his compass!

1595
01:30:58.620 --> 01:30:59.910
[♪ rock music playing]

1596
01:31:05.540 --> 01:31:07.880
Hinokami Kagura: Dance!

1597
01:31:10.010 --> 01:31:12.986
Just one problem with your attack.

1598
01:31:13.010 --> 01:31:14.840
You're wide open!

1599
01:31:17.390 --> 01:31:18.890
[TANJIRO] His fist!

1600
01:31:24.650 --> 01:31:26.060
[grunts]

1601
01:31:30.490 --> 01:31:32.126
[panting]

1602
01:31:32.150 --> 01:31:33.426
Fighting spirit.

1603
01:31:33.450 --> 01:31:35.756
Instincts. Compass.

1604
01:31:35.780 --> 01:31:37.030
Perception.

1605
01:31:37.530 --> 01:31:41.176
Striking with killing intent.
Sensing the invisible.

1606
01:31:41.200 --> 01:31:43.330
Executing the impossible.

1607
01:31:43.790 --> 01:31:45.040
I see.

1608
01:31:46.750 --> 01:31:48.460
So. that's it.

1609
01:31:51.260 --> 01:31:53.430
- [birds chirping]
- [leaves rustling]

1610
01:31:56.340 --> 01:31:58.890
[laughter]

1611
01:32:05.600 --> 01:32:07.996
Um. Father?
What do you think about

1612
01:32:08.020 --> 01:32:10.440
when you dance the Hinokami Kagura?

1613
01:32:11.030 --> 01:32:14.990
If it's too tiring for you.
I can take your place next year.

1614
01:32:15.530 --> 01:32:17.870
I don't want you to overwork yourself.

1615
01:32:19.370 --> 01:32:21.200
Thank you. Tanjiro.

1616
01:32:21.910 --> 01:32:24.436
But to be honest.
I haven't found the Kagura

1617
01:32:24.460 --> 01:32:27.830
to be the least bit tiring
over the last few years.

1618
01:32:28.460 --> 01:32:30.226
I can't quite explain it.

1619
01:32:30.250 --> 01:32:33.736
but back when I learned it
from your grandfather years ago.

1620
01:32:33.760 --> 01:32:37.776
even though I was younger.
healthier and stronger than now.

1621
01:32:37.800 --> 01:32:40.850
I found it to be far more tiring back then.

1622
01:32:43.100 --> 01:32:44.536
[♪ poignant music playing]

1623
01:32:44.560 --> 01:32:47.286
[TANJIRO] For generations.
the Kagura was performed

1624
01:32:47.310 --> 01:32:50.060
by the Kamado family
at the start of each year.

1625
01:32:50.570 --> 01:32:52.586
It was an exhausting performance

1626
01:32:52.610 --> 01:32:55.490
that would last from sunset till dawn.

1627
01:32:56.700 --> 01:32:59.256
There are 12 different forms
that must be repeated

1628
01:32:59.280 --> 01:33:01.216
over and over again.

1629
01:33:01.240 --> 01:33:03.830
thousands of times before daybreak.

1630
01:33:06.670 --> 01:33:08.186
I think my exhaustion

1631
01:33:08.210 --> 01:33:10.540
was the result
of unnecessary movement.

1632
01:33:11.040 --> 01:33:12.726
Using the correct movements

1633
01:33:12.750 --> 01:33:15.630
and breathing patterns
are vital to the dance.

1634
01:33:16.380 --> 01:33:19.276
It's what allows you
to produce maximum strength

1635
01:33:19.300 --> 01:33:21.076
while using minimal actions.

1636
01:33:21.100 --> 01:33:24.116
Once you've mastered
your breathing and movement.

1637
01:33:24.140 --> 01:33:26.810
your mind will become transparent.

1638
01:33:27.520 --> 01:33:29.310
Transparent?

1639
01:33:30.270 --> 01:33:32.046
But before any of that.

1640
01:33:32.070 --> 01:33:34.416
you must memorize
the moves of the dance

1641
01:33:34.440 --> 01:33:37.756
and slowly ingrain them
into your muscle memory.

1642
01:33:37.780 --> 01:33:41.256
In doing so.
you'll open up your five senses

1643
01:33:41.280 --> 01:33:43.766
and become aware
of the shape of your own body.

1644
01:33:43.790 --> 01:33:45.580
vessel by vessel.

1645
01:33:47.160 --> 01:33:50.226
That was the truly strenuous part.

1646
01:33:50.250 --> 01:33:53.606
All you can think is that
even if you go on struggling.

1647
01:33:53.630 --> 01:33:55.510
you'll never succeed.

1648
01:33:56.050 --> 01:33:57.946
After you've learned all these things

1649
01:33:57.970 --> 01:33:59.526
and committed them to memory.

1650
01:33:59.550 --> 01:34:02.736
you'll understand how to remove
what you don't need.

1651
01:34:02.760 --> 01:34:06.616
only leaving behind in your body
what is required of you.

1652
01:34:06.640 --> 01:34:08.560
closing off the rest.

1653
01:34:09.140 --> 01:34:10.400
Closing?

1654
01:34:11.150 --> 01:34:13.416
You know how people
often close their eyes

1655
01:34:13.440 --> 01:34:15.400
when they're trying to hear better?

1656
01:34:16.150 --> 01:34:18.006
In that same way.

1657
01:34:18.030 --> 01:34:20.126
you'll pick out the things
you need the most

1658
01:34:20.150 --> 01:34:22.780
in the movement
while eliminating the rest.

1659
01:34:23.370 --> 01:34:27.176
Eventually. you will be able
to open and close the vessels

1660
01:34:27.200 --> 01:34:30.596
and muscles in your body.
as if it were second nature.

1661
01:34:30.620 --> 01:34:33.710
The same way you blink
without a second thought.

1662
01:34:34.420 --> 01:34:36.186
When that happens.

1663
01:34:36.210 --> 01:34:39.670
a path illuminated
by a bright light will open.

1664
01:34:40.930 --> 01:34:44.866
If your mind is as clear
as possible. you'll begin to see

1665
01:34:44.890 --> 01:34:47.406
the Transparent World before you.

1666
01:34:47.430 --> 01:34:49.826
But this domain can only be reached

1667
01:34:49.850 --> 01:34:51.786
by pushing yourself past your limits.

1668
01:34:51.810 --> 01:34:54.440
despite the suffering
that may be required.

1669
01:34:54.980 --> 01:34:56.690
Will I ever get to see it?

1670
01:34:57.690 --> 01:35:01.150
If you work tirelessly.
then that's for you to decide.

1671
01:35:01.860 --> 01:35:03.966
There. All done.

1672
01:35:03.990 --> 01:35:05.200
[TANJIRO] Thank you.

1673
01:35:08.870 --> 01:35:11.646
Ten days before my father died.

1674
01:35:11.670 --> 01:35:14.476
an incident where a bear
began attacking people

1675
01:35:14.500 --> 01:35:16.630
happened on a neighboring mountain.

1676
01:35:17.130 --> 01:35:19.776
We lit bonfires around the house

1677
01:35:19.800 --> 01:35:22.630
and set up multiple ropes lined with bells.

1678
01:35:34.190 --> 01:35:35.400
Hmm?

1679
01:35:41.240 --> 01:35:42.700
[TANJURO] Tanjiro.

1680
01:35:46.990 --> 01:35:48.660
[TANJIRO] Yes. Father?

1681
01:35:49.620 --> 01:35:50.950
[TANJURO] Come with me.

1682
01:35:52.000 --> 01:35:53.960
[Tanjiro grunting. panting]

1683
01:36:03.510 --> 01:36:04.840
[grunts]

1684
01:36:23.320 --> 01:36:25.450
[breathing unsteadily]

1685
01:36:26.280 --> 01:36:28.450
[♪ dramatic sting]

1686
01:36:32.700 --> 01:36:36.000
[loud growling]

1687
01:36:40.170 --> 01:36:43.236
[TANJURO] I understand
you must be very hungry.

1688
01:36:43.260 --> 01:36:46.470
But I'm afraid I can't allow you
to come any closer.

1689
01:36:47.640 --> 01:36:50.826
If anyone were to try
and cause harm to my family.

1690
01:36:50.850 --> 01:36:53.470
I would be forced to show you no mercy.

1691
01:36:53.980 --> 01:36:56.310
If you disregard this warning...

1692
01:36:59.270 --> 01:37:02.190
I'll have no choice but to take your life.

1693
01:37:03.070 --> 01:37:04.650
- [roaring]
- [bells tinkling]

1694
01:37:05.110 --> 01:37:06.626
[thuds]

1695
01:37:06.650 --> 01:37:07.820
[gasps]

1696
01:37:11.450 --> 01:37:13.466
[bells tinkling]

1697
01:37:13.490 --> 01:37:17.306
[TANJIRO] The bear's head that
was as thick as a human torso

1698
01:37:17.330 --> 01:37:20.330
dropped to the ground
with the sound of the bells.

1699
01:37:22.250 --> 01:37:24.526
My eyes couldn't follow it.

1700
01:37:24.550 --> 01:37:26.276
But if I'm not mistaken.

1701
01:37:26.300 --> 01:37:29.640
my father slashed it twice
in the blink of an eye.

1702
01:37:31.260 --> 01:37:32.826
He must have.

1703
01:37:32.850 --> 01:37:35.980
His ax wouldn't have been
able to cut through otherwise.

1704
01:37:37.480 --> 01:37:41.036
All the while.
my father's scent never wavered.

1705
01:37:41.060 --> 01:37:43.546
Before and after beheading the bear.

1706
01:37:43.570 --> 01:37:47.110
he emitted no fear.
no killing intent.

1707
01:37:54.370 --> 01:37:56.370
I hope that you were watching.

1708
01:37:57.410 --> 01:38:00.186
A day might come
where you have to do the same.

1709
01:38:00.210 --> 01:38:02.040
[wind blowing]

1710
01:38:03.170 --> 01:38:05.276
[TANJIRO] My father
wasn't the type of person

1711
01:38:05.300 --> 01:38:06.800
to flaunt his strength.

1712
01:38:07.510 --> 01:38:09.816
I realized later on.

1713
01:38:09.840 --> 01:38:13.850
that night. he wanted me
to see it in action.

1714
01:38:15.060 --> 01:38:17.616
The movements necessary
to be able to see

1715
01:38:17.640 --> 01:38:20.270
the Transparent World he spoke of.

1716
01:38:22.360 --> 01:38:26.860
I'm sure my father. grandfather.
and great-grandfather

1717
01:38:27.360 --> 01:38:29.530
all learned the same way.

1718
01:38:31.160 --> 01:38:33.636
Whatever you do. never give up.

1719
01:38:33.660 --> 01:38:35.870
Always stay calm and focused.

1720
01:38:36.540 --> 01:38:39.460
Any wall you come up against
can be shattered

1721
01:38:40.000 --> 01:38:42.130
if you just work tirelessly.

1722
01:38:43.840 --> 01:38:45.726
[TANJIRO] I understand. Father.

1723
01:38:45.750 --> 01:38:47.300
In that moment...

1724
01:38:47.840 --> 01:38:49.186
that's why I was able to dodge

1725
01:38:49.210 --> 01:38:52.340
Akaza's inescapable blow to my side.

1726
01:38:55.100 --> 01:38:56.906
If I hadn't moved in time.

1727
01:38:56.930 --> 01:38:59.390
I'm positive that strike
would have killed me.

1728
01:39:00.060 --> 01:39:02.706
When I was alternating moves
with Mr. Giyu.

1729
01:39:02.730 --> 01:39:05.270
weaving my attacks
in between each of his.

1730
01:39:05.770 --> 01:39:09.190
I was protected from being hit
by those lethal blows.

1731
01:39:09.690 --> 01:39:10.876
But in that instant.

1732
01:39:10.900 --> 01:39:13.570
even Mr. Giyu couldn't make it in time.

1733
01:39:14.820 --> 01:39:19.830
However. for whatever reason.
I knew dodging was possible.

1734
01:39:20.330 --> 01:39:23.016
And for just a split second.

1735
01:39:23.040 --> 01:39:24.920
I was able to see it.

1736
01:39:26.670 --> 01:39:28.300
That world.

1737
01:39:30.090 --> 01:39:32.106
[♪ enchanting music playing]

1738
01:39:32.130 --> 01:39:34.640
The Transparent World.

1739
01:39:36.930 --> 01:39:40.140
Even his body
started to look transparent.

1740
01:39:41.230 --> 01:39:45.060
The same is when Hantengu
was hiding inside his own heart.

1741
01:39:45.560 --> 01:39:48.690
I don't know if I saw him or smelled him.

1742
01:39:53.150 --> 01:39:54.586
Dodge.

1743
01:39:54.610 --> 01:39:57.830
I used only the senses
that would let me do that.

1744
01:39:58.370 --> 01:40:02.080
Without thinking. my body
moved faster than ever before.

1745
01:40:03.370 --> 01:40:06.856
When I'm inside the Transparent
World my father spoke of.

1746
01:40:06.880 --> 01:40:10.170
my battle instincts improve drastically.

1747
01:40:12.170 --> 01:40:14.446
I can see my opponent's lungs

1748
01:40:14.470 --> 01:40:16.800
and the blood moving
throughout their body.

1749
01:40:17.300 --> 01:40:19.786
I can see my own muscles contracting

1750
01:40:19.810 --> 01:40:22.600
faster and clearer than before.

1751
01:40:26.100 --> 01:40:28.376
If I close off the fighting spirit

1752
01:40:28.400 --> 01:40:31.046
that Akaza must be detecting me with.

1753
01:40:31.070 --> 01:40:32.860
I can go for his neck.

1754
01:40:33.320 --> 01:40:35.110
[screeches]

1755
01:40:45.830 --> 01:40:47.396
[TANJIRO] See it.

1756
01:40:47.420 --> 01:40:48.936
See it!

1757
01:40:48.960 --> 01:40:51.066
[exhales]

1758
01:40:51.090 --> 01:40:52.316
[♪ rock music playing]

1759
01:40:52.340 --> 01:40:53.816
It looks like you've thrown about

1760
01:40:53.840 --> 01:40:55.930
every last Water Form at me.

1761
01:40:56.550 --> 01:40:59.100
Enough is enough.
wouldn't you say?

1762
01:40:59.680 --> 01:41:01.536
I'm putting an end to this.

1763
01:41:01.560 --> 01:41:04.680
But you have my respect
for lasting so long!

1764
01:41:06.190 --> 01:41:07.310
[GIYU] What?

1765
01:41:08.440 --> 01:41:10.440
In the middle of my downswing...

1766
01:41:11.900 --> 01:41:13.730
he hit it from the side.

1767
01:41:15.360 --> 01:41:17.110
And snapped my sword!

1768
01:41:17.700 --> 01:41:19.990
- Goodbye. Giyu.
- [impact grunts]

1769
01:41:24.120 --> 01:41:25.910
[flesh squelching]

1770
01:41:26.870 --> 01:41:29.500
[muted silence]

1771
01:41:30.250 --> 01:41:31.316
[thuds]

1772
01:41:31.340 --> 01:41:33.460
[♪ intense dramatic music playing]

1773
01:41:43.600 --> 01:41:46.600
- [exhales]
- [flame roaring]

1774
01:41:49.270 --> 01:41:52.496
[GIYU] He stopped the attack
by cutting off his fist.

1775
01:41:52.520 --> 01:41:54.626
His breathing is different.

1776
01:41:54.650 --> 01:41:56.280
And his appearance...

1777
01:41:57.570 --> 01:41:59.990
I've been saved by Tanjiro.

1778
01:42:01.370 --> 01:42:03.306
[AKAZA] All of the cells in my body

1779
01:42:03.330 --> 01:42:04.926
down to the ones in my hair

1780
01:42:04.950 --> 01:42:08.160
are screaming at me to kill him
as soon as possible.

1781
01:42:09.870 --> 01:42:12.920
I don't know what kind of change
he underwent. but...

1782
01:42:14.170 --> 01:42:15.880
he's dangerous.

1783
01:42:17.420 --> 01:42:19.590
[GIYU] His focus is on Tanjiro.

1784
01:42:20.680 --> 01:42:22.300
Now's my chance.

1785
01:42:26.680 --> 01:42:29.520
[AKAZA] Technique Development.
Final Form:

1786
01:42:30.060 --> 01:42:32.440
Blue Silver Chaotic Afterglow!

1787
01:42:35.650 --> 01:42:38.046
[GIYU] His attack speed boosted again.

1788
01:42:38.070 --> 01:42:39.780
and the force is increased.

1789
01:42:40.240 --> 01:42:43.910
My only chance now is with Dead Calm!

1790
01:43:05.640 --> 01:43:08.470
[TANJIRO] This must be
what Father was talking about.

1791
01:43:08.980 --> 01:43:12.810
This is it.
The Transparent World.

1792
01:43:20.610 --> 01:43:27.120
Strange. It feels like
time is passing by so slowly.

1793
01:43:28.830 --> 01:43:33.516
Or maybe... their movements
just look slower now.

1794
01:43:33.540 --> 01:43:35.710
[♪ intense music continues]

1795
01:43:36.750 --> 01:43:38.090
[groans]

1796
01:43:39.460 --> 01:43:41.446
[GIYU] It's no use.

1797
01:43:41.470 --> 01:43:44.550
A hundred strikes at once is unavoidable.

1798
01:43:45.050 --> 01:43:46.696
Even with Dead Calm.

1799
01:43:46.720 --> 01:43:49.470
I still wasn't able to block all of them.

1800
01:43:50.810 --> 01:43:52.666
[AKAZA] Stand proud. Giyu.

1801
01:43:52.690 --> 01:43:55.536
Most wouldn't have been
able to survive that.

1802
01:43:55.560 --> 01:43:58.480
You must have evaded my fatal blows.

1803
01:43:59.280 --> 01:44:03.296
There's no need for you to die
like Kyojuro and Tanjiro did.

1804
01:44:03.320 --> 01:44:06.370
Give up your pride
and become a demon. Giyu.

1805
01:44:08.120 --> 01:44:11.580
[GIYU] Tanjiro's behind him
and he hasn't noticed?

1806
01:44:12.120 --> 01:44:14.686
- [Akaza speaking indistinctly]
- Is he masking his presence?

1807
01:44:14.710 --> 01:44:16.330
Now's our chance!

1808
01:44:17.170 --> 01:44:18.856
Tanjiro. do it!

1809
01:44:18.880 --> 01:44:21.300
If you have the strength. behead him.

1810
01:44:21.800 --> 01:44:23.736
Before he notices you.

1811
01:44:23.760 --> 01:44:25.276
go for it!

1812
01:44:25.300 --> 01:44:29.196
Akaza! Prepare to be decapitated!

1813
01:44:29.220 --> 01:44:30.470
[AKAZA] Huh?

1814
01:44:35.020 --> 01:44:37.560
[GIYU] He willingly gave himself away!

1815
01:44:38.190 --> 01:44:39.980
[AKAZA] He's still alive?

1816
01:44:40.440 --> 01:44:42.416
I never would have thought
someone like him

1817
01:44:42.440 --> 01:44:44.650
could survive an attack like that.

1818
01:44:45.200 --> 01:44:46.926
Well. it doesn't matter.

1819
01:44:46.950 --> 01:44:49.386
After all. my Destructive Death.
Compass Needle

1820
01:44:49.410 --> 01:44:50.990
can detect any attack!

1821
01:44:51.450 --> 01:44:54.806
The stronger my opponent's
fighting spirit is.

1822
01:44:54.830 --> 01:44:57.750
the greater
my Compass Needle's reaction.

1823
01:44:59.130 --> 01:45:00.340
[quivers]

1824
01:45:00.920 --> 01:45:02.630
What is this?

1825
01:45:03.090 --> 01:45:05.776
What is this odd presence he's emitting?

1826
01:45:05.800 --> 01:45:07.776
It feels like he's turned himself

1827
01:45:07.800 --> 01:45:09.616
into some other creature.

1828
01:45:09.640 --> 01:45:10.930
It's like...

1829
01:45:12.350 --> 01:45:14.906
his fighting spirit is gone.

1830
01:45:14.930 --> 01:45:16.246
But how?

1831
01:45:16.270 --> 01:45:19.020
I have to calm down. Focus!

1832
01:45:19.480 --> 01:45:20.860
[grunts]

1833
01:45:21.610 --> 01:45:23.070
[flame roaring]

1834
01:45:25.360 --> 01:45:27.426
[TANJIRO] Hinokami Kagura:

1835
01:45:27.450 --> 01:45:30.046
Setting Sun Transformation.

1836
01:45:30.070 --> 01:45:32.240
[♪ intriguing music playing]

1837
01:45:33.080 --> 01:45:35.200
[tinkling]

1838
01:45:48.130 --> 01:45:49.260
[gasps]

1839
01:45:51.510 --> 01:45:54.220
[Akaza straining]
This can't be possible.

1840
01:45:56.810 --> 01:45:59.190
[Tanjiro exhales]

1841
01:46:01.230 --> 01:46:03.546
[AKAZA] In the last
several hundred years.

1842
01:46:03.570 --> 01:46:07.030
I've never once seen a human
without any fighting spirit.

1843
01:46:07.490 --> 01:46:10.490
Even newborn children had traces of it.

1844
01:46:11.070 --> 01:46:13.596
And yet. in that instant.

1845
01:46:13.620 --> 01:46:15.556
his fighting spirit vanished

1846
01:46:15.580 --> 01:46:18.000
as if it were never there to begin with.

1847
01:46:21.500 --> 01:46:23.816
It's as if I was facing an anomaly

1848
01:46:23.840 --> 01:46:25.566
that shouldn't even exist.

1849
01:46:25.590 --> 01:46:28.300
So. my senses
were thrown into confusion.

1850
01:46:28.760 --> 01:46:31.800
My Compass Needle detected nothing.

1851
01:46:32.350 --> 01:46:33.826
[tinkling]

1852
01:46:33.850 --> 01:46:36.906
But that's not the biggest issue
at hand here.

1853
01:46:36.930 --> 01:46:38.656
When on the battlefield.

1854
01:46:38.680 --> 01:46:41.326
there's no telling
what could come your way.

1855
01:46:41.350 --> 01:46:44.036
It's vital that you're able
to deal with the unexpected

1856
01:46:44.060 --> 01:46:45.570
at a moment's notice.

1857
01:46:46.070 --> 01:46:48.320
And I'm able to do that!

1858
01:46:48.940 --> 01:46:51.860
Or at least... I thought so.

1859
01:46:52.780 --> 01:46:55.516
But during that short battle.

1860
01:46:55.540 --> 01:47:00.000
he was able to grasp something
and use it to surpass my speed.

1861
01:47:00.500 --> 01:47:02.976
Whatever it was he learned
was able to shatter

1862
01:47:03.000 --> 01:47:05.316
centuries' worth
of martial arts techniques

1863
01:47:05.340 --> 01:47:07.340
with a single head-on attack.

1864
01:47:08.050 --> 01:47:12.196
Within those eyes of his.
there was no hatred. no rage.

1865
01:47:12.220 --> 01:47:15.300
no killing intent or fighting spirit.

1866
01:47:15.970 --> 01:47:18.946
He must have somehow seen
what I'd been looking for:

1867
01:47:18.970 --> 01:47:23.350
the domain that lies
within the realm of the highest.

1868
01:47:25.060 --> 01:47:27.610
None other than the selfless state.

1869
01:47:29.730 --> 01:47:32.426
For some time now.
I've had a vague sense

1870
01:47:32.450 --> 01:47:34.490
that this state of mind existed.

1871
01:47:34.950 --> 01:47:37.556
And yet. even after all these centuries.

1872
01:47:37.580 --> 01:47:39.370
I've yet to attain it.

1873
01:47:46.880 --> 01:47:47.920
[gasps]

1874
01:47:48.500 --> 01:47:50.146
[AKAZA] Not yet!

1875
01:47:50.170 --> 01:47:51.896
I can still fight!

1876
01:47:51.920 --> 01:47:54.550
I will continue to become stronger!

1877
01:48:00.810 --> 01:48:03.890
[TANJIRO] This is bad.
He's reattaching his head!

1878
01:48:04.350 --> 01:48:06.480
[effort grunting]

1879
01:48:08.150 --> 01:48:10.360
- [thuds]
- [gasps]

1880
01:48:13.030 --> 01:48:15.410
[AKAZA] I can't die here.

1881
01:48:16.780 --> 01:48:18.620
Not like this.

1882
01:48:21.620 --> 01:48:24.370
I have to become stronger.

1883
01:48:26.460 --> 01:48:29.816
Stronger than anyone else
in the whole world!

1884
01:48:29.840 --> 01:48:31.630
Stronger!

1885
01:48:32.090 --> 01:48:33.896
- [thuds]
- [fizzles out]

1886
01:48:33.920 --> 01:48:37.090
I have to find a way to become stronger.

1887
01:48:39.180 --> 01:48:40.310
[clatters]

1888
01:48:44.230 --> 01:48:45.560
[body thuds]

1889
01:48:46.520 --> 01:48:49.440
[TANJIRO] That's it. It's over.

1890
01:48:51.150 --> 01:48:52.570
We won!

1891
01:48:53.530 --> 01:48:54.860
[sighs in relief]

1892
01:48:55.240 --> 01:48:57.160
[grunts in pain]

1893
01:48:57.530 --> 01:48:59.200
So lightheaded.

1894
01:49:01.030 --> 01:49:03.226
My muscles are cramping up.

1895
01:49:03.250 --> 01:49:05.370
My body's reached its limit.

1896
01:49:08.000 --> 01:49:10.800
Tanjiro. are you all ri...
[gasps]

1897
01:49:11.630 --> 01:49:14.356
His body hasn't disintegrated yet.

1898
01:49:14.380 --> 01:49:17.010
Does... Does this mean...

1899
01:49:17.470 --> 01:49:18.510
Tan...

1900
01:49:19.180 --> 01:49:20.616
[♪ intense music playing]

1901
01:49:20.640 --> 01:49:21.970
[grunts]

1902
01:49:28.850 --> 01:49:32.666
[TANJIRO] He's moving!
His body is still intact!

1903
01:49:32.690 --> 01:49:34.940
The severed part is closing up!

1904
01:49:36.150 --> 01:49:38.046
[strained grunting]

1905
01:49:38.070 --> 01:49:39.966
I can't see straight.

1906
01:49:39.990 --> 01:49:41.580
I can't.

1907
01:49:44.910 --> 01:49:46.120
[impact grunts]

1908
01:49:51.170 --> 01:49:52.526
[strained gasping]

1909
01:49:52.550 --> 01:49:55.356
No. No way.

1910
01:49:55.380 --> 01:49:57.776
Slashing his neck didn't kill him!

1911
01:49:57.800 --> 01:50:01.260
Is there some kind of condition
like with Gyutaro and Daki?

1912
01:50:01.720 --> 01:50:02.760
That can't be it.

1913
01:50:03.310 --> 01:50:06.810
His head disintegrated.
yet he hasn't given up!

1914
01:50:07.310 --> 01:50:10.650
It's like he's trying to evolve!

1915
01:50:12.480 --> 01:50:13.770
[impact grunts]

1916
01:50:16.940 --> 01:50:18.426
If we don't do something.

1917
01:50:18.450 --> 01:50:21.280
his head will stop
being his weak point like Muzan!

1918
01:50:21.950 --> 01:50:24.006
This battle isn't over yet.

1919
01:50:24.030 --> 01:50:25.950
I have to fight...

1920
01:50:26.700 --> 01:50:27.846
Tanjiro!

1921
01:50:27.870 --> 01:50:29.476
He's fainted.

1922
01:50:29.500 --> 01:50:31.056
Of course he has.

1923
01:50:31.080 --> 01:50:33.670
He's long since passed his limit.

1924
01:50:38.510 --> 01:50:40.180
[grunts]

1925
01:50:43.300 --> 01:50:46.496
Water Breathing. Fourth Form:

1926
01:50:46.520 --> 01:50:48.996
[♪ epic music playing]

1927
01:50:49.020 --> 01:50:50.810
Striking Tide!

1928
01:50:55.780 --> 01:50:57.416
Ridiculous!

1929
01:50:57.440 --> 01:51:00.490
He lost his head and can still
regenerate that quickly?

1930
01:51:01.240 --> 01:51:03.370
[sword clanking]

1931
01:51:04.490 --> 01:51:06.620
[grunting]

1932
01:51:13.250 --> 01:51:16.170
[yelling]

1933
01:51:20.550 --> 01:51:22.510
- [coughs]
- [blood splatters]

1934
01:51:24.850 --> 01:51:27.236
I can't hear out of my left ear.

1935
01:51:27.260 --> 01:51:29.350
and my right hand has gone numb.

1936
01:51:30.770 --> 01:51:34.310
I can still grip my sword.
but who knows for how long.

1937
01:51:42.990 --> 01:51:44.070
Wait!

1938
01:51:45.160 --> 01:51:46.280
I...

1939
01:51:46.910 --> 01:51:49.990
I'm here. I'm still alive!

1940
01:51:50.500 --> 01:51:55.040
If you wanna kill Tanjiro.
you'll have to defeat me first!

1941
01:51:59.130 --> 01:52:01.396
[AKAZA] An indomitable spirit.

1942
01:52:01.420 --> 01:52:02.946
It will never bend.

1943
01:52:02.970 --> 01:52:06.010
no matter what crisis it finds itself in.

1944
01:52:06.800 --> 01:52:09.496
We don't fight the way samurai do.

1945
01:52:09.520 --> 01:52:11.576
We don't carry weapons.

1946
01:52:11.600 --> 01:52:14.730
though we carry our convictions
like swords.

1947
01:52:16.270 --> 01:52:19.570
[MAN] Though we carry
our convictions like swords.

1948
01:52:20.280 --> 01:52:24.320
our battles are waged with our fists.

1949
01:52:25.740 --> 01:52:28.830
[AKAZA] You are such an eyesore!

1950
01:52:31.620 --> 01:52:33.000
[soft thump]

1951
01:52:39.340 --> 01:52:40.880
[GIRL] Please stop.

1952
01:52:47.090 --> 01:52:48.680
[AKAZA] Who is that?

1953
01:52:54.020 --> 01:52:55.996
Mr. Hakuji.

1954
01:52:56.020 --> 01:52:57.836
please. that's enough!

1955
01:52:57.860 --> 01:52:59.400
[♪ poignant music playing]

1956
01:53:00.940 --> 01:53:05.070
[AKAZA] Let go. Let go of my hand.

1957
01:53:05.530 --> 01:53:07.070
Just who are you?

1958
01:53:08.870 --> 01:53:12.176
Stop. You don't
have to keep going. [sniffles]

1959
01:53:12.200 --> 01:53:14.750
Let's leave this place together.

1960
01:53:15.120 --> 01:53:17.056
[AKAZA] I can't.

1961
01:53:17.080 --> 01:53:20.420
I've still got unfinished
business with those two.

1962
01:53:21.800 --> 01:53:23.800
[GIRL] What do you mean by that?

1963
01:53:24.380 --> 01:53:26.606
[AKAZA] I've got to become stronger.

1964
01:53:26.630 --> 01:53:28.050
I've got to!

1965
01:53:28.550 --> 01:53:31.600
I'll kill anyone who gets in my way.

1966
01:53:32.310 --> 01:53:35.036
Why do you want that? [sniffles]

1967
01:53:35.060 --> 01:53:38.100
For what reason
do you need to become stronger?

1968
01:53:39.650 --> 01:53:43.796
[AKAZA] Because...
unless I'm strong enough.

1969
01:53:43.820 --> 01:53:47.150
I won't be able to bring
any more back home to him.

1970
01:53:49.280 --> 01:53:51.580
He needs medicine.

1971
01:53:53.620 --> 01:53:56.460
I must become stronger.

1972
01:53:57.210 --> 01:53:58.500
[grunts angrily]

1973
01:53:58.830 --> 01:54:02.170
If I don't. I won't be able to
get away with the money I stole.

1974
01:54:03.500 --> 01:54:05.316
If I happen to be caught.

1975
01:54:05.340 --> 01:54:07.670
I won't be able to defend myself.

1976
01:54:09.090 --> 01:54:10.866
If I'm not strong enough.

1977
01:54:10.890 --> 01:54:14.510
the magistrate will catch me
and have me beaten and lashed.

1978
01:54:14.970 --> 01:54:17.060
[whipping]

1979
01:54:17.940 --> 01:54:19.416
[MAGISTRATE] We've already given you

1980
01:54:19.440 --> 01:54:22.336
three tattoos on each arm for stealing.

1981
01:54:22.360 --> 01:54:24.916
Next time.
we'll chop off your hand.

1982
01:54:24.940 --> 01:54:26.490
[Hakuji chuckling]

1983
01:54:29.200 --> 01:54:31.200
[laughing]

1984
01:54:32.910 --> 01:54:34.966
[ATTENDANT]
Bow your head and repent!

1985
01:54:34.990 --> 01:54:37.346
If you're gonna chop it off.
then do it!

1986
01:54:37.370 --> 01:54:40.266
Go ahead and take both of them
if you're really serious.

1987
01:54:40.290 --> 01:54:42.476
I'll just use my feet to steal.

1988
01:54:42.500 --> 01:54:45.460
You're not gonna catch me again.
so make it count!

1989
01:54:47.920 --> 01:54:51.406
[MAGISTRATE] To hear this from
someone at such a young age.

1990
01:54:51.430 --> 01:54:54.076
This boy of 11 has already
taken on punishments

1991
01:54:54.100 --> 01:54:56.520
that would make a grown man faint.

1992
01:54:57.770 --> 01:54:59.746
You are a demon child!

1993
01:54:59.770 --> 01:55:01.956
Go and call me
whatever names you want.

1994
01:55:01.980 --> 01:55:04.666
"Demon child" suits me just damn fine!

1995
01:55:04.690 --> 01:55:06.956
They say I already had teeth
when I was born.

1996
01:55:06.980 --> 01:55:07.966
so I guess I am.

1997
01:55:07.990 --> 01:55:10.256
- Be quiet!
- Dirty little punk!

1998
01:55:10.280 --> 01:55:13.386
[HAKUJI] Don't you mean
"demon child." you bastard?

1999
01:55:13.410 --> 01:55:15.660
[grunts]

2000
01:55:17.120 --> 01:55:18.176
Hmph!

2001
01:55:18.200 --> 01:55:21.726
SOUTH TOWN MAGISTRATE'S OFFICE

2002
01:55:21.750 --> 01:55:22.856
[birds calling]

2003
01:55:22.880 --> 01:55:24.016
[MAN 1] Hakuji!

2004
01:55:24.040 --> 01:55:26.316
[MAN 2] Oh! [panting]
There you are!

2005
01:55:26.340 --> 01:55:28.816
[voice breaking] When you were
caught for stealing again.

2006
01:55:28.840 --> 01:55:32.050
word about it made its way
back to your father.

2007
01:55:32.590 --> 01:55:35.100
He hung himself. Hakuji!

2008
01:55:35.550 --> 01:55:36.600
Huh?

2009
01:55:39.810 --> 01:55:42.060
[Hakuji's father weakly]
"Dear Hakuji.

2010
01:55:43.190 --> 01:55:45.310
live an honest life.

2011
01:55:45.900 --> 01:55:48.110
You can still start over."

2012
01:55:48.900 --> 01:55:51.070
- [wind blowing]
- [leaves rustling]

2013
01:55:53.030 --> 01:55:54.086
[♪ poignant music continues]

2014
01:55:54.110 --> 01:55:55.346
[paper fluttering]

2015
01:55:55.370 --> 01:55:57.756
[HAKUJI] What kind of world is this?

2016
01:55:57.780 --> 01:56:00.500
Are the poor not even allowed to live?

2017
01:56:05.500 --> 01:56:06.670
[voice breaking] Dad.

2018
01:56:08.920 --> 01:56:11.066
To hell with this rotten world.

2019
01:56:11.090 --> 01:56:13.300
To all of it! [sobbing]

2020
01:56:15.800 --> 01:56:20.036
Every rotten human.
they can all burn in hell!

2021
01:56:20.060 --> 01:56:22.270
[grunts angrily]

2022
01:56:23.940 --> 01:56:27.376
Why do scumbags like them
get the privilege of living

2023
01:56:27.400 --> 01:56:30.666
when my father had to die
in such a horrible way?

2024
01:56:30.690 --> 01:56:33.296
He was never a burden to me.

2025
01:56:33.320 --> 01:56:35.410
So why would he feel that way?

2026
01:56:35.860 --> 01:56:39.200
You didn't do anything wrong.
Dad. You didn't!

2027
01:56:41.200 --> 01:56:43.516
I never cared about getting beaten

2028
01:56:43.540 --> 01:56:45.436
after I was caught stealing.

2029
01:56:45.460 --> 01:56:49.266
Even if they beat me until every
bone in my body was broken.

2030
01:56:49.290 --> 01:56:51.356
I could take it all for you. Dad.

2031
01:56:51.380 --> 01:56:52.776
For centuries even.

2032
01:56:52.800 --> 01:56:55.470
Learn your lesson!
Live an honest life!

2033
01:56:56.220 --> 01:56:59.236
[HAKUJI] Why don't you
shut the hell up. you scumbag?

2034
01:56:59.260 --> 01:57:01.246
Medicine's expensive.

2035
01:57:01.270 --> 01:57:03.930
The hell do you expect me
to do about that?

2036
01:57:05.390 --> 01:57:09.020
My dad's only getting thinner
and thinner by the day.

2037
01:57:10.110 --> 01:57:13.190
He's so malnourished.
you can see his bones.

2038
01:57:13.780 --> 01:57:17.160
I just want him to have
something better to eat.

2039
01:57:19.410 --> 01:57:22.120
I would have happily given my life...

2040
01:57:24.040 --> 01:57:26.250
[voice breaking]
if it meant saving his.

2041
01:57:32.380 --> 01:57:36.380
I'd have done anything...
for my father!

2042
01:57:39.260 --> 01:57:41.486
[breathing heavily]

2043
01:57:41.510 --> 01:57:44.406
- [clapping]
- Huh?

2044
01:57:44.430 --> 01:57:45.576
SORYU

2045
01:57:45.600 --> 01:57:47.666
[MAN] Well. well.
I am quite impressed.

2046
01:57:47.690 --> 01:57:50.286
I was called over
because someone said that

2047
01:57:50.310 --> 01:57:51.796
a child was about to be killed.

2048
01:57:51.820 --> 01:57:55.256
But you've laid out seven
grown-ups with your bare fists.

2049
01:57:55.280 --> 01:57:57.626
You've got some talent.
don't ya?

2050
01:57:57.650 --> 01:58:01.426
Not just anyone can take on
that many guys and still win.

2051
01:58:01.450 --> 01:58:04.080
[chuckling] That's the kind of
spunk I like to see.

2052
01:58:06.290 --> 01:58:08.436
[AKAZA] What's going on here?

2053
01:58:08.460 --> 01:58:10.460
Who is this man?

2054
01:58:11.460 --> 01:58:13.816
Could these be my memories?

2055
01:58:13.840 --> 01:58:15.856
How about you join my dojo?

2056
01:58:15.880 --> 01:58:18.090
I don't have any students at the moment.

2057
01:58:18.550 --> 01:58:20.566
Stay out of my way.
you old fart!

2058
01:58:20.590 --> 01:58:22.076
You lookin' to die?

2059
01:58:22.100 --> 01:58:23.986
- Those tattoos.
- Uh?

2060
01:58:24.010 --> 01:58:25.640
You're a criminal from Edo.

2061
01:58:26.310 --> 01:58:28.206
I'm guessing after being thrown out.

2062
01:58:28.230 --> 01:58:30.916
you eventually found your way here.

2063
01:58:30.940 --> 01:58:32.956
I never asked for your opinion.

2064
01:58:32.980 --> 01:58:35.456
Now shut up
and get the hell out of my way!

2065
01:58:35.480 --> 01:58:39.070
[scoffs] All right.
Time to be reborn!

2066
01:58:39.950 --> 01:58:41.490
You ready?

2067
01:58:42.370 --> 01:58:46.700
That's it. Drop dead. old man!
[grunting]

2068
01:58:47.450 --> 01:58:48.710
[impact grunts]

2069
01:58:56.920 --> 01:58:59.396
[strained grunt. coughs. gasps]

2070
01:58:59.420 --> 01:59:00.760
[body thuds]

2071
01:59:04.430 --> 01:59:05.786
SORYU

2072
01:59:05.810 --> 01:59:07.786
[MAN] I'll give it to you. You're tough.

2073
01:59:07.810 --> 01:59:08.787
DOJO

2074
01:59:08.811 --> 01:59:10.456
After that beating I gave you.

2075
01:59:10.480 --> 01:59:12.600
you came to in less than an hour.

2076
01:59:13.650 --> 01:59:15.020
The name's Keizo.

2077
01:59:15.690 --> 01:59:17.626
I teach the Soryu style of fighting

2078
01:59:17.650 --> 01:59:20.126
which uses only your bare hands.

2079
01:59:20.150 --> 01:59:23.280
Like I said. I don't have
any other students.

2080
01:59:23.780 --> 01:59:27.490
So I get by by doing whatever
odd jobs I can for people.

2081
01:59:30.080 --> 01:59:32.806
I have a daughter
who's in rather poor health.

2082
01:59:32.830 --> 01:59:35.210
I'd like you to help look after her.

2083
01:59:35.710 --> 01:59:39.130
I'd be here if I could.
but I have to work.

2084
01:59:40.130 --> 01:59:42.606
My wife was pushed
to the edge of exhaustion

2085
01:59:42.630 --> 01:59:44.090
and drowned herself.

2086
01:59:45.100 --> 01:59:47.640
Life sure takes a bite
out of you. doesn't it?

2087
01:59:51.770 --> 01:59:53.746
If I were a more capable man.

2088
01:59:53.770 --> 01:59:56.520
my wife and daughter wouldn't
have suffered like this.

2089
01:59:59.530 --> 02:00:01.876
You said you knew I was a criminal.

2090
02:00:01.900 --> 02:00:05.120
Are you really all right leaving
your daughter around me?

2091
02:00:06.490 --> 02:00:08.096
Why wouldn't I be?

2092
02:00:08.120 --> 02:00:10.886
I pummeled the criminal
out of you earlier. didn't I?

2093
02:00:10.910 --> 02:00:12.000
It's fine.

2094
02:00:12.870 --> 02:00:15.106
[♪ tender music playing]

2095
02:00:15.130 --> 02:00:17.250
[AKAZA] They are alike.

2096
02:00:24.880 --> 02:00:26.760
I get it now.

2097
02:00:28.050 --> 02:00:30.720
The reason you disgusted me earlier.

2098
02:00:31.220 --> 02:00:32.456
It was because you would've

2099
02:00:32.480 --> 02:00:35.600
dredged up memories
of my worthless past.

2100
02:00:40.570 --> 02:00:43.110
[KEIZO] This is my daughter. Koyuki.

2101
02:00:43.780 --> 02:00:45.160
[coughing]

2102
02:00:46.110 --> 02:00:48.570
[AKAZA] My worthless past.

2103
02:00:51.830 --> 02:00:53.250
Worthless.

2104
02:00:57.380 --> 02:01:00.210
[coughing]

2105
02:01:02.380 --> 02:01:05.800
Hakuji. I'm so sorry.

2106
02:01:06.680 --> 02:01:08.906
[chuckles] How are you feeling?

2107
02:01:08.930 --> 02:01:10.946
[coughing]

2108
02:01:10.970 --> 02:01:12.680
You okay being up?

2109
02:01:13.680 --> 02:01:14.730
[KOYUKI] Hmm.

2110
02:01:15.390 --> 02:01:18.706
Looks like you've got more color
in your cheeks this morning.

2111
02:01:18.730 --> 02:01:20.480
[chuckles] That's good.

2112
02:01:21.150 --> 02:01:22.230
Hmm.

2113
02:01:22.820 --> 02:01:26.086
- Huh?
- Oh. yeah. This boy.

2114
02:01:26.110 --> 02:01:28.176
His name is... [chuckles]

2115
02:01:28.200 --> 02:01:31.466
Well. I've asked him countless
times. and he won't say.

2116
02:01:31.490 --> 02:01:33.620
- Go on. get inside.
- [grunts]

2117
02:01:35.330 --> 02:01:36.540
Have a seat.

2118
02:01:38.330 --> 02:01:41.340
I wanna know his name
when I get back. Okay?

2119
02:01:52.930 --> 02:01:54.180
Um...

2120
02:01:54.640 --> 02:01:57.690
Your... Your face.

2121
02:01:58.270 --> 02:01:59.690
You're hurt.

2122
02:02:00.270 --> 02:02:01.810
Are you all right?

2123
02:02:05.070 --> 02:02:07.086
[AKAZA] "I'll make you better.

2124
02:02:07.110 --> 02:02:08.926
I'll save you.

2125
02:02:08.950 --> 02:02:10.320
Protect you."

2126
02:02:10.950 --> 02:02:15.500
In that past life. all I did
was spew a bunch of lies.

2127
02:02:15.950 --> 02:02:17.660
I was so pathetic.

2128
02:02:19.540 --> 02:02:22.000
[birds chirping]

2129
02:02:27.130 --> 02:02:29.550
[coughing]

2130
02:02:34.260 --> 02:02:35.930
Oh. thank you.

2131
02:02:37.430 --> 02:02:40.206
[HAKUJI] You don't have to
thank me every time. you know.

2132
02:02:40.230 --> 02:02:41.980
Just focus on resting.

2133
02:02:43.730 --> 02:02:47.626
I'm sorry for causing
you trouble like this.

2134
02:02:47.650 --> 02:02:49.780
It's fine. Really.

2135
02:02:51.620 --> 02:02:54.410
Koyuki. you want this closed?

2136
02:02:55.200 --> 02:02:58.620
Hmm. You can leave it open.

2137
02:03:00.540 --> 02:03:03.340
[HAKUJI] Koyuki was very
delicate and frail.

2138
02:03:04.750 --> 02:03:08.606
I would change out her towels
and nightgown and give her water

2139
02:03:08.630 --> 02:03:10.260
even throughout the night.

2140
02:03:10.840 --> 02:03:13.656
And whenever she needed
to use the lavatory.

2141
02:03:13.680 --> 02:03:16.036
obviously she was too weak
to be able to go

2142
02:03:16.060 --> 02:03:17.600
without needing assistance.

2143
02:03:21.560 --> 02:03:24.836
I was used to taking care
of the sick because of my dad.

2144
02:03:24.860 --> 02:03:28.586
and since I had an almost
inhuman physical endurance.

2145
02:03:28.610 --> 02:03:30.860
it really wasn't a big deal for me.

2146
02:03:33.410 --> 02:03:35.846
[crows cawing]

2147
02:03:35.870 --> 02:03:38.330
Sorry to make you help me all day.

2148
02:03:44.920 --> 02:03:47.776
[HAKUJI] Why do people
who are suffering from illness

2149
02:03:47.800 --> 02:03:50.220
always feel the need to say
they're sorry?

2150
02:03:51.090 --> 02:03:53.510
"Sorry to make you do things for me."

2151
02:03:54.050 --> 02:03:56.640
"Sorry if my coughing's bothering you."

2152
02:03:57.260 --> 02:04:00.390
"Sorry I can't put food
on the table like I should."

2153
02:04:02.480 --> 02:04:05.376
They didn't choose
to have to live this way.

2154
02:04:05.400 --> 02:04:07.626
Of course they wanna breathe normally.

2155
02:04:07.650 --> 02:04:10.030
They can't help it if they start coughing.

2156
02:04:11.280 --> 02:04:12.796
Out of everyone.

2157
02:04:12.820 --> 02:04:15.320
they're the ones suffering the most.

2158
02:04:18.080 --> 02:04:20.540
Sorry again to make you do this.

2159
02:04:21.080 --> 02:04:22.936
Because of my sickness.

2160
02:04:22.960 --> 02:04:25.476
you're not able to do your training.

2161
02:04:25.500 --> 02:04:27.840
or even go out and have fun.

2162
02:04:28.710 --> 02:04:30.726
[HAKUJI] I don't care about having fun.

2163
02:04:30.750 --> 02:04:32.090
I never have.

2164
02:04:32.880 --> 02:04:36.066
As far as training goes.
I squeeze it in whenever I can.

2165
02:04:36.090 --> 02:04:37.600
so. it's fine.

2166
02:04:38.890 --> 02:04:39.970
Are you sure?

2167
02:04:40.640 --> 02:04:43.690
Even you need to take a little break.

2168
02:04:44.520 --> 02:04:48.086
I hear there are fireworks
happening tonight.

2169
02:04:48.110 --> 02:04:49.770
You should go see them.

2170
02:04:51.110 --> 02:04:52.916
Fireworks. huh?

2171
02:04:52.940 --> 02:04:55.426
If you don't feel nauseous at night.

2172
02:04:55.450 --> 02:04:58.966
I could carry you on my back
and go see them on the bridge.

2173
02:04:58.990 --> 02:05:00.200
Huh?

2174
02:05:03.750 --> 02:05:05.846
If you're not feeling up to it.

2175
02:05:05.870 --> 02:05:09.016
they'll do fireworks again
next year. and after that.

2176
02:05:09.040 --> 02:05:11.210
So. we can just go when you're better.

2177
02:05:16.130 --> 02:05:18.050
[crying softly]

2178
02:05:19.800 --> 02:05:22.326
There was one thing that was hard

2179
02:05:22.350 --> 02:05:23.810
about taking care of her.

2180
02:05:23.980 --> 02:05:26.916
And that was whenever she would
suddenly break out into tears

2181
02:05:26.940 --> 02:05:28.810
in the middle of our conversations.

2182
02:05:29.480 --> 02:05:33.530
I can imagine how she felt.
bedridden and sick as she was.

2183
02:05:33.990 --> 02:05:36.426
but it still made me uncomfortable.

2184
02:05:36.450 --> 02:05:37.756
[insects trilling]

2185
02:05:37.780 --> 02:05:40.330
SORYU

2186
02:05:48.040 --> 02:05:49.580
[impact grunts. wheezes]

2187
02:05:50.710 --> 02:05:53.550
[sighs] Ah. now I understand.

2188
02:05:54.090 --> 02:05:55.896
The symbol used for Hakuji.

2189
02:05:55.920 --> 02:05:57.486
it's the same as komainu.

2190
02:05:57.510 --> 02:05:59.616
[chuckles] That makes sense.

2191
02:05:59.640 --> 02:06:01.826
You and I really are the same.
after all.

2192
02:06:01.850 --> 02:06:05.076
We only thrive when we have
something to protect.

2193
02:06:05.100 --> 02:06:06.536
Just like the komainu

2194
02:06:06.560 --> 02:06:09.270
who protect the entrance
to the shrines. [chuckles]

2195
02:06:09.730 --> 02:06:11.860
[laughs heartily]

2196
02:06:12.440 --> 02:06:13.900
[♪ gentle music playing]

2197
02:06:14.110 --> 02:06:17.086
[HAKUJI] There was a story as to
how my master owned this land.

2198
02:06:17.110 --> 02:06:20.296
even though he wasn't a samurai
or anything like that.

2199
02:06:20.320 --> 02:06:23.790
He had rescued an elderly man
from a group of bandits.

2200
02:06:24.370 --> 02:06:26.596
The old man. who had no living heirs.

2201
02:06:26.620 --> 02:06:28.886
was so impressed
by his Soryu technique

2202
02:06:28.910 --> 02:06:30.936
that he left him not only his land.

2203
02:06:30.960 --> 02:06:32.880
but the dojo that lay upon it.

2204
02:06:36.050 --> 02:06:39.196
However. there were those
with envious eyes

2205
02:06:39.220 --> 02:06:42.220
who wished to have the land
and dojo all to themselves.

2206
02:06:42.890 --> 02:06:45.366
The Kenjutsu Dojo next door

2207
02:06:45.390 --> 02:06:48.140
started harassing the Soryu Dojo.

2208
02:06:49.890 --> 02:06:52.996
Because of that.
the Soryu Dojo had a hard time

2209
02:06:53.020 --> 02:06:54.440
keeping any students.

2210
02:07:01.870 --> 02:07:06.750
But now. thanks to my training
here and caring for Koyuki...

2211
02:07:08.000 --> 02:07:11.170
my heart has finally found salvation.

2212
02:07:12.210 --> 02:07:14.380
[effort grunting]

2213
02:07:24.720 --> 02:07:26.770
[chuckles]

2214
02:07:30.310 --> 02:07:34.230
Three short years went by
and I turned 18.

2215
02:07:35.360 --> 02:07:36.980
Koyuki was 16.

2216
02:07:37.440 --> 02:07:40.166
She was almost never
bedridden anymore

2217
02:07:40.190 --> 02:07:42.700
and was now able to live a normal life.

2218
02:07:43.870 --> 02:07:45.320
[chuckles]

2219
02:07:45.910 --> 02:07:47.176
[birds chirping]

2220
02:07:47.200 --> 02:07:49.160
Hakuji! Come here.

2221
02:07:49.910 --> 02:07:50.950
Yes. sir.

2222
02:07:51.410 --> 02:07:52.896
[insects trilling]

2223
02:07:52.920 --> 02:07:54.210
This dojo.

2224
02:07:54.330 --> 02:07:57.300
would you be willing
to take it over for me. Hakuji?

2225
02:07:58.000 --> 02:08:01.340
Koyuki's told me that
she's quite fond of you as well.

2226
02:08:02.300 --> 02:08:03.590
[exclaims in surprise]

2227
02:08:11.140 --> 02:08:14.286
[HAKUJI] As someone branded
with the tattoos of a criminal.

2228
02:08:14.310 --> 02:08:17.770
picturing any kind of future
for myself was hard enough.

2229
02:08:19.110 --> 02:08:23.466
But a future in which someone
could like a person like me?

2230
02:08:23.490 --> 02:08:25.530
I couldn't have even dreamed it.

2231
02:08:27.490 --> 02:08:30.136
My dad asked me to lead an honest life.

2232
02:08:30.160 --> 02:08:32.250
something I never thought was possible.

2233
02:08:32.750 --> 02:08:35.000
But perhaps it really is.

2234
02:08:36.460 --> 02:08:39.146
The faint hope of being able to start over

2235
02:08:39.170 --> 02:08:41.396
began to swell within me

2236
02:08:41.420 --> 02:08:44.220
until it felt like it was about to burst.

2237
02:08:49.310 --> 02:08:50.786
[♪ tender music playing]

2238
02:08:50.810 --> 02:08:53.456
But I could never have predicted
in that moment

2239
02:08:53.480 --> 02:08:55.456
that the two people I wanted to protect

2240
02:08:55.480 --> 02:08:57.810
more than anything else in this life...

2241
02:08:58.820 --> 02:09:01.360
would end up meeting the fate they did.

2242
02:09:06.280 --> 02:09:09.530
I had made a trip to Edo
to visit my dad's grave.

2243
02:09:10.330 --> 02:09:13.410
I wanted to let him know
that I was getting married.

2244
02:09:23.210 --> 02:09:27.050
I returned before even a full
day and night had passed.

2245
02:09:29.970 --> 02:09:32.850
Yet a sense of dread came over me.

2246
02:09:33.850 --> 02:09:36.326
My chest started to feel tight

2247
02:09:36.350 --> 02:09:39.480
and a terrible feeling of nausea
overtook me.

2248
02:09:40.190 --> 02:09:41.520
[retches]

2249
02:09:41.980 --> 02:09:44.490
[MAN] Someone put poison in the well!

2250
02:09:45.320 --> 02:09:46.886
[voice breaking]
The other school was so angry

2251
02:09:46.910 --> 02:09:48.846
they couldn't beat you or Mr. Keizo.

2252
02:09:48.870 --> 02:09:51.096
they went and did this out of spite!

2253
02:09:51.120 --> 02:09:53.676
It's atrocious. Unthinkable!

2254
02:09:53.700 --> 02:09:55.750
They even killed Koyuki!

2255
02:09:59.170 --> 02:10:00.590
[HAKUJI] Why?

2256
02:10:00.790 --> 02:10:04.276
Why is it whenever the ones I
care about are in mortal peril.

2257
02:10:04.300 --> 02:10:06.550
I'm never there for them?

2258
02:10:11.930 --> 02:10:13.260
[fireworks bursting in distance]

2259
02:10:13.890 --> 02:10:15.406
[crickets chirping]

2260
02:10:15.430 --> 02:10:18.520
I had even gone
and made a promise to her.

2261
02:10:20.610 --> 02:10:23.230
Are you sure that I'm the one for you?

2262
02:10:25.320 --> 02:10:26.900
When we were children.

2263
02:10:27.360 --> 02:10:29.886
do you remember when you talked to me

2264
02:10:29.910 --> 02:10:31.870
about seeing the fireworks?

2265
02:10:32.490 --> 02:10:36.830
- Huh? Uh... no. not really.
- [giggles softly]

2266
02:10:38.080 --> 02:10:40.806
Because of those little talks
we used to have.

2267
02:10:40.830 --> 02:10:43.516
there were a lot of things
which I took with me

2268
02:10:43.540 --> 02:10:45.630
that gave me hope for the future.

2269
02:10:46.840 --> 02:10:50.316
You said even if we couldn't see
the fireworks that year.

2270
02:10:50.340 --> 02:10:53.826
we could go to the one
happening next year.

2271
02:10:53.850 --> 02:10:55.560
or the year after that.

2272
02:10:56.270 --> 02:10:59.536
The truth is.
I could never imagine a future

2273
02:10:59.560 --> 02:11:01.956
where I'd still be alive a year later.

2274
02:11:01.980 --> 02:11:04.770
and certainly not any longer than that.

2275
02:11:05.940 --> 02:11:08.126
My mother couldn't either.

2276
02:11:08.150 --> 02:11:11.280
I think that's why she ended up
taking her own life.

2277
02:11:11.780 --> 02:11:14.256
'cause she didn't want to see me die.

2278
02:11:14.280 --> 02:11:16.096
Not just her.

2279
02:11:16.120 --> 02:11:18.976
I could tell my father
had given up hope. too.

2280
02:11:19.000 --> 02:11:20.750
deep down inside.

2281
02:11:21.870 --> 02:11:24.210
Because I was just so weak.

2282
02:11:25.540 --> 02:11:28.146
But you never treated me that way.

2283
02:11:28.170 --> 02:11:30.840
You were able to see a future for me.

2284
02:11:31.680 --> 02:11:35.196
You talked to me about
doing things as if...

2285
02:11:35.220 --> 02:11:38.326
As if it were obvious
that I'd still be here.

2286
02:11:38.350 --> 02:11:41.600
[crying softly]
That made me so very happy.

2287
02:11:52.950 --> 02:11:56.030
So. yes. I am sure you're the one for me.

2288
02:11:58.080 --> 02:11:59.450
Would you...

2289
02:12:00.000 --> 02:12:02.120
Would you be my husband?

2290
02:12:02.540 --> 02:12:03.830
[distant explosion]

2291
02:12:09.130 --> 02:12:10.236
[fireworks bursting]

2292
02:12:10.260 --> 02:12:11.340
Yes.

2293
02:12:11.970 --> 02:12:14.590
I promise to become stronger
than anyone.

2294
02:12:15.220 --> 02:12:17.760
and protect you for the rest of my life.

2295
02:12:19.140 --> 02:12:20.390
[exclaims]

2296
02:12:22.230 --> 02:12:25.560
[HAKUJI] In the end. I was all talk.

2297
02:12:26.060 --> 02:12:29.190
I wasn't able to fulfill
any of my promises.

2298
02:12:29.730 --> 02:12:31.110
[chuckles]

2299
02:12:36.780 --> 02:12:38.950
[♪ foreboding music playing]

2300
02:12:41.750 --> 02:12:44.420
What do you want? [gasps]

2301
02:12:44.960 --> 02:12:46.686
You've got some nerve.

2302
02:12:46.710 --> 02:12:49.500
Wait. You're from the Soryu...

2303
02:12:50.380 --> 02:12:52.196
[screaming]

2304
02:12:52.220 --> 02:12:53.840
[♪ somber music playing]

2305
02:12:57.800 --> 02:12:59.140
[man grunts]

2306
02:13:02.680 --> 02:13:05.666
[Hakuji grunts. yells]

2307
02:13:05.690 --> 02:13:07.690
[groans angrily]

2308
02:13:12.860 --> 02:13:15.966
The family. the Soryu Dojo.
were recently poisoned.

2309
02:13:15.990 --> 02:13:18.296
And we believe that a student of theirs

2310
02:13:18.320 --> 02:13:21.056
retaliated against the Kenjutsu Dojo.

2311
02:13:21.080 --> 02:13:23.886
Sixty-seven people
were murdered inside.

2312
02:13:23.910 --> 02:13:26.596
He shattered their skulls
and crushed their organs.

2313
02:13:26.620 --> 02:13:28.040
all barehanded.

2314
02:13:28.580 --> 02:13:30.066
Not only were most of the bodies

2315
02:13:30.090 --> 02:13:32.606
mangled and mutilated
beyond recognition.

2316
02:13:32.630 --> 02:13:35.906
most had limbs missing
that we couldn't even locate.

2317
02:13:35.930 --> 02:13:38.276
Organs. limbs. brain matter.

2318
02:13:38.300 --> 02:13:40.366
even jaws and eyeballs were found

2319
02:13:40.390 --> 02:13:43.520
strewn across the walls
and the ceiling of the premises.

2320
02:13:44.310 --> 02:13:47.350
This killer was no ordinary human.

2321
02:13:48.730 --> 02:13:51.020
[wet squelching]

2322
02:13:52.400 --> 02:13:55.530
[breathing shakily]

2323
02:14:10.580 --> 02:14:12.726
[MUZAN] I heard
there was some commotion

2324
02:14:12.750 --> 02:14:14.646
about a demon sighting here.

2325
02:14:14.670 --> 02:14:17.180
even though I know I never sent one.

2326
02:14:17.720 --> 02:14:20.616
So. I decided to come see for myself.

2327
02:14:20.640 --> 02:14:22.810
Yet all I find is a human.

2328
02:14:23.390 --> 02:14:25.600
How utterly disappointing.

2329
02:14:26.680 --> 02:14:29.810
[HAKUJI] Move. or I'll kill you!

2330
02:14:30.980 --> 02:14:33.320
- [thuds]
- [splatters]

2331
02:14:34.730 --> 02:14:36.086
It just so happens

2332
02:14:36.110 --> 02:14:39.740
I was contemplating
creating 12 powerful demons.

2333
02:14:40.320 --> 02:14:42.596
I wonder if you'll be able to withstand

2334
02:14:42.620 --> 02:14:45.120
the amount of blood
I'm about to give you.

2335
02:14:47.120 --> 02:14:49.330
You... [grunts]

2336
02:14:50.710 --> 02:14:54.340
do whatever you want.

2337
02:14:55.210 --> 02:14:57.970
None of it matters.

2338
02:15:03.850 --> 02:15:05.906
[thunder rumbling]

2339
02:15:05.930 --> 02:15:08.060
[♪ somber music playing]

2340
02:15:08.850 --> 02:15:10.980
[grunting]

2341
02:15:12.520 --> 02:15:15.570
[AKAZA] After becoming a demon.
I lost my memories...

2342
02:15:16.150 --> 02:15:19.240
and once again.
started to seek out power.

2343
02:15:19.700 --> 02:15:21.046
- [thuds]
- [grunts]

2344
02:15:21.070 --> 02:15:22.410
- [flesh squelches]
- [grunts]

2345
02:15:29.290 --> 02:15:30.750
[clangs]

2346
02:15:31.620 --> 02:15:33.380
- [wet squelching]
- [sword clatters]

2347
02:15:34.500 --> 02:15:36.186
It's not enough!

2348
02:15:36.210 --> 02:15:38.066
It will never be enough!

2349
02:15:38.090 --> 02:15:39.970
[thunderclap]

2350
02:15:42.050 --> 02:15:45.326
Even though I had nothing
left to my name.

2351
02:15:45.350 --> 02:15:48.600
Even though I had nothing
worth fighting for anymore.

2352
02:15:50.850 --> 02:15:53.996
Even though my family
was no longer around

2353
02:15:54.020 --> 02:15:57.940
and I had no desire
to live in a world without them.

2354
02:16:00.490 --> 02:16:03.926
For over a century.
I committed senseless massacres

2355
02:16:03.950 --> 02:16:05.780
over and over again.

2356
02:16:06.700 --> 02:16:09.926
Thinking about it now.
it's pathetic.

2357
02:16:09.950 --> 02:16:11.620
It's absurd.

2358
02:16:12.500 --> 02:16:15.250
All those deaths were meaningless.

2359
02:16:20.670 --> 02:16:22.776
Even if I died now.

2360
02:16:22.800 --> 02:16:26.300
I couldn't go where the other
three were waiting for me.

2361
02:16:27.470 --> 02:16:32.390
Damn you for dredging up
these memories. You bastard!

2362
02:16:34.270 --> 02:16:36.206
Pathetic humans.

2363
02:16:36.230 --> 02:16:39.570
clinging on to life
with their fragile bodies!

2364
02:16:40.690 --> 02:16:44.466
Even their strongest eventually die

2365
02:16:44.490 --> 02:16:46.820
and vanish into thin air!

2366
02:16:47.450 --> 02:16:49.530
[flesh squelching]

2367
02:16:50.160 --> 02:16:52.016
[GIYU] He's still not dead?

2368
02:16:52.040 --> 02:16:53.870
You can't be serious.

2369
02:16:55.040 --> 02:16:57.750
I have to kill him before it's too late.

2370
02:16:58.750 --> 02:17:02.920
If we let him regenerate.
there will be no stopping him.

2371
02:17:04.630 --> 02:17:06.050
- [loud thump]
- [gasps]

2372
02:17:08.010 --> 02:17:10.236
[grunts] I must have passed out.

2373
02:17:10.260 --> 02:17:11.720
What's going on?

2374
02:17:13.430 --> 02:17:17.400
His head's back!
But how is that even possible?!

2375
02:17:18.560 --> 02:17:20.650
I decapitated him!

2376
02:17:21.320 --> 02:17:23.490
[♪ intense music playing]

2377
02:17:26.780 --> 02:17:29.700
Destructive Death:
Annihilation Type.

2378
02:17:30.410 --> 02:17:32.596
Stop it!

2379
02:17:32.620 --> 02:17:35.346
[AKAZA] Seriously?
He can still move?

2380
02:17:35.370 --> 02:17:38.056
[TANJIRO] Mr. Giyu and I
are going to win!

2381
02:17:38.080 --> 02:17:42.000
Akaza. I'll behead you
as many times as it takes!

2382
02:17:44.880 --> 02:17:46.380
My sword!

2383
02:17:47.680 --> 02:17:50.100
[GIYU] It slipped out of his hands.

2384
02:17:51.100 --> 02:17:52.720
[TANJIRO] I lost my grip.

2385
02:17:55.020 --> 02:17:56.270
[effort grunts]

2386
02:18:01.860 --> 02:18:03.690
[KEIZO] All right. young man.

2387
02:18:04.440 --> 02:18:06.150
Time to be reborn.

2388
02:18:08.280 --> 02:18:11.120
[AKAZA] I despise those who are weak.

2389
02:18:13.200 --> 02:18:17.346
Weaklings... Instead of
fighting you fair and square.

2390
02:18:17.370 --> 02:18:19.920
they always resort to cheap tricks.

2391
02:18:20.710 --> 02:18:22.500
They're atrocious.

2392
02:18:23.000 --> 02:18:25.146
They have no patience.

2393
02:18:25.170 --> 02:18:27.446
And they quickly grow desperate.

2394
02:18:27.470 --> 02:18:30.050
Just thinking about them makes me sick.

2395
02:18:32.100 --> 02:18:35.770
I killed people
with my fists for protection.

2396
02:18:36.310 --> 02:18:40.020
I desecrated my master's
beloved Soryu with blood.

2397
02:18:41.310 --> 02:18:44.440
And I couldn't follow
my father's last wishes!

2398
02:18:46.860 --> 02:18:48.400
That's right.

2399
02:18:48.950 --> 02:18:51.370
The one I wanted to kill...

2400
02:18:53.080 --> 02:18:54.580
[clatters]

2401
02:18:56.830 --> 02:18:59.556
[TANJIRO] This couldn't be
worse. I dropped my sword!

2402
02:18:59.580 --> 02:19:01.396
[♪ foreboding music playing]

2403
02:19:01.420 --> 02:19:03.960
My fists aren't enough to stop him!

2404
02:19:14.390 --> 02:19:16.906
He's about to unleash
the Annihilation Type move

2405
02:19:16.930 --> 02:19:18.770
he used on Mr. Rengoku!

2406
02:19:21.940 --> 02:19:25.150
I've got to take Mr. Giyu
with me out of the attack range!

2407
02:19:29.360 --> 02:19:31.990
[GIYU] Leave me! Save yourself!

2408
02:19:37.580 --> 02:19:39.620
[AKAZA] I've got to kill...

2409
02:19:42.080 --> 02:19:43.710
that weakling

2410
02:19:44.170 --> 02:19:46.340
I've come to hate!

2411
02:20:05.020 --> 02:20:07.190
[♪ dramatic music playing]

2412
02:20:12.660 --> 02:20:14.280
[thudding]

2413
02:20:17.200 --> 02:20:19.330
[grunts. gasps]

2414
02:20:19.910 --> 02:20:22.040
[flesh squelching]

2415
02:20:26.170 --> 02:20:27.210
[blood spurts]

2416
02:20:29.250 --> 02:20:31.670
[TANJIRO] He just attacked himself.

2417
02:20:34.430 --> 02:20:36.760
Why would he turn on himself like that?

2418
02:20:37.680 --> 02:20:38.850
Why?

2419
02:20:40.430 --> 02:20:42.286
[♪ melancholic music playing]

2420
02:20:42.310 --> 02:20:43.706
For a second.

2421
02:20:43.730 --> 02:20:46.810
I could pick up the scent
of gratitude from him.

2422
02:20:48.070 --> 02:20:50.280
Why did he smile at me?

2423
02:20:54.070 --> 02:20:56.716
[AKAZA] That's enough! Stop it!

2424
02:20:56.740 --> 02:20:59.160
I don't want to regenerate!

2425
02:20:59.740 --> 02:21:01.596
Don't you get it?

2426
02:21:01.620 --> 02:21:03.460
The battle is over!

2427
02:21:05.420 --> 02:21:08.726
In that decisive moment. I lost.

2428
02:21:08.750 --> 02:21:11.066
That technique he beheaded me with

2429
02:21:11.090 --> 02:21:13.260
was nothing short of perfection.

2430
02:21:14.510 --> 02:21:18.946
He anticipated my movements
and pivoted at the last second.

2431
02:21:18.970 --> 02:21:22.470
then struck me down before
I could unleash my attack.

2432
02:21:23.390 --> 02:21:25.230
It's over now.

2433
02:21:25.940 --> 02:21:30.520
Let me accept my fate and go to hell.

2434
02:21:33.690 --> 02:21:35.650
[TANJIRO] Where's he trying to go?

2435
02:21:41.870 --> 02:21:44.870
[gasps softly]
He stopped in his tracks.

2436
02:21:47.790 --> 02:21:49.080
[HAKUJI] Dad.

2437
02:21:50.960 --> 02:21:52.880
Are you feeling better now?

2438
02:21:53.420 --> 02:21:55.420
Are you in pain anymore?

2439
02:21:56.680 --> 02:21:59.300
No need to worry. son. I'm fine.

2440
02:22:00.100 --> 02:22:02.140
Thank you. Hakuji.

2441
02:22:08.560 --> 02:22:10.310
I'm sorry. Father.

2442
02:22:10.810 --> 02:22:14.206
I'm sorry I couldn't start over
like you wanted.

2443
02:22:14.230 --> 02:22:15.940
I failed you.

2444
02:22:18.990 --> 02:22:20.950
[KEIZO] Do not despair.

2445
02:22:21.530 --> 02:22:23.806
Regardless of who you grow up to be.

2446
02:22:23.830 --> 02:22:27.386
you're still my son and still my student.

2447
02:22:27.410 --> 02:22:29.630
Heaven may not accept you...

2448
02:22:30.960 --> 02:22:32.606
but you needn't worry.

2449
02:22:32.630 --> 02:22:34.710
Our hearts will be with you.

2450
02:22:37.010 --> 02:22:38.510
Master.

2451
02:22:39.720 --> 02:22:40.840
[gasps]

2452
02:22:41.390 --> 02:22:45.036
Didn't you say you were seeking
to become stronger than anyone?

2453
02:22:45.060 --> 02:22:50.020
Don't tell me you intend
to let it end like this. Akaza.

2454
02:22:51.980 --> 02:22:55.376
[AKAZA] That's right.
I can't die here.

2455
02:22:55.400 --> 02:22:57.440
I have to get stronger!

2456
02:22:58.740 --> 02:23:00.636
So what if I got beheaded?

2457
02:23:00.660 --> 02:23:03.370
Who cares if I win or lose the fight?

2458
02:23:04.080 --> 02:23:06.700
If I kill those who stand in my way...

2459
02:23:07.500 --> 02:23:10.460
then there's still hope
for me to get stronger!

2460
02:23:12.920 --> 02:23:14.396
I made a promise!

2461
02:23:14.420 --> 02:23:16.420
I'm not about to break it!

2462
02:23:22.300 --> 02:23:24.640
[breathing shakily]

2463
02:23:25.680 --> 02:23:26.826
[♪ tender music playing]

2464
02:23:26.850 --> 02:23:28.560
Mr. Hakuji.

2465
02:23:29.270 --> 02:23:31.100
thank you so much.

2466
02:23:31.600 --> 02:23:33.520
You've done more than enough.

2467
02:23:37.860 --> 02:23:39.280
It's okay.

2468
02:23:39.780 --> 02:23:41.506
We're all right now.

2469
02:23:41.530 --> 02:23:43.136
Akaza!

2470
02:23:43.160 --> 02:23:45.280
[♪ epic cinematic music playing]

2471
02:23:48.910 --> 02:23:51.790
[wailing]

2472
02:23:53.120 --> 02:23:54.516
Sorry!

2473
02:23:54.540 --> 02:23:57.250
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you!

2474
02:23:57.880 --> 02:24:01.220
I wasn't there
when you needed me to be!

2475
02:24:01.840 --> 02:24:05.026
I couldn't keep a single promise I made.

2476
02:24:05.050 --> 02:24:08.946
I'm sorry. [sobbing] Please
try to forgive me. Koyuki.

2477
02:24:08.970 --> 02:24:12.310
I'm so sorry.
[continues sobbing]

2478
02:24:15.230 --> 02:24:17.706
I'm so happy you remembered us.

2479
02:24:17.730 --> 02:24:20.440
I can't tell you
how happy that makes me.

2480
02:24:21.110 --> 02:24:24.386
And to see you now
as the man that I once knew.

2481
02:24:24.410 --> 02:24:26.200
I'm so grateful.

2482
02:24:34.460 --> 02:24:37.420
Welcome home. Hakuji.

2483
02:24:41.760 --> 02:24:43.550
Hey. Hakuji.

2484
02:24:43.930 --> 02:24:45.300
Welcome home.

2485
02:24:54.020 --> 02:24:55.650
[HAKUJI] I'm back now.

2486
02:24:56.190 --> 02:24:58.440
I'm finally back home.

2487
02:25:01.740 --> 02:25:03.490
Welcome back home...

2488
02:25:04.490 --> 02:25:05.990
my darling.

2489
02:25:10.290 --> 02:25:11.410
[gasps softly]

2490
02:25:12.620 --> 02:25:14.790
[♪ gentle music playing]

2491
02:25:33.640 --> 02:25:35.366
[Tanjiro breathing shakily]

2492
02:25:35.390 --> 02:25:36.940
He vanished.

2493
02:25:39.900 --> 02:25:41.230
[gasps]

2494
02:25:42.440 --> 02:25:43.990
[inhales deeply]

2495
02:25:44.950 --> 02:25:46.450
[exhales sharply]

2496
02:25:48.320 --> 02:25:50.530
It's over. Right?

2497
02:25:54.660 --> 02:25:56.040
Gotta hurry...

2498
02:25:57.040 --> 02:26:00.500
and get to where Ms. Tamayo is.

2499
02:26:01.460 --> 02:26:02.670
And then...

2500
02:26:09.640 --> 02:26:11.680
[grunts weakly] Tanjiro.

2501
02:26:17.640 --> 02:26:18.770
[exhales]

2502
02:26:21.020 --> 02:26:23.940
[Kasugai Crow cawing]

2503
02:26:24.780 --> 02:26:29.636
Tanjiro! Giyu!
Have defeated Upper Three!

2504
02:26:29.660 --> 02:26:33.636
They are unable to stay
conscious due to exhaustion!

2505
02:26:33.660 --> 02:26:35.250
They've passed out!

2506
02:26:40.630 --> 02:26:46.566
Tanjiro! Giyu!
Have defeated Upper Three!

2507
02:26:46.590 --> 02:26:48.380
Upper Three!

2508
02:26:53.060 --> 02:26:54.486
[♪ haunting choral music playing]

2509
02:26:54.510 --> 02:26:56.496
[KOKUSHIBO] Akaza!

2510
02:26:56.520 --> 02:26:59.350
His presence has vanished.

2511
02:27:01.270 --> 02:27:04.020
What a baffling conclusion.

2512
02:27:06.990 --> 02:27:08.450
Akaza...

2513
02:27:09.820 --> 02:27:13.990
what happened to your burning
ambition to defeat me?

2514
02:27:15.910 --> 02:27:20.330
To think you'd abandoned
everything you stood for...

2515
02:27:21.460 --> 02:27:25.250
and turned your back
on the path to greatness.

2516
02:27:26.090 --> 02:27:27.880
[♪ music intensifies]

2517
02:27:31.970 --> 02:27:35.010
Your weakness appalls me.

2518
02:27:40.140 --> 02:27:41.270
Huh?

2519
02:27:42.270 --> 02:27:43.480
[exclaims]

2520
02:27:43.860 --> 02:27:45.020
This feeling.

2521
02:27:45.570 --> 02:27:48.110
Could Lord Akaza be dead?

2522
02:27:49.570 --> 02:27:50.926
Very strange.

2523
02:27:50.950 --> 02:27:54.490
Surely my imagination
must be running wild. right?

2524
02:27:54.990 --> 02:27:59.830
It almost felt like Lord Akaza
had turned into some creature.

2525
02:28:02.330 --> 02:28:05.106
But now that he's dead.
I guess it doesn't matter.

2526
02:28:05.130 --> 02:28:07.250
- [laughs]
- [rattling]

2527
02:28:08.300 --> 02:28:10.106
Let's see.

2528
02:28:10.130 --> 02:28:11.510
where was I?

2529
02:28:12.090 --> 02:28:14.260
Oh. I remember.

2530
02:28:14.720 --> 02:28:17.470
I had just asked for your name.
hadn't I?

2531
02:28:18.600 --> 02:28:20.390
[Kanao breathing shakily]

2532
02:28:30.360 --> 02:28:32.836
[KASUGAI CROW] Tanjiro! Giyu!

2533
02:28:32.860 --> 02:28:35.296
Have defeated Upper Three!

2534
02:28:35.320 --> 02:28:36.830
Upper Three!

2535
02:28:37.490 --> 02:28:38.766
Did you hear that?

2536
02:28:38.790 --> 02:28:42.200
Yes. Excellent work. Tomioka.

2537
02:28:42.750 --> 02:28:44.880
Excellent work. Kamado.

2538
02:28:45.580 --> 02:28:47.790
[♪ closing theme song playing]

2539
02:28:49.960 --> 02:28:53.486
Mr. Tomioka and Tanjiro.
They did it!

2540
02:28:53.510 --> 02:28:56.220
[IGURO] Now it's our turn
to follow their lead.

2541
02:28:56.760 --> 02:28:58.100
Right!

2542
02:29:05.480 --> 02:29:06.730
[demon snarling]

2543
02:29:12.530 --> 02:29:14.910
Hang in there. Agatsuma!

2544
02:29:18.910 --> 02:29:20.306
[cawing]

2545
02:29:20.330 --> 02:29:22.346
[INOSUKE] Start flapping
those wings faster.

2546
02:29:22.370 --> 02:29:23.910
or I'm gonna keep poking!

2547
02:29:24.460 --> 02:29:25.896
You're gonna use those wings

2548
02:29:25.920 --> 02:29:27.856
to show me where
the strongest demon is!

2549
02:29:27.880 --> 02:29:29.170
You hear me?

2550
02:29:29.670 --> 02:29:31.880
I'm coming through!

2551
02:29:32.380 --> 02:29:33.566
Hyah!

2552
02:29:33.590 --> 02:29:35.066
Now we're talkin'!

2553
02:29:35.090 --> 02:29:37.866
I'm sensing a powerful demon over here.

2554
02:29:37.890 --> 02:29:39.470
[cawing]

2555
02:29:44.730 --> 02:29:46.690
Where is Big Brother?

2556
02:29:56.780 --> 02:29:58.796
Where are all the Upper Ranks?

2557
02:29:58.820 --> 02:30:01.030
Tell me! Come on!

2558
02:30:01.530 --> 02:30:04.250
I'm gonna bury you all!

2559
02:30:12.090 --> 02:30:13.986
[KANATA] The passageway leading north

2560
02:30:14.010 --> 02:30:15.896
on the 88th level is clear.

2561
02:30:15.920 --> 02:30:17.590
No sign of Muzan.

2562
02:30:18.260 --> 02:30:20.116
[KUINA] The 100th and 27th levels

2563
02:30:20.140 --> 02:30:22.760
in the southeast are clear.
No sign of Muzan.

2564
02:30:23.770 --> 02:30:25.456
He's in here.

2565
02:30:25.480 --> 02:30:26.826
He has to be.

2566
02:30:26.850 --> 02:30:28.060
But where is he?

2567
02:30:28.980 --> 02:30:31.246
[KANATA] There's no sign
of Muzan on any of the levels

2568
02:30:31.270 --> 02:30:33.690
from 90 to 100. either.

2569
02:30:35.440 --> 02:30:38.466
[KUINA] Covering the entire
100th and 33rd levels.

2570
02:30:38.490 --> 02:30:40.030
No sign of Muzan.

2571
02:30:41.530 --> 02:30:43.766
Our crows will find you.

2572
02:30:43.790 --> 02:30:46.540
You can only hide from us for so long.

2573
02:30:47.080 --> 02:30:50.346
We'll search every inch
of this Infinity Castle.

2574
02:30:50.370 --> 02:30:54.460
Even if you try to run from us.
we will hunt you down.

2575
02:30:54.920 --> 02:30:56.550
[plucking]

2576
02:30:58.550 --> 02:30:59.970
FOUR

2577
02:31:00.550 --> 02:31:02.720
[continues plucking biwa strings]

2578
02:31:09.060 --> 02:31:12.150
Multi-layered structures
are headed northeast.

2579
02:31:12.650 --> 02:31:16.296
Attention! The castle's
expanding in every direction.

2580
02:31:16.320 --> 02:31:18.086
Folding over themselves!

2581
02:31:18.110 --> 02:31:21.360
[Nakime plucking biwa strings faster]

2582
02:31:22.120 --> 02:31:23.870
[BOTH] And becoming one!

2583
02:31:29.620 --> 02:31:32.210
[gasps] You can't be serious.

2584
02:31:33.340 --> 02:31:34.766
No.

2585
02:31:34.790 --> 02:31:35.976
It's fine.

2586
02:31:36.000 --> 02:31:38.010
We've come too far to lose.

2587
02:31:38.760 --> 02:31:40.776
Crows. push forward.

2588
02:31:40.800 --> 02:31:42.760
and find Muzan!

2589
02:31:47.520 --> 02:31:50.666
[MUZAN] Try all you want.
Demon Slayers!

2590
02:31:50.690 --> 02:31:52.826
But each one of you will meet your end

2591
02:31:52.850 --> 02:31:54.440
before ever reaching me!

2592
02:31:54.980 --> 02:31:58.796
You may be feeling smug after
beheading one of my Upper Ranks.

2593
02:31:58.820 --> 02:32:02.860
but unless you could kill me.
your triumph is meaningless!

2594
02:32:03.700 --> 02:32:06.846
[laughs maliciously]

2595
02:32:06.870 --> 02:32:09.596
You're all going to die
the most pointless deaths

2596
02:32:09.620 --> 02:32:12.556
all the while never seeing my face!

2597
02:32:12.580 --> 02:32:16.840
I can't think of a more fitting
end for the Demon Slayer Corps.

2598
02:32:17.340 --> 02:32:19.816
Mark my words.
When I'm done here.

2599
02:32:19.840 --> 02:32:22.630
I'm going to make you regret
the day you were born!

2600
02:32:23.720 --> 02:32:25.026
Just wait.

2601
02:32:25.050 --> 02:32:28.246
You're each going to squirm
and writhe in pain.

2602
02:32:28.270 --> 02:32:30.156
Draw your final breaths

2603
02:32:30.180 --> 02:32:33.286
because for every one
of you Demon Slayers.

2604
02:32:33.310 --> 02:32:36.860
there is no tomorrow!

2605
02:32:46.950 --> 02:32:48.490
[KASUGAI CROW 1] Please. Giyu.

2606
02:32:52.000 --> 02:32:53.960
Don't die!

2607
02:33:00.920 --> 02:33:04.760
[KASUGAI CROW 2] We can't
have you dying on us. Tanjiro.

2608
02:33:17.150 --> 02:33:19.416
[music ends]

2609
02:33:19.440 --> 02:33:21.610
[♪ closing theme song playing]

2609
02:33:22.305 --> 02:34:22.322
